2025-12-18 01:35:12,234 - [add-v4-8-narr-batch0] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-4eaac178-e674-4327-8910-9c408036c6d8', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an episodic memory generation expert. Convert each conversation unit into an episodic memory.\n\n**Conversation Units to Process:**\n[\n  {\n    "unit_id": 0,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:47 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Hey Evan, good to see you! What\'s new since we last met? Anything cool happening?\\nEvan: Hey Sam! Good to see you! Yeah, I just got back from a trip with my family in my new Prius."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 1,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:48 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow, not bad, what happened to the old one? Where\'d you go, by the way?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 2,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:48 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a lake with rocks and mountains in the background] My old prius broke down, decided to get it repaired and sell it. Glad you asked, we went to Rockies, check it out."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 3,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:49 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow! Looks amazing. When did you get to go there?\\nEvan: We all hiked the trails last week - the views were amazing!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 4,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:50 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photography of a man and a child walking through a forest] Wow, that\'s cool. I love hiking, but it\'s been ages since I\'ve done it. I did this hike with my dad way back when I was ten. Going hiking together was great fun, and really special for us."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 5,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:50 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Aww, that\'s cute. How far did you two hike?\\nSam: We hiked a good distance - quite a feat for me back then. It\'s definitely a great memory."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 6,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:51 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: What other hobbies have you found for yourself?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 7,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a person holding a paint set in a store] Nothing so far, but I was thinking about trying painting. Do you have any hobbies you love?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 8,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Cool idea, Sam! I love it. Have you tried it before?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 9,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Not yet, but I\'m keen to give it a go. It looks like a nice way to chill and get creative."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 10,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a painting of a cactus in the desert] Yep, it\'s a great stress-buster. I started doing this a few years back."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 11,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow, that\'s impressive! How did you get into watercolor painting?\\nEvan: My friend got me into it and gave me some advice, and I was hooked right away!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 12,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow! I hope I can find something I\'m as passionate about as you are with watercolor painting."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 13,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: You\'ll find it, just keep trying new things until something sparks your excitement."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 14,\n    "timestamp": "May 18, 2023(Thursday) at 01:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan! I\'m excited to try new things, should be fun!\\nEvan: No worries, Sam! Super pumped for you! Let\'s catch up soon and see how you\'re enjoying your new hobbies!\\nSam: Yeah, I\'ll keep you posted. See you soon!\\nEvan: Take it easy, Evan! Can\'t wait to see you. Have a good one!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 15,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:11 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a person holding a book in front of a lake] Hey Sam, good to hear from you! Since we last talked, lots has been happening! Last weekend, I took my family on a road trip to Jasper. It was amazing! We drove through the Icefields Parkway and the glaciers and lakes were gorgeous. I got a shot of a glacier, check it out!\\nSam: Hey Evan, looks amazing! I\'ve never been to Jasper, but it looks breathtaking. Tell me more about your road trip. Was it relaxing?\\nEvan: Hey Sam, thanks for asking! It was great - fresh air, peacefulness and a cozy cabin surrounded by mountains and forests made it feel like a real retreat."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 16,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:12 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: That sounds great, Evan! It\'s so important to take time for ourselves and find peace, especially after a hard week. Mine\'s been tough.\\nEvan: Sorry to hear that, Sam. Is there anything I can do to help?\\nSam: Thanks, Evan. Appreciate the offer, but had a check-up with my doctor a few days ago and, yikes, the weight wasn\'t great. It was pretty eye-opening."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 17,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:14 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: That must have been a challenging experience, Sam. It\'s tough when we have to confront our own health challenges. Remember, it\'s never too late to make positive changes for a healthier lifestyle. Is there anything I can do to support you in this journey?\\nSam: Thanks, Evan. Breaking old habits isn\'t easy. Do you have any tips for starting the process?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 18,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:15 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yeah, what worked for me was finding a fitness routine I really enjoy. It\'s my go-to, I love the feeling of being healthy and strong. Making it fun and finding little ways to make smarter choices in my diet really added up. Don\'t forget, you got this!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 19,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:15 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan. Like you said, I\'ve been looking for a hobby to stay motivated. I\'ve been thinking about trying painting. Do you think it will help me de-stress?\\nEvan: Of course, Sam! Painting is a great way to relieve stress and be creative. It gives you the freedom to explore colors and textures and express feelings. I\'ve been doing it for a few years now and it helps me find peace. But unfortunately it won\'t help you with your weight problem, besides painting I recommend exercising!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 20,\n    "timestamp": "May 24, 2023(Wednesday) at 07:16 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan! Appreciate the encouragement. I\'ll give it a go and let you know how it turns out.\\nEvan: Awesome, Sam! Have fun with it and don\'t put too much pressure on yourself. Can\'t wait to hear how it\'s going!\\nSam: Cheers, Evan! I won\'t stress - just gonna enjoy it.\\nEvan: Alright Sam, have fun with it! Keep me updated!\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! Will do. Bye for now.\\nEvan: Take care, Sam! I\'ll catch up with you later."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 21,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 03:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a person holding a bottle of medicine in their hand] Hey Sam! Long time no talk! How\'re you doing? Life\'s been quite the rollercoaster lately. I had a health scare last week – a sudden heart palpitation incident that really shook me up. It\'s been a serious wake-up call about my lifestyle.\\nSam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a plate of vegetables and a glass of milk] Hey Evan, great hearing from you! Sorry about that, glad you\'re feeling better now."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 22,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 03:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Trying to eat healthier these days.\\nEvan: That salad looks yummy! I\'m being extra careful with my health lately. I\'m trying to eat less processed food and sugary snacks, even though I love ginger snaps. Have you made any changes to your diet recently?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 23,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 03:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Nah, no changes for me. Still enjoying my soda and candy, although I know it\'s not the best habit to have.\\nEvan: Yeah, breaking habits can be tough. Making small changes can have a big impact later on. Have you considered swapping soda for flavored seltzer water? It\'s still bubbly and tasty, but without the sugar. And instead of candy, you could try dark chocolate with high cocoa content - it\'s a healthier option. What do you think?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 24,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 03:57 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yeah, good idea! I\'ll give it a try.\\nEvan: Awesome, Sam! Let me know how it goes. Making small changes can really help you live a healthier life. Don\'t forget - every step matters!\\nSam: Hey Evan, thanks! Appreciate it. I\'ll definitely keep you posted.\\nEvan: I\'m here for you, Sam. Let\'s continue supporting each other on our health journeys. It\'s important to remember that progress takes time.\\nSam: Yeah, you\'re right. It takes time, but I\'m up for keep trying and making those tiny changes.\\nEvan: C\'mon, keep it up! Every little bit counts, you\'ll get there!\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! I appreciate your support, it means a lot to me to have you in my corner."\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL units in order (unit_id 0, 1, 2, ...)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Each narrative should be self-contained and retrievable\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
