2025-12-18 01:35:58,473 - [add-v4-8-narr-batch1] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-d58a0ff8-ca85-43bd-ba67-c738088e3ece', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an episodic memory generation expert. Convert each conversation unit into an episodic memory.\n\n**Conversation Units to Process:**\n[\n  {\n    "unit_id": 25,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:01 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a man with a beard holding a dumbble] Yes, Sam! I\'m here for you. Let\'s rock our workouts and reach our goals! Exercise clears the mind - it\'s amazing!\\nSam: Wow, that\'s awesome! Could you give me a hand with getting started?\\nEvan: Sure Sam, I\'d be glad to help. Let\'s get together and I\'ll show you some basic exercises. We\'ll reach our goals!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 26,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:02 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Cool, can\'t wait! Thank you. By the way, I\'m coming from the shop and I had a frustrating issue at the supermarket. The self-checkout machines were all broken, my mood is terrible now!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 27,\n    "timestamp": "June 06, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:03 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Sorry you were in that situation, hopefully it won\'t happen again!\\nSam: Yeah, I hope so, take care of yourself."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 28,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:52 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Hey Evan, I need to talk to you. My friends were mocking my weight last Friday and it hurt. That made me realize I need to make changes.\\nEvan: Hey Sam, sorry about that. Don\'t worry, progress takes time. Let\'s work on it together.\\nSam: Thanks for the support, Evan. I\'m working on my health and getting active!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 29,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:53 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a set of five cards with the words let it shine] That\'s great, Sam! I struggled with my health a few years ago, but stuck with it. Here\'s a reminder of my commitment - my gym membership card. It\'s not just about exercise, diet and lifestyle changes also play a big role.\\nSam: That\'s awesome, Evan! What do you think made the biggest impact on your health journey?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 30,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:54 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a table full of fresh produce and vegetables] I made some dietary changes, like cutting down on sugary snacks and eating more veggies and fruit, and it made a big impact on my health. Have you considered any changes?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 31,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:55 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yep, I\'m reducing my soda and candy intake. It\'s tough, but I\'m determined to make a change."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 32,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:55 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a table with a variety of sodas and water bottles] Go for it, Sam! It\'s tough at first, but you got this. Try flavored seltzer water instead. It can be a great alternative to soda. Btw I can\'t stop thinking about that new mystery novel I started. It\'s so gripping!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 33,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:56 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Sounds good, Evan. I\'ve tried it before and it was nice. Do you have any ideas for low-calorie snacks to pair with it? And what\'s the novel?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 34,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:56 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a table with bowls of fruit and a bottle of alcohol] Definitely, how about some flavored seltzer with some air-popped popcorn or fruit? It\'s yum and healthy! The novel I\'m reading is \\"The Great Gatsby\\"."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 35,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:57 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yum, that sounds good! Thanks! And I\'ll definitely read that novel sometime."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 36,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:57 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a book with a green apple next to it] No worries, Sam! Focus on healthy swaps and taking small steps. Stay upbeat!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 37,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:58 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: That reminder is inspiring. Thanks for reminding me to focus on progress, not perfection."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 38,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:58 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: By the way, have you thought about exercising? Trust me, it\'s just as important as eating right."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 39,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:59 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Starting tomorrow, I will go to the gym and exercise regularly. The sooner I start, the sooner I will see the rewards of this activity."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 40,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 10:59 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: That\'s awesome, Sam! It\'s such a rewarding and tough activity - keep going and have fun!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 41,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 11:00 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan! Your support means a lot. I really appreciate it."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 42,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 11:00 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: No worries, you\'ve got this!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 43,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 11:01 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan. I really appreciate it."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 44,\n    "timestamp": "July 27, 2023(Thursday) at 11:01 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: No worries, Sam. I\'m here if you need me. Keep going!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 45,\n    "timestamp": "August 07, 2023(Monday) at 07:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a couple walking through the snow holding hands] Hey Sam, how\'s it going? Last week I went on a trip to Canada and something unreal happened - I met this awesome Canadian woman and it was like something out of a movie. She\'s incredible and being with her makes me feel alive.\\nSam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a person walking on the beach with a surfboard] Congrats Evan! She must be something special! Being with someone who makes you feel alive is amazing. I\'m sorry to hear that you\'re dealing with health issues lately, it can be really tough. It\'s hard to fully enjoy things sometimes."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 46,\n    "timestamp": "August 07, 2023(Monday) at 07:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a container of cookies on a counter] Woah. such a nice view! Thanks, Sam! She\'s definitely great. Every moment with her is really fun and energizing. It\'s a nice change, especially after dealing with health issues."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 47,\n    "timestamp": "August 07, 2023(Monday) at 07:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: But you never know what life\'s gonna throw at you. Btw look what life has thrown for me right now haha.\\nSam: Looks good to eat! Dealing with health problems can be challenging and take away from enjoyable experiences."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 48,\n    "timestamp": "August 07, 2023(Monday) at 07:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a woman and a child playing on a swing set] Ginger snaps are my weakness for sure! Dealing with health issues has been tough, but it\'s made me appreciate the good moments more. These are the ones who bring lots of joy even through the hard times."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 49,\n    "timestamp": "August 07, 2023(Monday) at 07:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: It looks like your kids are having a great time! And how long have you been prioritizing your health?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a box with a fitness watch on it] Yes, they bring me such joy. My healthy road has been a long one. I\'ve been working on it for two years now, so there have been ups and downs, but I\'m doing my best."\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL units in order (unit_id 0, 1, 2, ...)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Each narrative should be self-contained and retrievable\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
