2025-12-18 01:39:45,320 - [add-v4-8-narr-batch6] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-0d4a8cb1-02e1-4b43-9801-bf9370b72bdc', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an episodic memory generation expert. Convert each conversation unit into an episodic memory.\n\n**Conversation Units to Process:**\n[\n  {\n    "unit_id": 150,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:51 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yup, Sam! Set some goals, like a certain distance to run or number of push-ups to do. It\'ll give you something to strive for and stay motivated. Also, try to find an exercise that you enjoy and maybe even get a buddy for extra fun and accountability. Sound good?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 151,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yeah, that sounds like a good idea. Having goals and someone to exercise with might help. I\'ll give it a try!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 152,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Awesome, Sam! Getting started will get easier with time. And don\'t forget it\'s about feeling good and reaching goals, too. Let\'s plan a hike soon!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 153,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Sounds awesome, Evan! Can\'t wait to go on a hike with you. It\'s going to be a fun challenge and a great opportunity to appreciate the beauty of nature."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 154,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Definitely, Sam! Hiking is an awesome way to bond with nature and push ourselves. It\'s gonna be a cool memory for us both. It\'s great to see progress, was just at the gym yesterday. Gaining strength!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 155,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Super excited to get fit with ya. Let\'s hit the trails soon!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 156,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Thanks, Sam! That\'s so nice of you. We\'ll definitely have a great time on our hike!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 157,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Totally! I\'m so pumped for this hike. Connecting with nature is exactly what I need. Thanks so much for the support and always being there. Means a lot."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 158,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Sure thing! Our hike is going to be awesome, I can tell. I\'m always here to support you."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 159,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan. I appreciate your support."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 160,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: No problem, Sam. Whenever you need support, I\'m here for you. Stay safe!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 161,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:57 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, I\'ll get in touch if I need anything. Stay safe. Bye!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 162,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:57 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Later! Stay safe and don\'t hesitate to holler if you need anything. Can\'t wait to hit the trail."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 163,\n    "timestamp": "October 25, 2023(Wednesday) at 02:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Morning, Evan. I\'ve been trying to keep up with my new health routine, but it\'s tough. My family\'s really pushing for it, and I feel so pressured.\\nEvan: I hear you, Sam. It\'s important to have people who encourage you, but not stress you out."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 164,\n    "timestamp": "October 25, 2023(Wednesday) at 02:56 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: By the way, I just got back from my morning walk. It really helps to start the day actively.\\nSam: Yeah, it\'s easier when you have a great support system. Thanks for being there for me.\\nEvan: No worries, Sam. I\'ll be there for you. Take it slow and treat yourself.\\nSam: Thanks for the reminder to take it easy. I sometimes get impatient with myself when I want results fast, but I gotta be patient.\\nEvan: Yep, progress takes time. So just take it one step at a time.\\nSam: Yes, you\'re right, Evan. Taking it slow is better than doing too much. I appreciate your support."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 165,\n    "timestamp": "October 25, 2023(Wednesday) at 02:59 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a man sitting at a table with a lot of fruits and vegetables] I get it, Sam. I went through a similar phase a twoyears ago. Changed my diet, started walking regularly, things like that.\\nSam: Wow, Evan, you look great! How did you manage the change?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 166,\n    "timestamp": "October 25, 2023(Wednesday) at 03:00 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: I started focusing more on my well-being rather than fixating on quick results. Letting go of that pressure made a huge difference.\\nSam: That\'s impressive, Evan. It\'s inspiring to see how you transformed by changing your mindset.\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam. Letting go of unrealistic expectations was liberating, both physically and mentally.\\nSam: You\'re really doing great, Evan! I want to feel that same sense of freedom."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 167,\n    "timestamp": "October 25, 2023(Wednesday) at 03:02 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Thanks, Sam. Just take it one day at a time. Celebrate small victories.\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! Focusing on small wins sounds like a plan. I\'ll take it one day at a time.\\nEvan: Exactly! Congrats on every little victory. Keep it up, I\'m here for you.\\nSam: Your support means everything. Here\'s to moving forward!\\nEvan: Anytime, Sam! Let\'s keep pushing ahead. I\'m here to help you. Take care!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 168,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:13 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Hey Evan! Hope you\'re doing good. Got some good news to share - I\'m a Weight Watchers coach in my group now! It\'s a pretty big accomplishment for me, feel really proud.\\nEvan: Congrats Sam! That\'s awesome! I\'m super proud of you. Becoming a Weight Watchers coach is a big deal. Keep going!\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! Appreciate your support. It\'s been a journey, and being chosen as a coach is a great step in my quest for better health.\\nEvan: Wow, Sam! You\'ve come such a long way. It\'s exciting to see what comes next for you in your quest for better health.\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! It feels great to see progress. Being a coach will hopefully keep me motivated and help others stay committed too. It\'s a big challenge, but I\'m ready for it!\\nEvan: That\'s awesome, Sam! Helping others stay committed and motivated is so rewarding. You really inspire us. Keep up the great work!\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! Your kind words mean a lot. It\'s been a difficult road, but I\'m determined to continue making a positive impact."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 169,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:16 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a guitar laying on the floor with a guitar strap] Sorry about missing any events, I\'ve had some personal challenges since we last spoke. Still here for you though - do you need any support or want to share anything? Btw look what i got!\\nSam: Hey, it looks so vintage and cool! What model is it? How\'ve you been doing lately? I\'m here if you wanna chat."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 170,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:17 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: It\'s a 1968 Kustom K-200A vintage guitar and I got it as a gift from a close friend. It\'s been a tough time for me since we last caught up; I lost my job last month, which has been pretty rough. But I really appreciate your support through all this."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 171,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:18 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Sorry to hear about your job, Evan. What happened?\\nEvan: It\'s been a bit of a rough patch lately. The company downsized, and I was part of that. I\'m currently on the hunt for a new job, which hasn\'t been easy, but I\'m keeping my spirits up and staying hopeful.\\nSam: Sorry about your job, Evan. It\'s tough when it comes out of nowhere, but I\'m proud of how you\'re handling it. Let me know if you need someone to talk to or if I can do anything to help. You\'ll get through this.\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam. Your support means a lot. It\'s been quite a ride, but I really appreciate having someone like you to talk to. I\'ll definitely reach out if I need anything.\\nSam: For sure, Evan! I\'m here for ya. Life can be tough sometimes, but we got this. Stay positive and it\'ll all work out. Just know that I\'m here if you need someone to talk to."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 172,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:20 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a person walking on the beach with a surfboard] Thanks, Sam. Your kind words and support mean a lot. It\'s great to have you here. I\'m gonna stay positive and keep going. Cheers!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 173,\n    "timestamp": "November 09, 2023(Thursday) at 09:21 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow, that sunset is stunning! It\'s so soothing just to see it. Is that a special spot you go to watch sunsets?\\nEvan: Yeah, it\'s this peaceful place close to my home. I often go there to relax and unwind.\\nSam: That sounds wonderful, Evan! I\'d love to check it out with you sometime.\\nEvan: Oh, I wish I could bring you along. That picture was actually taken last Friday at my favorite spot by the beach. Watching the waves and the sunset colors really helps me find peace, especially during tough times. It\'s a beautiful reminder of nature\'s resilience. We should definitely plan to go together someday.\\nSam: No worries, Evan. And yes, we should make a plan to go. That photo is just mesmerizing!\\nEvan: I\'m glad you like it! It\'s a really calming place. Let\'s make a point to visit it together soon.\\nSam: Absolutely, Evan! A trip there sounds like the perfect way to de-stress.\\nEvan: Awesome, let\'s do it! Let\'s plan it for next month, I\'m already excited about exploring it together!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 174,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:30 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Hey Ev! Long time no chat. How\'s it going? Hope all is well.\\nEvan: Hey Sam, good to hear from you! Life\'s been a wild ride lately. Last week, I had a health scare and had to go to the hospital. They found something suspicious during a check-up, which freaked me out. Thankfully, it was all a misunderstanding, but it made me realize how important it is to keep an eye on my health."\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."