joy the moment.\\nSam: That\'s awesome, Evan! Let\'s make it a habit to appreciate something each day."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 180,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:33 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: It really helps us enjoy life more. What do you think?\\nEvan: Sounds good, Sam! Let\'s take the time to appreciate the little things in life."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 181,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:34 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks for always being there, Evan. It means a lot.\\nEvan: Sure, Sam. I\'m here for you. We gotta stick together, especially now."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 182,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:35 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yeah, Evan. Life can be tough sometimes, but having supportive people like you makes it way easier.\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a group of people sitting around a fire pit] Yeah, Sam. Tough times are way easier with friends we can rely on. We\'ve got each other!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 183,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:36 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Looks like you\'re having a blast! I was wondering, what do you do to stay fit and healthy?\\nEvan: That was wild! I stay in shape by hitting the gym and taking my car out for a spin. Gotta keep it up!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 184,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:36 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: How are you doing on your fitness goals, Sam?\\nSam: Fitness goals have been hard to reach, but hey, that\'s life!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 185,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:37 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a small island with a lone boat in the water] Yeah Sam, it\'s true. Progress takes time, so keep pushing.\\nSam: Where is that? It looks gorgeous!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 186,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:38 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a sun shining through the clouds over a body of water] This little island is where I grew up and it\'s my happy place.\\nSam: Wow, that spot looks gorgeous. Growing up there must have been so peaceful and stunning."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 187,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:39 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yeah, it was. That place shaped me and will always hold a special place in my heart.\\nSam: Yeah, it can be soul-calming."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 188,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:40 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a person walking on a beach at sunset] Yeah, it really is. So serene and calming.\\nSam: It\'s heavenly!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 189,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:41 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a sunset over a body of water] Yeah, it\'s like a little slice of paradise. I always feel so peaceful and serene when I\'m there.\\nSam: Wow, it really seems like a peaceful retreat. Thanks for showing me!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 190,\n    "timestamp": "November 21, 2023(Tuesday) at 07:42 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: No prob, always good to chat about those tranquil times. Take it easy!\\nSam: Take care, buddy. Hang in there!\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam. If you need to talk, I\'m here for you too."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 191,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:16 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Hey Sam, good to hear from you. I\'ve hit a bit of a snag - my new Prius, the one I just bought, broke down. It\'s a bit of a stressor since I rely on it for my active lifestyle and road trips. It\'s frustrating when new things go awry so soon.\\nSam: Hey Evan, that\'s rough. Dealing with a new car breaking down is such a hassle, especially when it\'s your main mode of transport."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 192,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:17 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: You\'re telling me. I was really counting on this new Prius to be reliable. It\'s always a challenge when you have to deal with unexpected issues like this. But, I guess it\'s just one of those things - even new cars can have problems.\\nSam: It\'s tough when your plans get derailed by something like this. But hey, sometimes these setbacks lead to new opportunities.\\nEvan: True, I\'m trying to see it as a chance to explore other ways of staying active and traveling. Maybe it\'s an opportunity to try something different."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 193,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:18 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a variety of bowls of fruit and yogurt] Exactly, it\'s all about finding the silver lining. Speaking of new things, I attended a Weight Watchers meeting yesterday. Learned some great tips."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 194,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:19 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: That smoothie bowl looks fantastic! How was the meeting? Yeah, I\'ve been thinking about trying yoga, something gentle yet effective for stress relief and flexibility. What\'s your take on it, Sam?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 195,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:19 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: The meeting was really insightful, and that smoothie bowl was a hit! Yoga\'s a great choice, it\'s done wonders for my flexibility and stress levels. You should definitely try it.\\nEvan: I think I will. Thanks for the suggestion, Sam.\\nSam: Anytime, Evan. If you need any yoga tips or anything else, just let me know."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 196,\n    "timestamp": "December 05, 2023(Tuesday) at 08:21 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Your support\'s been invaluable. Thanks again, Sam!\\nSam: No worries, Evan. We all need a bit of help when trying new things. It\'s great to have support.\\nEvan: Absolutely. It makes a big difference knowing you\'re not alone in these situations.\\nSam: Definitely. Take care, and let me know how the yoga goes. Bye!\\nEvan: Will do. Thanks for everything, Sam. Talk soon. Bye!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 197,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:45 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Hey Sam, hope you\'re doing good. Wanted to share some amazing news - my partner is pregnant! We\'re so excited! It\'s been a while since we had a kiddo around.\\nSam: Congrats, Ev! That\'s great news! Parenthood is so amazing."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 198,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:45 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: How are you feeling about it?\\nEvan: So excited and a bit nervous! It\'s been a while since I had a toddler around but I\'m really looking forward to it. Parenthood is so rewarding. I still remember when my first child was born, the joy was amazing. Looking forward to witness the miracle of life and build more memories with my family!\\nSam: Wow, you\'re gonna be an amazing parent! Treasure those memories, they\'re truly special."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 199,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:47 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a desk with a lamp, a picture frame, and a sign] Thanks Sam! Absolutely. Talking of memories, I want to show you this. It\'s a collage of some of our top family memories. Each photo has an amazing moment - birthdays, holidays, vacations - so good to look back and recall all the great times we had.\\nSam: That\'s so lovely, Evan. Your family looks so happy."\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL units in order (unit_id 0, 1, 2, ...)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Each narrative should be self-contained and retrievable\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
