2025-12-18 01:41:08,453 - [add-v4-8-narr-batch8] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8823b77f-2931-4372-a883-69a712e30b77', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an episodic memory generation expert. Convert each conversation unit into an episodic memory.\n\n**Conversation Units to Process:**\n[\n  {\n    "unit_id": 200,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:47 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: What\'s the story behind that sign in the center?\\nEvan: Oh, that one? It\'s from our trip to Banff. We have this sign in the frame that says \'Bring it on Home\' - it\'s our family\'s motto, always reminding us of the importance of togetherness, no matter where we are.\\nSam: That\'s really touching, Evan. It\'s important to have something that keeps the family bond strong."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 201,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:49 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Absolutely, Sam. My family means the world to me. They\'re my rock. I\'m looking forward to expanding our family and creating even more beautiful memories.\\nSam: That\'s wonderful to hear, Evan! It\'s clear how much you value your family."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 202,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:49 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Are you thinking of any specific plans or events to add to that collage?\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam! Yeah, we\'re planning a big family reunion next summer. It\'s going to be a blast and a perfect opportunity to add to our collage.\\nSam: Sounds fantastic! If you need any tips on organizing such a big event, just let me know. I\'m always here to support and celebrate your family\'s milestones."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 203,\n    "timestamp": "December 09, 2023(Saturday) at 01:51 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Thanks, Sam! Your support means a lot. I\'ll keep you updated. Take care, bye!\\nSam: Take care, Evan! Can\'t wait to hear about it. Bye!\\nEvan: Bye Sam. I\'ll definitely keep you updated. Thanks for the kind words and support. Take care!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 204,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:48 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Hey Sam, what\'s up? Long time no see, huh? Lots has happened.\\nSam: Hey Evan! Long time no see. I\'m doing okay, been through a few bumps."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 205,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:48 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: How about you?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a young boy with crutches and a backpack] It\'s not easy for us right now, my son had an accident last Tuesday, he fell off his bike and it was rough. But he\'s doing better now."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 206,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:49 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: How are you dealing with all this?\\nSam: Darn, sorry to hear that. Hope he\'s feeling better. Same here, it\'s been tough lately."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 207,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:49 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: After we talked, I started thinking about ways to cope with it, but it\'s been challenging."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 208,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:50 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Life can be hard sometimes. Do you have any hobbies or activities that make you happy?\\nSam: I used to love hiking, but it\'s been a while since I had the chance to do it."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 209,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:51 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: I remember you mentioning that! Hiking is indeed a great way to center oneself and be one with nature. We should definitely plan a hike soon!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 210,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:51 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Yeah, I\'m struggling with my weight and it\'s affecting my confidence. I feel like I can\'t overcome all the challenges with my weight, I keep lacking motivation."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 211,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:52 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yeah, I understand it can be challenging. But remember, it\'s important to believe in yourself and take it one day at a time, Sam. Your worth is not defined by your weight.\\nSam: Cheers, Evan. Appreciate the help. It\'s tough breaking out of my comfort zone."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 212,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:53 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Stepping out of your comfort zone can be intimidating, but it\'s totally worth it. Just challenge yourself to try something new, even if it\'s just a little thing. You got this!\\nSam: Thanks, Evan. I\'ll take your advice. Trying new things can be difficult."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 213,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a woman standing in front of a painting] Yeah, trying something new and succeeding gives a great feeling of accomplishment. Give it a go, even if it\'s just a little thing. You\'ll be amazed!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 214,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:54 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: She looks so confident! What kind of painting is that in the background?\\nEvan: This is a contemporary figurative painting that I\'ve finished few days ago, emphasizing the emotional state through expressive brushwork and vibrant color choices. It captures a moment of introspection, where the subject is deeply immersed in thought. Very proud of it!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 215,\n    "timestamp": "December 17, 2023(Sunday) at 06:55 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: That\'s amazing work, who\'s the girl standing next to painting?\\nEvan: That\'s a close friend of mine who helped me get this painting published in the exhibition!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 216,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:25 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Hey Evan! Long time no see, how\'s it going?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photography of a bride and groom kissing in front of a tree] Hey Sam! Long time no see! Been up and down lately, got married last week - how about you?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 217,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:26 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Congratulations, Evan! Is that the woman from Canada?\\nEvan: Yes, that\'s her, I don\'t know why we didn\'t get married before, because I was in love with her at first sight!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 218,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:27 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow, Evan! Love at first sight? That sounds like something straight out of a fairy tale. What are your thoughts on it? Do you believe in love at first sight?\\nEvan: I totally believe in it. It was like time stopped and I felt like a spark lit inside me - it was so right.\\nSam: That\'s awesome, Evan! Finding that kind of connection must feel really liberating. Love can be so powerful, huh?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 219,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:28 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a person sitting on a rock near the water] Yeah, Sam, love is truly amazing. It brings so much happiness and fulfillment, like a beautiful sunset that lights up our lives and brings peace. Incredible!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 220,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:29 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wish I could feel the same about love, but I\'ve started to enjoy running in the mornings, and it\'s been a great way to clear my head. What can you do, right?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a painting with a white background and a blue, orange, and black painting] Yeah, I get it. Life\'s all about finding what works for you. Like your morning runs, they\'re a step towards something good, right? Keep trying new things, Sam, and you might find your own version of love in the most unexpected places. Embrace the journey — it’s full of surprises!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 221,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:30 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Such a minimalistic and stunning piece of work, I wonder what inspired the artist to create it.\\nEvan: The painting is mine, I made it when I was a mix of emotions - sad, mad, and hopeful. Art is amazing how it can portray feelings without words.\\nSam: Wow, Evan! Art is really amazing at expressing emotions - it\'s truly fascinating."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 222,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:31 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a painting with a bird flying over it] It\'s amazing how art can express emotions so well. It really helps me recognize and handle my own feelings. This painting is giving me a massive rush of joy!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 223,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:32 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: That\'s stunning! What emotions did you create this painting with?\\nEvan: I painted this with a sense of joy and freedom. The spontaneous strokes and bold colors reflect a playful and liberated mood, embracing the creative process without restraint."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 224,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:33 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a woman holding flowers in front of her face] Wow, Evan, this is amazing! You\'ve got serious talent and creativity. Making this must have been so satisfying! Here\'s a painting that inspired me when I went to an exhibit few days ago.\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam! I appreciate the compliment. This painting has such an inspiring vibe; you really have a knack for understanding art! How about you? How long have you been painting?"\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL units in order (unit_id 0, 1, 2, ...)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Each narrative should be self-contained and retrievable\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
