2025-12-18 01:41:46,547 - [add-v4-8-narr-batch9] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-737675cc-aaa4-45f6-8624-81d3056466b1', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': '\nYou are an episodic memory generation expert. Convert each conversation unit into an episodic memory.\n\n**Conversation Units to Process:**\n[\n  {\n    "unit_id": 225,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:34 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: I do sketch occasionally, but I haven\'t created anything remarkable yet. I have a feeling I\'ll have something to show off before long! Seeing your passion for it is inspiring.\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam! Glad I could motivate you. If you ever want to give it a go, I\'m happy to help get you started. Speaking of which, you know what? I lost my keys again, it\'s become a weekly ritual for me!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 226,\n    "timestamp": "December 26, 2023(Tuesday) at 04:35 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Ooh, Evan, I\'d put a GPS sensor on your keys!\\nEvan: Great idea, I think I\'ll do that as soon as I find it!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 227,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:00 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photography of a man standing on a rock looking out over a valley] Hey Evan! I’m really getting into this healthier lifestyle—just took my friends on an epic hiking trip last Friday!\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a small stream running through a lush green forest] Hey Sam! That’s fantastic—nothing like a good hike to feel alive."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 228,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:00 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: We took the Prius for a long drive to the mountains last weekend. It was perfect until we got into a little scrape on the way back.\\nSam: Oh no, were you guys okay after the accident?\\nEvan: Yeah, we were fine, thanks. Just a minor accident, but it put a bit of a damper on telling my work friends about getting married. They’ve been a great support, though."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 229,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:02 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: I bet they were thrilled to hear about your marriage, despite the mishap!\\nEvan: Absolutely, it\'s been a whirlwind of emotions. Good thing the accident was minor. Just a reminder to take it easy on the road, I guess.\\nSam: True, it’s important to stay safe. Glad you can still enjoy the peaceful moments after something like that.\\nEvan: Definitely, nature brings peace and clarity - it\'s a great experience.\\nSam: Nature can make everything else seem small and help us find peace inside. It reminds us of the bigger picture, you know?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 230,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:04 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a woman sitting at a table with plates and glasses] For sure, and nature has been a great healer. Speaking of which, I’ve got to share some of these new healthy snacks I’ve been trying.\\nSam: They look healthy and delicious! Perfect for after a hike or, I guess, post-accident recovery, huh?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a bunch of cookies on a cooling rack] Exactly! They’re packed with nutrients and really easy to make. You also need to try these cookies, they are awesome! I’ll send you the recipes.\\nSam: Thanks, I’d appreciate that. It’s good to find new ways to stay healthy. Do you have any healthier snack ideas?\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a bowl of coconut balls and a bowl of oats] Yeah, I\'ve been trying to eat healthier too. Check out this cool recipe I discovered for these energy balls.\\nSam: Do you like them? I know they can be an acquired taste.\\nEvan: I enjoy the taste of these. They\'re energizing and a healthy way to satisfy your sweet tooth.\\nSam: Awesome! Always on the lookout for healthy snacks, thanks for the tip!\\nEvan: Glad to help - hope you enjoy it!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 231,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:09 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Thanks, Evan! I\'ll give these a try. They look yum. Your help means a lot to me."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 232,\n    "timestamp": "December 31, 2023(Sunday) at 11:09 AM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Btw you know what? I went to the store again and, unsurprisingly, had issues with the self-checkout. It\'s becoming a regular annoyance.\\nEvan: That\'s very strange, I\'ve never had a problem with it once!\\nSam: Apparently I attract that to me, if you ever want to be in that situation, call me at the store with you!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 233,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:32 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a man and a woman standing on a rocky beach] Hey Sam, guess what? My partner and I told our extended fam about our marriage yesterday – it was so special! We\'ve been totally overwhelmed by all their love and support.\\nSam: Congrats on the news, Evan! You two look so happy in the pic. These moments make life so wonderful; super stoked for you!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 234,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:33 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Thanks, Sam! It was an awesome moment, and I feel really lucky to have found someone who gets me. Plus, our families are really happy for us - that\'s the best part!\\nSam: Wow, Evan. It\'s awesome that you\'ve found someone who gets you! Having your family\'s support must feel great.\\nEvan: Definitely, family support is so important. Knowing they\'re happy about our marriage is awesome and so comforting.\\nSam: Yeah, it\'s awesome to have that support. It definitely brings more happiness and joy.\\nEvan: Yeah Sam, that means a lot to me. Our bond just keeps getting stronger and it brings such a good feeling to our lives. Family really is everything.\\nSam: Agree, Evan! Family is everything - they bring so much love and happiness. They\'re always there for us no matter what. I\'m grateful for their support and love.\\nEvan: For sure, Sam. That\'s what makes family so special. They bring so much love and happiness. It\'s great having their support and knowing they\'re always there for us. I feel really fortunate to have their never-ending love and support.\\nSam: Yeah, definitely, Evan. We both have amazing families that are always there for us. Always a blessing.\\nEvan: Yeah, Sam. Our families give us so much joy, support, and love. They\'re a real blessing! I don\'t know what I\'d do without them.\\nSam: Hey, Evan. My family has been my rock through everything. Don\'t know what I\'d do without them.\\nEvan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a group of people sitting at a table with food] Yeah, they are our rock. We\'re blessed to have them."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 235,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:38 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: Wow, you guys are awesome! What\'s cooking tonight?\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam! We\'re having a family get-together tonight and enjoying some homemade lasagna. Super excited! By the way, I\'ve started a new diet—limiting myself to just two ginger snaps a day. What\'s on your menu tonight?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 236,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:39 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: By the way, I\'ve started a new diet—limiting myself to just two ginger snaps a day. What\'s on your menu tonight?\\nSam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a plate of food with bread and meat] That\'s a great discipline, Evan! We\'re keeping it light tonight, just some homemade lasagna. Can\'t compete with your ginger snap limit though!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 237,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:40 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Oh this must be very hearty and delicious, well I\'ll have to stick to the diet plan, even with the family gathering!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 238,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:40 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a pie with raspberries and limes on top] Yeah, the lasagna was pretty awesome, but check out what I had for dessert, I\'m sure you\'re drooling!\\nEvan: Looks yummy! Did you make that?\\nSam: No, I didn\'t make it. This is actually a pic from my cousin\'s wedding. It\'s super special."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 239,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:42 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a wedding cake with candles and flowers on a table] Wow Sam! Weddings are indeed special. This looks great, yum!\\nSam: Ooh, nice cake! Reminds me of special occasions. Do you have any upcoming plans?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 240,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:43 PM",\n    "messages": "Evan: [Evan shared an image: a photo of a stream running through a snowy forest filled with snow] Thanks Sam! We\'re off to Canada next month for our honeymoon. So excited to create some awesome memories. Looking forward to exploring the beautiful snowy landscapes there.\\nSam: Wow, that looks great! What are your plans for the trip?\\nEvan: We\'re planning to ski, try the local cuisine, and enjoy the beautiful views. We\'re really excited!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 241,\n    "timestamp": "January 06, 2024(Saturday) at 01:44 PM",\n    "messages": "Sam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a container of french fries covered in caramel] Sounds amazing, Ev! Skiing, trying local dishes, and enjoying the breathtaking views - the perfect honeymoon. Have an incredible time creating unforgettable memories!\\nEvan: Yeah, Sam! Gonna try some poutine while we\'re there - can\'t wait!\\nSam: Never tried it? Can\'t say I blame you, it\'s kind of a Canadian thing. Let me know how you like it!\\nEvan: Sure thing, Sam! Let\'s see if it lives up to the hype. I\'ll let you know what happens!\\nSam: Yeah, Evan! Let me know all about it. Don\'t forget the details!\\nEvan: Cool, Sam. I\'ll keep you posted. Talk soon!\\nSam: Awesome, Evan! Catch you soon. Have a great trip!\\nEvan: Thanks, Sam! Catch you later. Have a great one!"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 242,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:17 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Hey Sam, hope you\'re doing good. Something funny happened last night.\\nSam: Hey Evan, what\'s up? What happened? Let me know."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 243,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:18 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yesterday I went out with my friends and had a bit too much to drink. I ended up doing something I regret and it involved someone\'s roses.\\nSam: What\'s up with that incident? All good now?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 244,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:19 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Oof, Sam, so embarrassing! I had a pee accident near some roses - can you believe it? I\'m so sorry about that.\\nSam: Uh oh, Evan! That\'s awkward. Did anyone get mad at you? Are you okay?"\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 245,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:20 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: I was so embarrassed when I saw what happened the next morning, so I apologized and luckily they were understanding. Yeah, I was out of control--guess I gotta be more careful next time.\\nSam: They were understanding? Phew! We all mess up sometimes, we\'re human after all."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 246,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:21 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Yeah, they were understanding, which was great. But it\'s a good reminder to be more careful. We all make mistakes, but it\'s important to learn from them."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 247,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:21 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Speaking of, my partner and I tried snowshoeing this weekend. It was part of a new adventure for us and surprisingly fun.\\nSam: [Sam shared an image: a photo of a white board with a bunch of writing on it] Yeah, Evan, you\'re right. Mistakes happen, but it\'s good to learn from them. Snowshoeing sounds like a great way to stay active during the winter. I\'ve been thinking and I made a meal plan and workout schedule. I\'m getting motivated by something I saw, so starting today I\'m gonna do my best to stay on track."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 248,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:22 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: Good work, Sam! You\'ve got a plan and you\'re dedicated to staying healthy - have you asked your doctor for advice? They could probably give you even more diet and exercise tips.\\nSam: Thanks, Evan! Haven\'t seen a doctor in a while, but it\'s probably a good idea to get some advice. I\'m going to make an appointment soon."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 249,\n    "timestamp": "January 10, 2024(Wednesday) at 12:23 AM",\n    "messages": "Evan: What advice are you planning to get from the doctor?\\nSam: I\'m gonna ask the doc about a balanced diet plan and getting advice on low-impact exercises, given my current situation."\n  }\n]\n\n**Instructions:**\nFor each unit, generate a structured episodic memory with:\n1. `title`: A concise, descriptive title (10-20 words) that includes key topics/activities\n2. `content`: A detailed third-person narrative following ALL requirements below\n\n**IMPORTANT TIME HANDLING:**\n- Use each unit\'s timestamp as the exact time when that conversation/episode began\n- When the conversation mentions relative times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week"), preserve both the original relative expression AND calculate the absolute date\n- Format time references as: "original relative time (absolute date)" - e.g., "last week (May 7, 2023)"\n- This dual format supports both absolute and relative time-based questions\n\n**Requirements for `content`:**\n1. The content must include all important information from the conversation.\n2. Convert the dialogue format into a narrative description.\n3. Maintain chronological order and causal relationships.\n4. Use third-person unless explicitly first-person.\n5. Include specific details that aid keyword search, especially concrete activities, places, and objects.\n6. For time references, use the dual format: "relative time (absolute date)" to support different question types.\n7. When describing decisions or actions, naturally include the reasoning or motivation behind them.\n8. Use specific names consistently rather than pronouns to avoid ambiguity in retrieval.\n9. CRITICAL DETAIL PRESERVATION:\n   - Person Names: Always include full names of people mentioned (e.g., "went to yoga with Amy\'s colleague, Rob" not just "went to yoga with a colleague")\n   - Special Nouns & Entities: Preserve all proper nouns, brand names, place names, organization names exactly as mentioned\n   - Item Names: Include specific product names, book titles, movie names, restaurant names, etc.\n   - Quantities & Numbers: Record exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times (e.g., "ordered 3 pizzas" not "ordered pizzas")\n   - Specific Activities: Use precise activity descriptions (e.g., "practiced hot yoga" not just "exercised")\n   - Time Points: Include all specific times mentioned (e.g., "at 3:30 PM", "every Tuesday", "twice a week")\n10. FREQUENCY INFORMATION:\n   - Record recurring activities and their frequency (e.g., "goes to yoga class every Tuesday and Thursday")\n   - Note patterns of behavior (e.g., "mentioned calling mom three times during the conversation")\n   - Include habitual actions (e.g., "usually has coffee at 8 AM before work")\n   - Document repetition counts (e.g., "asked about the project status twice")\n\n**Output Format (BATCH):**\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL units:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "title": "Descriptive title here",\n            "content": "Detailed narrative content here..."\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "title": "...",\n            "content": "..."\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL units in order (unit_id 0, 1, 2, ...)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Each narrative should be self-contained and retrievable\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
