oto of himself performing a squat on a gym machine. He acknowledged that health challenges could be discouraging. Evan described how he had started lifting weights one year ago and found it to be a challenging but rewarding journey, noting visible progress. Evan offered to support Sam if he was interested in trying weightlifting."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 122,\n    "timestamp": "October 08, 2023(Sunday) at 03:10 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 03:10 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed interest in starting weightlifting and asked Evan for advice on how to begin."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 123,\n    "timestamp": "October 08, 2023(Sunday) at 03:10 PM",\n    "narrative": "Also at 03:10 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan encouraged Sam by emphasizing the importance of starting with proper form and technique. He recommended finding a trainer to help avoid injuries while building strength. Evan advised starting with light weights and gradually increasing intensity as strength improved. He stressed the importance of consistency in the workout routine and invited Sam to keep him updated on his progress, wishing him good luck."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 124,\n    "timestamp": "October 08, 2023(Sunday) at 03:11 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 03:11 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Sam thanked Evan for the advice and stated his intention to find a trainer to assist him. Sam promised to keep Evan informed about his weightlifting journey."\n  }\n]\n\n---\n\n### EXTRACTION RULES\n\n#### 1. Atomicity\n* Each entry in `"atomic_fact"` must express **exactly one coherent unit of meaning** — an action, emotion, reason, plan, decision, or statement.\n* If a speaker expresses multiple ideas (e.g., an event and its reason), split them into multiple atomic facts.\n* Each atomic_fact must be **independent and retrievable on its own**.\n\n#### 2. Time & Date Handling\n* Do **not** add or prepend timestamps such as "On March 10, 2024" to each fact.\n* The `"time"` field already represent