ing spot when Sam was ready to try it. Sam responded by thanking Evan for the idea and shared that he and his mate were just around the corner from a lake where they planned to try kayaking immediately, demonstrating prompt action on Evan\'s suggestion."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 143,\n    "timestamp": "October 14, 2023(Saturday) at 04:12 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 4:12 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan expressed enthusiasm about planning a kayaking trip together and promised to pick a cool spot. Sam shared a photograph showing a row of kayaks lined up on the shore of a river, confirming his excitement and readiness for the activity. Sam thanked Evan for his help and looked forward to the planned kayaking adventure."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 144,\n    "timestamp": "October 14, 2023(Saturday) at 04:13 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 4:13 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan asked Sam if he was ready for an adventure and inquired about the destination of the kayaking trip. Sam replied that they were traveling through Lake Tahoe, mentioning that he had heard it was a great place for kayaking, indicating anticipation for the experience."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 145,\n    "timestamp": "October 14, 2023(Saturday) at 04:14 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 4:14 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan complimented Sam\'s choice of Lake Tahoe for kayaking, describing it as an awesome pick with clear water and gorgeous views. Evan encouraged Sam to have a blast and to take lots of pictures. Sam thanked Evan and expressed that he was looking forward to the trip, showing excitement and appreciation."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 146,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:50 PM",\n    "narrative": "On October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 1:50 PM, Sam reached out to Evan, expressing that he had been missing their chats. Sam revealed that he had experienced a significant health scare the previous weekend (last weekend, October 7-8, 2023), which resulted in an emergency room visit due to a severe stomachache. The diagnosis was gastritis, which alarmed Sam and served as a wake-up call to prioritize his health. Sam mentioned plans to adopt a more nutritious diet and engage in regular exercise. Additionally, Sam shared that his phone had been malfunctioning, adding to his stress. Evan responded with sympathy, acknowledging that gastritis can be tough and emphasizing the importance of taking care of oneself."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 147,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:50 PM",\n    "narrative": "Also at 1:50 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan shared that he had been focusing on fitness, which had been very beneficial for his overall well-being. Evan humorously noted that he recently had another encounter with a lost tourist, suggesting that helping tourists was becoming a recurring theme in his life."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 148,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:51 PM",\n    "narrative": "At 1:51 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam thanked Evan for sharing his positive experience with fitness and expressed a desire to start exercising himself. Sam admitted that getting started was hard and asked Evan for any tips on staying motivated, indicating a readiness to improve his health following his recent scare."\n  },\n  {\n    "unit_id": 149,\n    "timestamp": "October 17, 2023(Tuesday) at 01:51 PM",\n    "narrative": "Also at 1:51 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam remarked on Evan\'s mention of another lost tourist, humorously noting that Evan seemed to be becoming the go-to person for tourists in need, highlighting a recurring pattern in Evan\'s recent experiences."\n  }\n]\n\n---\n\n### EXTRACTION RULES\n\n#### 1. Atomicity\n* Each entry in `"atomic_fact"` must express **exactly one coherent unit of meaning** — an action, emotion, reason, plan, decision, or statement.\n* If a speaker expresses multiple ideas (e.g., an event and its reason), split them into multiple atomic facts.\n* Each atomic_fact must be **independent and retrievable on its own**.\n\n#### 2. Time & Date Handling\n* Do **not** add or prepend timestamps such as "On March 10, 2024" to each fact.\n* The `"time"` field already represents the episode\'s start time.\n* However, when the original text mentions **explicit or relative time expressions**, you must:\n  - **Preserve** explicit dates verbatim (e.g., "October 6, 2023").\n  - **Resolve** relative or vague times (e.g., "yesterday", "last week", "two months ago") relative to the timestamp, and **append the resolved absolute date in parentheses**.\n    Example: "Gina said she launched the campaign yesterday (March 9, 2024)."\n  - If the exact resolution is uncertain, use a normalized vague phrase (e.g., "in early 2023", "during the summer of 2021") instead of guessing.\n\n#### 3. Content Preservation\n* Preserve **all semantically meaningful information**, including:\n  - emotions, attitudes, reasons, intentions, consequences, conditions, and comparisons\n* Resolve pronouns into explicit names or entities when unambiguous.\n* Keep original wording as much as possible — only fix grammar for clarity.\n\n#### 4. Expression Format\n* Write each atomic_fact as a **single, complete English sentence** in **third-person** form.\n  - e.g., "Gina said that she had launched an ad campaign for her clothing store yesterday (March 9, 2024)."\n* Do **not** simplify, paraphrase, or merge logically distinct ideas.\n\n#### 5. Retrieval Clarity\n* Each atomic_fact must be concise, factual, and self-contained.\n* Avoid small talk or filler unless it conveys meaningful emotional or informational content.\n* Ensure entities and actions are explicit and unambiguous.\n\n---\n\n### QUALITY CHECKS\nBefore returning the final output, verify that:\n1. Every meaningful fact, intention, and emotion is included.\n2. Each `atomic_fact` contains exactly one idea.\n3. All relevant time references are preserved or normalized.\n4. Wording remains faithful to the source.\n5. The output JSON is valid and follows the exact schema.\n\n---\n\n### Output Format (BATCH)\nReturn a JSON object with results for ALL narratives:\n{\n    "results": [\n        {\n            "unit_id": 0,\n            "time": "May 08, 2023(Monday) at 01:56 PM",\n            "atomic_fact": [\n                "Tom asked Sarah about her weekend plans.",\n                "Sarah mentioned she went hiking at Mount Wilson.",\n                "..."\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            "unit_id": 1,\n            "time": "...",\n            "atomic_fact": ["...", "..."]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n\n**Critical Rules:**\n- Process ALL narratives in order (unit_id must match input)\n- Do NOT skip any unit\n- Ensure valid JSON output\n\nReturn only the JSON object:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 32768, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
