im updated on his progress, wishing him good luck.\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Evan Encourages Sam to Start Workouts and Offers Exercise Guidance\n  Content: On June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:01 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man with a beard holding a dumbbell to Sam, expressing his enthusiasm and support for their workout goals. Evan emphasized that exercise clears the mind and encouraged Sam to join him in reaching their fitness objectives. Sam responded positively, expressing excitement and requesting help to get started with exercising. Evan gladly offered to meet with Sam to demonstrate some basic exercises, reinforcing their shared commitment ...\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Evan Encourages Sam to Start Exercising and Plans a Hike Together\n  Content: On October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Sam commits to finding a trainer and promises to keep Evan updated on progress\n  Content: At 03:11 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Sam thanked Evan for the advice and stated his intention to find a trainer to assist him. Sam promised to keep Evan informed about his weightlifting journey.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Sam starts new diet and exercise; Evan suffers knee injury impacting fitness\n  Content: On August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:18 AM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had started a new diet and exercise routine the previous Monday (August 21, 2023) and that it had made a huge difference, making him feel great. Sam asked Evan about any recent changes in his life. Evan responded that he was glad Sam\'s new routine was going well but shared that he had twisted his knee the previous Friday (August 25, 2023), causing significant pain and making it difficult to maintain his usual fitness ro...\n\nDocument 8:\n  Title: Sam Shares Frustration About Broken Self-Checkout Machines After Shopping\n  Content: At 4:02 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam told Evan that he was excited about starting workouts but shared a recent frustrating experience at the supermarket. Sam explained that all the self-checkout machines were broken when he tried to shop, which negatively affected his mood. This incident occurred just before their conversation, as Sam mentioned he was coming from the shop.\n\nDocument 9:\n  Title: Sam Seeks Tips from Evan on Staying Motivated to Start Fitness Routine\n  Content: At 1:51 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam thanked Evan for sharing his positive experience with fitness and expressed a desire to start exercising himself. Sam admitted that getting started was hard and asked Evan for any tips on staying motivated, indicating a readiness to improve his health following his recent scare.\n\nDocument 10:\n  Title: Evan Shares Personal Fitness Routine and Diet Tips for Health Improvement\n  Content: At 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Evan shared that what worked for him was finding a fitness routine he genuinely enjoyed, which became his go-to activity. He loved the feeling of being healthy and strong. Evan emphasized making exercise fun and incorporating small smarter dietary choices that added up over time. He encouraged Sam by affirming that Sam had the capability to succeed.\n\n\n**Instructions**:\nFollow these steps to ensure an accurate evaluation:\n\n1.  **Deconstruct the Query**: Break down the user\'s query into its core informational needs (e.g., who, what, where, when, why, how). Identify all key entities and concepts.\n2.  **Scan for Keywords**: Quickly scan the documents for the key entities and concepts from the query. This is a preliminary check for relevance.\n3.  **Detailed Analysis**: Read the relevant parts of the documents carefully. Determine if they contain explicit facts that directly answer *all aspects* of the query. Do not rely on making significant inferences or assumptions. The answer should be explicitly stated or very easily pieced together from the text.\n4.  **Sufficiency Judgment**:\n    *   If all parts of the query are directly and explicitly answered, the documents are **sufficient**.\n    *   If any significant part of the query is not answered, the documents are **insufficient**.\n    *   If you are uncertain, err on the side of caution and label it as **insufficient**. Do not guess.\n5.  **Formulate Reasoning**: Based on your analysis, write a brief (1-2 sentences) explanation for your judgment.\n6.  **Identify Missing Information**: If the documents are insufficient, list the specific pieces of information that are missing to fully answer the query.\n\n**Output Format** (strict JSON, no additional text before or after the JSON block):\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true or false,\n  "reasoning": "Brief, clear explanation for your decision (1-2 sentences).",\n  "missing_information": ["list", "of", "specific", "missing", "information"]\n}\n\n**Examples**:\n\nExample 1 (Sufficient):\nQuery: "What is Alice\'s favorite hobby?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Alice mentioned she loves painting. She spends weekends at art galleries."\n  Document 2: "Alice\'s work involves creative projects."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true,\n  "reasoning": "Document 1 explicitly states that Alice\'s hobby is painting.",\n  "missing_information": []\n}\n\nExample 2 (Insufficient - Missing Detail):\nQuery: "Where did Bob go on vacation last year?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Bob talked about his work project deadline around June."\n  Document 2: "Bob likes to travel and explore new places. He recently came back from a trip."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention Bob likes to travel and recently took a trip, but do not specify where he went or if it was last year.",\n  "missing_information": ["specific vacation destination", "confirmat