or Introducing Him to Watercolor Painting\n  Content: At 1:54 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed admiration for Evan\'s painting skills and asked how Evan got into watercolor painting. Evan explained that a friend introduced him to the hobby and gave him advice, which led to him becoming hooked immediately.\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Evan lists essential painting supplies and offers to recommend specific items\n  Content: At 09:33 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan enthusiastically confirmed that painting is an excellent hobby. He advised Sam to acquire acrylic paints, brushes, a canvas or paper, and a palette for mixing colors. Evan also offered to provide specific product recommendations and suggested planning a painting session once Sam was ready.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Evan describes painting as self-expression based on feelings and memories\n  Content: At 09:02 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam praised Evan\'s artwork and inquired how Evan decided what to paint. Evan explained that he usually paints whatever is on his mind or reflects his feelings. His subjects often include good memories or places he wishes to visit. Evan described painting as a form of self-expression through art.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Evan Shares Watercolor Painting of Cactus as Stress-Relief Hobby\n  Content: Also at 1:53 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a watercolor painting depicting a cactus in the desert. He explained that painting was a great stress-buster for him and that he had started doing watercolor painting a few years ago.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Evan Shares Painting Depicting Joy and Freedom to Express Emotions\n  Content: At 4:31 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan shared a photo of another painting featuring a bird flying over it. He described how art helps him recognize and manage his own feelings. Evan explained that this particular painting gave him a massive rush of joy.\n\nDocument 8:\n  Title: Evan explains inspirations behind his sunset and cactus paintings from past trips\n  Content: At 09:01 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam complimented Evan\'s paintings and asked about the sources of inspiration. Evan explained that the sunset painting was inspired by a vacation taken a few years ago, highlighting the stunning colors he experienced. The cactus painting was inspired by a road trip taken the previous month (September 2023). Evan expressed enthusiasm about the interesting places that inspired his artwork.\n\nDocument 9:\n  Title: Evan and Sam agree to prepare supplies and paint together next Saturday\n  Content: At 09:34 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan confirmed the plan to prepare all necessary painting materials and proposed that they paint together the following Saturday. Evan expressed eagerness for the upcoming creative activity.\n\nDocument 10:\n  Title: Evan encourages Sam to try painting and offers to help with supplies\n  Content: At 09:32 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan responded to Sam\'s interest by describing painting as a very relaxing activity. Evan offered to assist Sam in getting started with painting, including recommending supplies, and invited Sam to let him know if he wanted to proceed.\n\n\n**Instructions**:\nFollow these steps to ensure an accurate evaluation:\n\n1.  **Deconstruct the Query**: Break down the user\'s query into its core informational needs (e.g., who, what, where, when, why, how). Identify all key entities and concepts.\n2.  **Scan for Keywords**: Quickly scan the documents for the key entities and concepts from the query. This is a preliminary check for relevance.\n3.  **Detailed Analysis**: Read the relevant parts of the documents carefully. Determine if they contain explicit facts that directly answer *all aspects* of the query. Do not rely on making significant inferences or assumptions. The answer should be explicitly stated or very easily pieced together from the text.\n4.  **Sufficiency Judgment**:\n    *   If all parts of the query are directly and explicitly answered, the documents are **sufficient**.\n    *   If any significant part of the query is not answered, the documents are **insufficient**.\n    *   If you are uncertain, err on the side of caution and label it as **insufficient**. Do not guess.\n5.  **Formulate Reasoning**: Based on your analysis, write a brief (1-2 sentences) explanation for your judgment.\n6.  **Identify Missing Information**: If the documents are insufficient, list the specific pieces of information that are missing to fully answer the query.\n\n**Output Format** (strict JSON, no additional text before or after the JSON block):\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true or false,\n  "reasoning": "Brief, clear explanation for your decision (1-2 sentences).",\n  "missing_information": ["list", "of", "specific", "missing", "information"]\n}\n\n**Examples**:\n\nExample 1 (Sufficient):\nQuery: "What is Alice\'s favorite hobby?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Alice mentioned she loves painting. She spends weekends at art galleries."\n  Document 2: "Alice\'s work involves creative projects."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true,\n  "reasoning": "Document 1 explicitly states that Alice\'s hobby is painting.",\n  "missing_information": []\n}\n\nExample 2 (Insufficient - Missing Detail):\nQuery: "Where did Bob go on vacation last year?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Bob talked about his work project deadline around June."\n  Document 2: "Bob likes to travel and explore new places. He recently came back from a trip."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention Bob likes to travel and recently took a trip, but do not specify where he went or if it was last year.",\n  "missing_information": ["specific vacation destination", "confirmation the trip was \'last year\'"]\n}\n\nExample 3 (Insufficient - Tangential Information):\nQuery: "What are the specs of the new \'Galaxy Z\' phone?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "The Galaxy Z is rumored to be released next month."\n  Document 2: "Tech enthusiasts are excited about the upcoming Galaxy Z launch event."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention the phone\'s upcoming release but provide no specific technical specifications.",\n  "missing_information": ["screen size", "processor type", "camera resolution", "battery capacity", "etc."]\n}\n\nNow evaluate:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
