ive update that he was taking a cooking class to learn how to make healthier meals. Evan expressed sympathy for Sam\'s rough week but noted that these challenges were forcing both of them to take better care of themselves. Evan mentioned hearing that Sam\'s cooking class was packed with healthy recipes and asked how it was going and whether Sam had picked up any new tasty meals.\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Sam Shares Photo of Grilled Salmon Dish from Cooking Class; Evan Requests Healthy Recipe Suggestions\n  Content: At 4:21 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a photo of a plate with a piece of salmon and some vegetables, reporting that the cooking class had been great and that he had learned awesome recipes. Sam described making a yummy grilled dish the previous night. Evan responded that the dish looked delicious and asked what ingredients Sam had used. Evan expressed interest in eating healthy and requested recipe suggestions.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Sam Shares Roasted Vegetable Recipe and Checks on Evan\'s Son\'s Recovery\n  Content: At 4:23 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam confirmed he had a tasty and easy roasted vegetable recipe to share with Evan. Sam then inquired about Evan\'s well-being after his son\'s soccer accident, acknowledging it must have been tough. Evan responded that his son\'s ankle was getting better but still sore. He described the initial period as rough but was thankful the injury was not serious.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Sam shares healthy diet progress with Evan and discusses positive effects\n  Content: On August 19, 2023 (Saturday) at 06:17 PM, Sam shared an image with Evan showing a bowl containing spinach, avocado, and strawberries. Sam announced that he was on a diet and living healthier, acknowledging that it had been tough but expressing determination to stick with it. Evan congratulated Sam on the great news and asked how the changes were going. Sam admitted it was tough but confirmed his persistence. Evan praised Sam\'