few years ago, highlighting the stunning colors he experienced. The cactus painting was inspired by a road trip taken the previous month (September 2023). Evan expressed enthusiasm about the interesting places that inspired his artwork.\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Evan Shares Watercolor Painting of Cactus as Stress-Relief Hobby\n  Content: Also at 1:53 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a watercolor painting depicting a cactus in the desert. He explained that painting was a great stress-buster for him and that he had started doing watercolor painting a few years ago.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Sam Compliments Evan’s Minimalistic Painting and Discusses Emotional Expression in Art\n  Content: At 4:30 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam admired the minimalistic and stunning nature of Evan’s painting and wondered about the inspiration behind it. Evan revealed that he had created the painting during a time when he was experiencing a mix of emotions including sadness, anger, and hopefulness. He reflected on how art can portray feelings without words. Sam expressed fascination with how art can express emotions so effectively.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Evan Identifies Woman in Photo as Close Friend Who Helped Publish Painting\n  Content: At 6:55 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Sam complimented Evan’s painting and asked who the girl standing next to it was. Evan explained that she was a close friend who had helped him get the painting published in an exhibition.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Sam Shares Inspirational Painting Photo and Praises Evan’s Artistic Talent\n  Content: At 4:33 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a photo of a woman holding flowers in front of her face, describing it as amazing and praising Evan’s serious talent and creativity. Sam noted that creating such a painting must have been very satisfying. Evan thanked Sam for the compliment and commented that the painting Sam shared had an inspiring vibe. Evan then asked Sam how long he