aking trip. Sam replied that they were traveling through Lake Tahoe, mentioning that he had heard it was a great place for kayaking, indicating anticipation for the experience.\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Evan Praises Lake Tahoe as Kayaking Destination; Sam Looks Forward to Trip\n  Content: At 4:14 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan complimented Sam\'s choice of Lake Tahoe for kayaking, describing it as an awesome pick with clear water and gorgeous views. Evan encouraged Sam to have a blast and to take lots of pictures. Sam thanked Evan and expressed that he was looking forward to the trip, showing excitement and appreciation.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Evan Recommends Kayaking as Outdoor Exercise; Sam Shows Enthusiasm to Try\n  Content: At 4:10 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan proposed kayaking as a fun and active outdoor hobby, describing it as paddling on a river or lake. Evan asked Sam for his thoughts on kayaking. Sam replied that kayaking sounded awesome and admitted he had not tried it yet but believed it would be a fun way to exercise and enjoy nature. Sam expressed definite interest in giving kayaking a try and thanked Evan for the suggestion.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Evan and Partner Plan Canadian Honeymoon with Skiing and Local Cuisine\n  Content: At 1:43 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan shared a photo of a stream running through a snowy forest and told Sam that he and his partner were going to Canada next month (February 2024) for their honeymoon. Evan expressed excitement about creating awesome memories and exploring the beautiful snowy landscapes. When Sam asked about their plans for the trip, Evan explained that they planned to ski, try local cuisine, and enjoy the beautiful views, emphasizing their excitement.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Evan recommends nearby lake with trails for Sam\'s hiking plans\n  Content: At 10:24 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed enthusiasm about hiking together and asked Evan which lake he recommended for exploring local trails. Evan shared another photo of a lake with a mountain in the background, describing it as gorgeous with many nearby trails that Sam would love. Sam admired the view and asked if the location was nearby. Evan said it was only a two-hour drive from their location but assured Sam that the trip was worth every minute due to the incredible views an...\n\nDocument 8:\n  Title: Sam Encourages Evan\'s Honeymoon Plans and Discusses Canadian Cuisine\n  Content: At 1:44 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Sam shared a photo of a container of caramel-covered french fries and commented that Evan\'s honeymoon plans sounded amazing, highlighting skiing, trying local dishes, and enjoying breathtaking views as the perfect combination. Evan mentioned he was looking forward to trying poutine while in Canada. Sam noted that he had never tried poutine and acknowledged it as a Canadian specialty, asking Evan to let him know how he liked it. Evan agreed to keep Sam po...\n\nDocument 9:\n  Title: Evan Shares Beach Sunset Photo as Low-Impact Exercise Suggestion; Sam Plans Beach Walks and Recurring Flying Dream\n  Content: At 12:27 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan shared a photo of a woman standing on a beach at sunset, suggesting that there are many enjoyable low-impact exercises beyond yoga, including beach walks. Evan described beach sunsets as both good exercise and calming experiences. Sam responded that the image looked zen and said he planned to try beach walks based on Evan\'s recommendation. Sam also shared that he had a recurring dream of flying over skyscrapers, which he wanted to brag about.\n\nDocument 10:\n  Title: Evan Encourages Sam to Control Recurring Flying Dreams and Enjoy Outdoor Activities\n  Content: On January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:28 AM, Evan encouraged Sam by suggesting that with a little more practice, Sam might learn to control his recurring flying dreams and asked Sam to update him once he mastered it. Evan wished Sam enjoyment of the fresh air and scenic views during his beach walks. Sam thanked Evan and expressed his intention to make the most of the outdoor activities, wishing Evan well in return.\n\n\n**Instructions**:\nFollow these steps to ensure an accurate evaluation:\n\n1.  **Deconstruct the Query**: Break down the user\'s query into its core informational needs (e.g., who, what, where, when, why, how). Identify all key entities and concepts.\n2.  **Scan for Keywords**: Quickly scan the documents for the key entities and concepts from the query. This is a preliminary check for relevance.\n3.  **Detailed Analysis**: Read the relevant parts of the documents carefully. Determine if they contain explicit facts that directly answer *all aspects* of the query. Do not rely on making significant inferences or assumptions. The answer should be explicitly stated or very easily pieced together from the text.\n4.  **Sufficiency Judgment**:\n    *   If all parts of the query are directly and explicitly answered, the documents are **sufficient**.\n    *   If any significant part of the query is not answered, the documents are **insufficient**.\n    *   If you are uncertain, err on the side of caution and label it as **insufficient**. Do not guess.\n5.  **Formulate Reasoning**: Based on your analysis, write a brief (1-2 sentences) explanation for your judgment.\n6.  **Identify Missing Information**: If the documents are insufficient, list the specific pieces of information that are missing to fully answer the query.\n\n**Output Format** (strict JSON, no additional text before or after the JSON block):\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true or false,\n  "reasoning": "Brief, clear explanation for your decision (1-2 sentences).",\n  "missing_information": ["list", "of", "specific", "missing", "information"]\n}\n\n**Examples**:\n\nExample 1 (Sufficient):\nQuery: "What is Alice\'s favorite hobby?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Alice mentioned she loves painting. She spends weekends at art galleries."\n  Document 2: "Alice\'s work involves creative projects."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true,\n  "reasoning": "Document 1 explicitly states that Alice\'s hobby is painting.",\n  "missing_information": []\n}\n\nExample 2 (Insufficient - Missing Detail):\nQuery: "Where did Bob go on vacation last year?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Bob talked about his work project deadline around June."\n  Document 2: "Bob likes to travel and explore new places. He recently came back from a trip."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention Bob likes to travel and recently took a trip, but do not specify where he went or if it was last year.",\n  "missing_information": ["specific vacation destination", "confirmation the trip was \'last year\'"]\n}\n\nExample 3 (Insufficient - Tangential Information):\nQuery: "What are the specs of the new \'Galaxy Z\' phone?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "The Galaxy Z is rumored to be released next month."\n  Document 2: "Tech enthusiasts are excited about the upcoming Galaxy Z launch event."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention the phone\'s upcoming release but provide no specific technical specifications.",\n  "missing_information": ["screen size", "processor type", "camera resolution", "battery capacity", "etc."]\n}\n\nNow evaluate:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
