uires about Sam\'s hobbies; Sam shares a feel-good movie image\n  Content: Also at 7:31 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan asked Sam if he had tried any new hobbies recently to help distract from his health issues. Sam replied by sharing an image of a book featuring a picture of a man on its cover, explaining that although he had not tried many new activities lately, he had recently acquired this item the day before (November 20, 2023) and considered it his go-to \'feel good\' movie or flick. This exchange highlighted Sam\'s attempt to find comfort and distraction th...\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Sam Reports Eating Healthier, Evan Describes Dietary Changes and Challenges\n  Content: Also at 3:55 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam mentioned that he was trying to eat healthier these days. Evan complimented the salad Sam shared and explained that he was being extra careful with his health, trying to reduce processed foods and sugary snacks despite his fondness for ginger snaps. Evan asked Sam if he had made any recent dietary changes.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Sam Opens Up About Health Struggles and Weight Challenges; Evan Offers Support and Encouragement\n  Content: On January 11, 2024 (Thursday) at 9:37 PM, Sam reached out to Evan after a few days without contact, expressing concern about his health issues that had made life difficult. Sam described feeling weighed down by his health problems, which hindered his ability to fully live, but he was trying to stay positive despite the challenges. Evan responded empathetically, acknowledging the difficulty of health interfering with life and commended Sam\'s positivity while reminding him to take care of himself...\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Evan Shares Heart Palpitation Health Scare, Sam Responds with Healthy Meal Photo\n  Content: On June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 3:55 PM, Evan reached out to Sam after a period of no contact, sharing that life had been a rollercoaster lately. Evan disclosed a recent health scare involving a sudden heart palpitation incident the previous week (around May 30, 2023), which served as a serious wake-up call about his lifestyle. Sam responded with a photo of a plate of vegetables and a glass of milk, expressing gladness that Evan was feeling better.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Sam admits struggle with cravings despite efforts to maintain healthy diet\n  Content: On September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:29 AM, Sam thanked Evan for his support and described managing his health journey as somewhat wild. Sam admitted that although he was trying to make healthier choices, he still experienced occasional cravings for sugary drinks and snacks, which he found to be a real struggle.\n\nDocument 8:\n  Title: Sam confides in Evan about health risks from weight and emotional struggle\n  Content: On October 8, 2023 (Sunday) at 03:09 PM, Sam reached out to Evan to share a personal concern. Sam revealed that during a medical check-up the previous Monday (October 2, 2023), his doctor had warned that his weight posed a serious health risk and that without changes, the situation could worsen. Although Sam had previously joked about his weight, the news was now hitting him hard, and he admitted to having a difficult time coping.\n\nDocument 9:\n  Title: Sam shares photo of fruit and yogurt bowls; discusses Weight Watchers meeting insights\n  Content: At 8:18 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared an image showing a variety of bowls filled with fruit and yogurt. Sam related this to his recent attendance at a Weight Watchers meeting the day before (December 4, 2023), where he had learned valuable tips. This indicated Sam’s ongoing efforts to improve his diet and health.\n\nDocument 10:\n  Title: Evan and Sam Reconnect After Time Apart, Share Life Updates\n  Content: On December 17, 2023 (Sunday) at 6:48 PM, Evan reached out to Sam, greeting him and noting it had been a long time since they last spoke. Evan mentioned that a lot had happened recently. Sam responded that he was doing okay but had experienced some difficulties or \'bumps\' in life.\n\n\n**Instructions**:\nFollow these steps to ensure an accurate evaluation:\n\n1.  **Deconstruct the Query**: Break down the user\'s query into its core informational needs (e.g., who, what, where, when, why, how). Identify all key entities and concepts.\n2.  **Scan for Keywords**: Quickly scan the documents for the key entities and concepts from the query. This is a preliminary check for relevance.\n3.  **Detailed Analysis**: Read the relevant parts of the documents carefully. Determine if they contain explicit facts that directly answer *all aspects* of the query. Do not rely on making significant inferences or assumptions. The answer should be explicitly stated or very easily pieced together from the text.\n4.  **Sufficiency Judgment**:\n    *   If all parts of the query are directly and explicitly answered, the documents are **sufficient**.\n    *   If any significant part of the query is not answered, the documents are **insufficient**.\n    *   If you are uncertain, err on the side of caution and label it as **insufficient**. Do not guess.\n5.  **Formulate Reasoning**: Based on your analysis, write a brief (1-2 sentences) explanation for your judgment.\n6.  **Identify Missing Information**: If the documents are insufficient, list the specific pieces of information that are missing to fully answer the query.\n\n**Output Format** (strict JSON, no additional text before or after the JSON block):\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true or false,\n  "reasoning": "Brief, clear explanation for your decision (1-2 sentences).",\n  "missing_information": ["list", "of", "specific", "missing", "information"]\n}\n\n**Examples**:\n\nExample 1 (Sufficient):\nQuery: "What is Alice\'s favorite hobby?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Alice mentioned she loves painting. She spends weekends at art galleries."\n  Document 2: "Alice\'s work involves creative projects."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true,\n  "reasoning": "Document 1 explicitly states that Alice\'s hobby is painting.",\n  "missing_information": []\n}\n\nExample 2 (Insufficient - Missing Detail):\nQuery: "Where did Bob go on vacation last year?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Bob talked about his work project deadline around June."\n  Document 2: "Bob likes to travel and explore new places. He recently came back from a trip."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention Bob likes to travel and recently took a trip, but do not specify where he went or if it was last year.",\n  "missing_information": ["specific vacation destination", "confirmation the trip was \'last year\'"]\n}\n\nExample 3 (Insufficient - Tangential Information):\nQuery: "What are the specs of the new \'Galaxy Z\' phone?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "The Galaxy Z is rumored to be released next month."\n  Document 2: "Tech enthusiasts are excited about the upcoming Galaxy Z launch event."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention the phone\'s upcoming release but provide no specific technical specifications.",\n  "missing_information": ["screen size", "processor type", "camera resolution", "battery capacity", "etc."]\n}\n\nNow evaluate:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
