lp in new endeavors\n  Content: At 8:21 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed that Sam’s support had been invaluable during his attempts to try new things like yoga. Sam replied that everyone needs help when starting new activities and that having support is important. Evan agreed, noting that knowing he was not alone made a big difference. Sam encouraged Evan to keep him updated on how yoga went and said goodbye. Evan reciprocated the farewell, thanking Sam and promising to talk soon. This exchange highlighted thei...\n\nDocument 4:\n  Title: Evan compliments smoothie bowl; inquires about yoga for stress relief and flexibility\n  Content: At 8:19 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan complimented the smoothie bowl Sam had shared and asked how the Weight Watchers meeting had gone. Evan also mentioned that he had been considering trying yoga as a gentle yet effective way to relieve stress and improve flexibility. He asked Sam for his opinion on yoga, seeking advice based on Sam’s experience.\n\nDocument 5:\n  Title: Evan Endorses Yoga for Stress Relief and Flexibility; Sam Hopes for Positive Changes with Diet and Yoga\n  Content: On January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:26 AM, Evan emphasized that yoga was a great starting point for Sam, sharing that yoga had helped him manage stress and maintain flexibility, which complemented a healthy diet well. Evan also acknowledged The Godfather as a legendary film worth multiple viewings. Sam expressed hope that combining a healthier diet with yoga would lead to positive changes in his well-being.\n\nDocument 6:\n  Title: Evan Shares Beach Sunset Photo as Low-Impact Exercise Suggestion; Sam Plans Beach Walks and Recurring Flying Dream\n  Content: At 12:27 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan shared a photo of a woman standing on a beach at sunset, suggesting that there are many enjoyable low-impact exercises beyond yoga, including beach walks. Evan described beach sunsets as both good exercise and calming experiences. Sam responded that the image looked zen and said he planned to try beach walks based on Evan\'s recommendation. Sam also shared that he had a recurring dream of flying over skyscrapers, which he wanted to brag about.\n\nDocument 7:\n  Title: Evan Encourages Sam to Start Workouts and Offers Exercise Guidance\n  Content: On June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:01 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man with a beard holding a dumbbell to Sam, expressing his enthusiasm and support for their workout goals. Evan emphasized that exercise clears the mind and encouraged Sam to join him in reaching their fitness objectives. Sam responded positively, expressing excitement and requesting help to get started with exercising. Evan gladly offered to meet with Sam to demonstrate some basic exercises, reinforcing their shared commitment ...\n\nDocument 8:\n  Title: Evan Offers to Help Sam Find Kayaking Spots; Sam Plans Immediate Kayaking with Friend\n  Content: At 4:11 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan reassured Sam that kayaking was a fun way to exercise and enjoy nature. Evan offered to help Sam by recommending a good kayaking spot when Sam was ready to try it. Sam responded by thanking Evan for the idea and shared that he and his mate were just around the corner from a lake where they planned to try kayaking immediately, demonstrating prompt action on Evan\'s suggestion.\n\nDocument 9:\n  Title: Sam advises low-impact exercises for Evan\'s knee; Evan swims and awaits PT\n  Content: On August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:20 AM, Sam reflected on life\'s unpredictability and emphasized the importance of adaptability and finding alternative ways to stay active when facing obstacles. Sam suggested Evan consider low-impact exercises or physical therapy for his knee. Sam also expressed interest in the book Evan mentioned. Evan confirmed that physical therapy was planned and hoped to get an appointment soon. Meanwhile, Evan was keeping activity low-key by swimming, which he found suitab...\n\nDocument 10:\n  Title: Evan Encourages Sam to Start Exercising and Plans a Hike Together\n  Content: On October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\n\n**Instructions**:\nFollow these steps to ensure an accurate evaluation:\n\n1.  **Deconstruct the Query**: Break down the user\'s query into its core informational needs (e.g., who, what, where, when, why, how). Identify all key entities and concepts.\n2.  **Scan for Keywords**: Quickly scan the documents for the key entities and concepts from the query. This is a preliminary check for relevance.\n3.  **Detailed Analysis**: Read the relevant parts of the documents carefully. Determine if they contain explicit facts that directly answer *all aspects* of the query. Do not rely on making significant inferences or assumptions. The answer should be explicitly stated or very easily pieced together from the text.\n4.  **Sufficiency Judgment**:\n    *   If all parts of the query are directly and explicitly answered, the documents are **sufficient**.\n    *   If any significant part of the query is not answered, the documents are **insufficient**.\n    *   If you are uncertain, err on the side of caution and label it as **insufficient**. Do not guess.\n5.  **Formulate Reasoning**: Based on your analysis, write a brief (1-2 sentences) explanation for your judgment.\n6.  **Identify Missing Information**: If the documents are insufficient, list the specific pieces of information that are missing to fully answer the query.\n\n**Output Format** (strict JSON, no additional text before or after the JSON block):\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true or false,\n  "reasoning": "Brief, clear explanation for your decision (1-2 sentences).",\n  "missing_information": ["list", "of", "specific", "missing", "information"]\n}\n\n**Examples**:\n\nExample 1 (Sufficient):\nQuery: "What is Alice\'s favorite hobby?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Alice mentioned she loves painting. She spends weekends at art galleries."\n  Document 2: "Alice\'s work involves creative projects."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": true,\n  "reasoning": "Document 1 explicitly states that Alice\'s hobby is painting.",\n  "missing_information": []\n}\n\nExample 2 (Insufficient - Missing Detail):\nQuery: "Where did Bob go on vacation last year?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "Bob talked about his work project deadline around June."\n  Document 2: "Bob likes to travel and explore new places. He recently came back from a trip."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention Bob likes to travel and recently took a trip, but do not specify where he went or if it was last year.",\n  "missing_information": ["specific vacation destination", "confirmation the trip was \'last year\'"]\n}\n\nExample 3 (Insufficient - Tangential Information):\nQuery: "What are the specs of the new \'Galaxy Z\' phone?"\nDocuments:\n  Document 1: "The Galaxy Z is rumored to be released next month."\n  Document 2: "Tech enthusiasts are excited about the upcoming Galaxy Z launch event."\nOutput:\n{\n  "is_sufficient": false,\n  "reasoning": "The documents mention the phone\'s upcoming release but provide no specific technical specifications.",\n  "missing_information": ["screen size", "processor type", "camera resolution", "battery capacity", "etc."]\n}\n\nNow evaluate:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 500, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0.0}}
