e scenery. Sam mentioned that the photo was taken last week (January 4-10, 2024) in the countryside.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 556c1043-b67c-43dd-b478-d3258e2f7346, Score: 0.0414)\nAt 4:35 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), immediately following their previous conversation, Sam suggested to Evan that he should put a GPS sensor on his keys to prevent losing them. Evan agreed that it was a great idea and planned to do so as soon as he found his keys.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: d21f8c82-92c9-413f-9737-3726ec2fab9b, Score: 0.0398)\nAt 06:29 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Sam expressed interest in Evan\'s road trips and asked if he had visited any fun places during those rides. Evan shared a photo of a person skiing on a snowy trail and said that last month he had driven somewhere fun with amazing views. Sam asked if Evan took advantage of skiing opportunities in Banff, suggesting it sounded like a lot of fun. Evan shared an image of a group skiing down a snow-covered slope and confirmed that the trip was great for skiing, with amazing snow and lots of fun. Evan expressed excitement about returning next year and asked Sam if he had tried any winter sports.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: e90206a4-4f5d-4515-b6bd-98f884055000, Score: 0.0395)\nAlso at 7:54 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam observed that Evan’s children appeared to be having a great time and inquired about how long Evan had been prioritizing his health. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a box containing a fitness watch and explained that his health journey has been ongoing for two years. He acknowledged that the process has had ups and downs but affirmed that he is doing his best to maintain his health.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: e6d879da-9c1c-410c-89a3-a53b6a31cb8d, Score: 0.0278)\nAt 4:15 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Evan encouraged Sam to keep up the good work, cheering for him. Evan then humorously shared that he had been searching for his keys for the last half hour with no luck and joked about losing it every week.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 6748eefd-6bef-42c0-875e-2a14b0857f45, Score: 0.0275)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:17 PM, Evan explained that the guitar was a 1968 Kustom K-200A vintage model, gifted by a close friend. Evan disclosed that he had been going through a tough time since they last spoke, revealing that he lost his job the previous month (October 2023), which had been difficult. He expressed appreciation for Sam\'s support during this period.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: d5160beb-19f4-40ee-b11d-28e4992c8a17, Score: 0.0274)\nOn December 26, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:34 PM, Sam shared with Evan that he occasionally sketches but had not yet created anything remarkable. Sam expressed optimism that he would soon have something to show off and found Evan\'s passion for sketching inspiring. Evan appreciated Sam\'s encouragement and offered to help him get started whenever he wanted. During this exchange, Evan also mentioned that he had lost his keys again, noting that it had become a weekly ritual for him to misplace them.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 5ba08f8a-6a8d-4efb-a3e0-0b870dba01bb, Score: 0.0260)\nAt 4:02 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam told Evan that he was excited about starting workouts but shared a recent frustrating experience at the supermarket. Sam explained that all the self-checkout machines were broken when he tried to shop, which negatively affected his mood. This incident occurred just before their conversation, as Sam mentioned he was coming from the shop.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: 3a15043c-800c-4b95-8b28-2ce769af8cf1, Score: 0.0250)\nOn May 24, 2023 (Wednesday) at 7:11 PM, Evan reached out to Sam, sharing that since their last conversation, much had happened. Evan described a recent family road trip to Jasper the previous weekend (May 20-21, 2023), highlighting the drive along the Icefields Parkway and the stunning glaciers and lakes they saw. Evan shared a photo of a glacier taken during the trip. Sam responded with enthusiasm, noting that he had never been to Jasper but found th