ories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 3bbfcf17-9c00-4391-ac45-62367610a79e, Score: 0.0479)\nAlso at 06:22 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan revealed to Sam that he had recently started taking painting classes a few days prior and was really enjoying the experience. He framed this as part of trying new things. Sam asked why Evan, who was already good at drawing, decided to join a painting class and inquired about how Evan originally started painting years ago. Evan shared an image of a painting of a forest scene on an easel and explained that a friend had given him that painting, which inspired him to start painting. He joined the classes to meet like-minded people and showcase his skills, believing that one can always improve. Sam complimented Evan\'s talent and asked if he had taken any other classes. Evan shared another image showing a brush, pencil, and eyeliners on a cloth, stating that he had only been painting with those tools so far but might explore other classes in the future. Evan described painting as a way to find peace and express himself.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: ce007fdd-7b7e-43b2-8974-3a3dc27aa55c, Score: 0.0463)\nAlso at 08:57 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam inquired if Evan had picked up any new hobbies. Evan replied by sharing a photograph showing a person with a cast on their leg, explaining that he had injured his knee playing basketball with his children the previous week (last week, September 29, 2023). Evan described the injury as a setback that made staying active difficult. He expressed missing outdoor adventures they had enjoyed with family the previous year, calling those times \'good times with the family.\'\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: e6eb97c3-ed81-4f29-883a-b23c49dd855f, Score: 0.0456)\nAt 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam expressed gladness that physical therapy was helping Evan and emphasized the importance of self-care. Sam asked if Evan had tried any enjoyable indoor activities or hobbies. Evan replied that he had been practicing his favorite hobby, watercolor painting, which he found to be a relaxing and engaging way to pass the time and enjoy colors.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: b71becd8-26a3-48ca-8ee0-b13a8a378c2a, Score: 0.0402)\nAt 4:10 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan proposed kayaking as a fun and active outdoor hobby, describing it as paddling on a river or lake. Evan asked Sam for his thoughts on kayaking. Sam replied that kayaking sounded awesome and admitted he had not tried it yet but believed it would be a fun way to exercise and enjoy nature. Sam expressed definite interest in giving kayaking a try and thanked Evan for the suggestion.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: e4345cdb-f400-4807-88d8-778b2e81e466, Score: 0.0303)\nAt 10:53 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared an image of a set of five cards with the words "let it shine," including a photo of his gym membership card, symbolizing his commitment to health. He revealed that he had struggled with his health a few years ago but persevered. Evan emphasized that exercise alone is not enough; diet and lifestyle changes are also crucial. Sam responded enthusiastically, asking Evan what had the biggest impact on his health journey.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: fe099c8e-8a71-4b93-a130-bde4a21419a6, Score: 0.0301)\nAlso at 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam mentioned that he had been looking for a hobby to stay motivated and was thinking about trying painting. Sam asked Evan if painting would help him de-stress. Evan affirmed that painting was a great way to relieve stress and be creative, allowing freedom to explore colors, textures, and express feelings. Evan shared that he had been painting for a few years and found it peaceful. However, Evan clarified that painting alone would not address Sam\'s weight concerns and recommended exercise as an additional necessary component.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: fec7ac28-e6ad-472a-8b38-dbf112117136, Score: 0.0301)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:59 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man sitting at a table filled with fruits and vegetables, illustrating his own health journey. He explained to Sam that about two years ago, he went through a similar phase where he changed his diet and started walking regularly. Sam complimented Evan on his appearance and asked how he managed the change. Evan responded that he shifted his focus to overall well-being rather than quick results, which relieved pressure and made a significant difference.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 5ad7a773-04eb-47e2-bc8b-bf4d73ad2308, Score: 0.0299)\nOn August 13, 2023 (Sunday) at 4:09 PM, Evan shared a photo of a tent pitched in a grassy field and greeted Sam, noting it had been a long time since they last talked. Evan mentioned returning from a vacation in Canada with his new significant other, where they enjoyed activities like hiking and biking while exploring the outdoors together. Sam responded enthusiastically, saying Canada sounded amazing and complimented the stunning photo. However, Sam also shared that things had been challenging lately, particularly with health issues.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 816b1c3e-762a-4816-a424-836783262dc5, Score: 0.0297)\nAlso at 03:09 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan responded by sharing a photo of himself performing a squat on a gym machine. He acknowledged that health challenges could be discouraging. Evan described how he had started lifting weights one year ago and found it to be a challenging but rewarding journey, noting visible progress. Evan offered to support Sam if he was interested in trying weightlifting.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: bbc400c1-5c37-4518-93cb-f9df7fa780c3, Score: 0.0284)\nAlso at 7:31 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan asked Sam if he had tried any new hobbies recently to help distract from his health issues. Sam replied by sharing an image of a book featuring a picture of a man on its cover, explaining that although he had not tried many new activities lately, he had recently acquired this item the day before (November 20, 2023) and considered it his go-to \'feel good\' movie or flick. This exchange highlighted Sam\'s attempt to find comfort and distraction through media.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: e90206a4-4f5d-4515-b6bd-98f884055000, Score: 0.0278)\nAlso at 7:54 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam observed that Evan’s children appeared to be having a great time and inquired about how long Evan had been prioritizing his health. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a box containing a fitness watch and explained that his health journey has been ongoing for two years. He acknowledged that the process has had ups and downs but affirmed that he is doing his best to maintain his health.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 6dfd531c-eb84-4b2b-a205-da0bb919f30f, Score: 0.0273)\nAlso at 1:55 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan encouraged Sam by saying that he would find a hobby he loved by continuing to try new things until something sparked his excitement.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 67c15a5b-428c-4818-b777-1764dfec2e04, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 1:54 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed admiration for Evan\'s painting skills and asked how Evan got into watercolor painting. Evan explained that a friend introduced him to the hobby and gave him advice, which led to him becoming hooked immediately.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 30439981-753e-4487-ac8b-9b49a4beeaa1, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 1:56 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam thanked Evan and expressed excitement about trying new hobbies, anticipating fun experiences. Evan reciprocated enthusiasm and suggested they catch up soon to discuss how Sam was enjoying his new hobbies. Sam agreed to keep Evan posted, and they exchanged friendly goodbyes, looking forward to their next meeting.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: bdee660c-22f1-43bd-b80e-86700d293907, Score: 0.0264)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:18 AM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had started a new diet and exercise routine the previous Monday (August 21, 2023) and that it had made a huge difference, making him feel great. Sam asked Evan about any recent changes in his life. Evan responded that he was glad Sam\'s new routine was going well but shared that he had twisted his knee the previous Friday (August 25, 2023), causing significant pain and making it difficult to maintain his usual fitness routine. Evan expressed frustration because staying active was very important to him.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: e7bf3bf4-7e97-4075-a048-bbfc1e48bfaa, Score: 0.0262)\nAt 1:52 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam shared a photo of a person holding a paint set in a store and mentioned that he had not yet found a hobby but was thinking about trying painting. Sam asked Evan if he had any hobbies he loved, indicating openness to exploring creative activities.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: d0b268a6-9def-4568-ab22-727528a3db77, Score: 0.0258)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What hobby did Evan start practicing a few years ago that he enjoys?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
