k to Evan, asking how he was doing following his health scare. Evan responded positively, stating that he was doing well and that doctors had confirmed everything was fine. He reflected that the experience taught him the value of life. Evan also commented on the movie Sam had mentioned, expressing interest in it. This moment underscored Evan\'s recovery and his renewed appreciation for life.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 55667a3b-6b84-4080-bce7-bb77204d1878, Score: 0.0277)\nAt 4:29 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam admitted that he had not experienced love in the same way but had started enjoying running in the mornings as a way to clear his head. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a painting with a white background featuring blue, orange, and black colors. He acknowledged Sam’s approach to life, emphasizing the importance of finding what works for oneself. Evan encouraged Sam to keep trying new things, suggesting that he might find his own version of love in unexpected places and urged him to embrace the journey, which is full of surprises.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: fb253bfa-ac7c-4a08-8270-64b0ac364cdc, Score: 0.0274)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 1:50 PM, Sam reached out to Evan, expressing that he had been missing their chats. Sam revealed that he had experienced a significant health scare the previous weekend (last weekend, October 7-8, 2023), which resulted in an emergency room visit due to a severe stomachache. The diagnosis was gastritis, which alarmed Sam and served as a wake-up call to prioritize his health. Sam mentioned plans to adopt a more nutritious diet and engage in regular exercise. Additionally, Sam shared that his phone had been malfunctioning, adding to his stress. Evan responded with sympathy, acknowledging that gastritis can be tough and emphasizing the importance of taking care of oneself.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: 0ccff4bb-a2bc-4b28-a992-a191593013ed, Score: 0.0267)\nAt 12:17 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan reached out to Sam, hoping he was doing well and mentioning that something funny had happened the previous night (January 9, 2024). Sam responded promptly, asking Evan what had happened and inviting him to share the story.\n\n[Memory 19] (ID: 9e7e3ee2-ec8c-4a3d-885c-0308f3593c85, Score: 0.0265)\nOn August 15, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:20 PM, Evan shared a photo of a person with a cast on their foot and updated Sam that it had been a few days since they last talked. Evan explained that life had been tough lately because his son had a soccer accident the previous Saturday (August 12, 2023) and hurt his ankle. Evan described how difficult it was to see his son hurt and that he had been looking after him and taking him to the doctor. Evan reflected on the challenges of being a dad watching his child go through pain. Sam expressed sympathy and said he could imagine how hard it must have been for Evan. Sam also shared that things had not been easy for himself either, mentioning a tough week and a doctor\'s appointment that served as a wake-up call to take better care of his own health.\n\n[Memory 20] (ID: f10e33e6-d0cf-479d-94b7-94ec4184d702, Score: 0.0262)\nAt 12:20 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan recounted that he was very embarrassed when he saw the consequences the next morning. He apologized to the affected parties, who were understanding. Evan acknowledged that he had been out of control and resolved to be more careful in the future. Sam expressed relief that the others were understanding and reminded Evan that everyone makes mistakes because they are human.\n\n\n\nQuestion: When did Evan have his sudden heart palpitation incident that really shocked him up?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
