eached out to Evan after a long time, asking how he was doing and hoping all was well. Evan responded that life had been a wild ride lately. He shared that the previous week (November 14-20, 2023), he experienced a health scare that required a hospital visit. During a check-up, something suspicious was found, which frightened Evan. Fortunately, it turned out to be a misunderstanding. This experience made Evan realize the importance of monitoring his health closely.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 9f474de9-fcbe-453e-8d28-a2fdf0db7089, Score: 0.0303)\nAt 7:14 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Evan acknowledged the challenge Sam faced confronting his health issues and reminded Sam that it was never too late to make positive lifestyle changes. Evan offered support for Sam\'s journey toward better health. Sam thanked Evan and asked for tips on how to start breaking old habits.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 46987ff9-f47e-46e6-b9e1-e0ed29f69dc9, Score: 0.0287)\nOn January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:26 AM, Evan emphasized that yoga was a great starting point for Sam, sharing that yoga had helped him manage stress and maintain flexibility, which complemented a healthy diet well. Evan also acknowledged The Godfather as a legendary film worth multiple viewings. Sam expressed hope that combining a healthier diet with yoga would lead to positive changes in his well-being.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 4eca99f1-707e-4890-87d0-d4df8e66d867, Score: 0.0285)\nAt 7:36 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam noticed Evan seemed to be having a good time and asked what Evan did to stay fit and healthy. Evan recounted that he maintained his fitness by regularly going to the gym and also enjoyed taking his car out for a spin, activities that helped him stay active and engaged. This conversation revealed Evan\'s active lifestyle habits.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 816b1c3e-762a-4816-a424-836783262dc5, Score: 0.0283)\nAlso at 03:09 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan responded by sharing a photo of himself performing a squat on a gym machine. He acknowledged that health challenges could be discouraging. Evan described how he had started lifting weights one year ago and found it to be a challenging but rewarding journey, noting visible progress. Evan offered to support Sam if he was interested in trying weightlifting.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: f0d0bcd1-cee7-4e28-983f-12468d7701e4, Score: 0.0281)\nAt 4:24 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam expressed relief that Evan\'s son\'s ankle was improving and acknowledged how hard it is to see loved ones hurt. Sam reminded Evan to look after himself as well, emphasizing the importance of health care. Evan agreed that taking care of themselves was a must and asked Sam how he had been feeling lately.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: bdee660c-22f1-43bd-b80e-86700d293907, Score: 0.0280)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:18 AM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had started a new diet and exercise routine the previous Monday (August 21, 2023) and that it had made a huge difference, making him feel great. Sam asked Evan about any recent changes in his life. Evan responded that he was glad Sam\'s new routine was going well but shared that he had twisted his knee the previous Friday (August 25, 2023), causing significant pain and making it difficult to maintain his usual fitness routine. Evan expressed frustration because staying active was very important to him.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 7b30517b-25f8-4783-9260-be5af49f4813, Score: 0.0280)\nOn September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:29 AM, Sam thanked Evan for his support and described managing his health journey as somewhat wild. Sam admitted that although he was trying to make healthier choices, he still experienced occasional cravings for sugary drinks and snacks, which he found to be a real struggle.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: f9d563bd-299f-4858-92ee-0e593305e984, Score: 0.0277)\nAt 1:51 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam thanked Evan for sharing his positive experience with fitness and expressed a desire to start exercising himself. Sam admitted that getting started was hard and asked Evan for any tips on staying motivated, indicating a readiness to improve his health following his recent scare.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: 938c817f-8fb8-466b-bf22-b443f0cf8113, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 10:57 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photograph of a book with a green apple beside it, symbolizing health and knowledge. He encouraged Sam to concentrate on making healthy swaps and taking small, manageable steps toward better health, advising Sam to stay positive and upbeat throughout the process.\n\n[Memory 19] (ID: ac0ad99d-4757-4b7a-9a82-624ed8b6db28, Score: 0.0270)\nAt 10:54 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a table full of fresh produce and vegetables to illustrate the dietary changes he made, such as reducing sugary snacks and increasing his intake of fruits and vegetables. He explained that these changes significantly improved his health and asked Sam if he had considered making any dietary adjustments.\n\n[Memory 20] (ID: e6eb97c3-ed81-4f29-883a-b23c49dd855f, Score: 0.0269)\nAt 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam expressed gladness that physical therapy was helping Evan and emphasized the importance of self-care. Sam asked if Evan had tried any enjoyable indoor activities or hobbies. Evan replied that he had been practicing his favorite hobby, watercolor painting, which he found to be a relaxing and engaging way to pass the time and enjoy colors.\n\n\n\nQuestion: Which year did Evan start taking care of his health seriously?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
