ble friends and reaffirmed that they had each other. This exchange underscored the value they placed on friendship and mutual reliance.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: fb55dac6-4f62-4037-b70f-ac4a8828c27d, Score: 0.0325)\nOn September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:31 AM, Sam complimented Evan on an impressive painting Evan had created. Sam acknowledged Evan\'s success in finding painting as a way to de-stress and expressed interest in exploring a calming hobby himself, considering painting as a potential option to help manage stress.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: b896592a-e8bc-458f-9255-32a41e58c555, Score: 0.0303)\nAlso at 09:03 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Evan asked Sam if he had other ways of expressing himself. Sam replied that he enjoyed drawing, though he was still learning, and primarily expressed himself through writing. Sam described writing as therapeutic and helpful for sorting out his feelings.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 5ecd42f2-a4ee-48c3-92f6-ca156967e30a, Score: 0.0303)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:18 PM, Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s job loss and asked what had happened. Evan explained that the company downsized, and he was part of that reduction. He was currently searching for a new job, which was challenging, but he remained hopeful and kept his spirits up. Sam acknowledged the difficulty of sudden job loss and praised Evan for handling it well. Sam offered to be there for Evan to talk or help in any way and expressed confidence that Evan would get through this. Evan thanked Sam for the support, emphasizing how much it meant to have someone to talk to, and promised to reach out if needed. Sam reiterated his availability and encouraged Evan to stay positive, affirming that life can be tough but they could get through it together.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 49270e99-17e1-43e4-8426-e87231ec757a, Score: 0.0302)\nOn January 11, 2024 (Thursday) at 9:37 PM, Sam reached out to Evan after a few days without contact, expressing concern about his health issues that had made life difficu