2025-12-18 01:59:11,773 - [answer-locomo_8_qa53] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-6b8d6c0f-a334-42fd-93db-89915a0ef453', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: faf07d42-cb24-49d4-9e8a-eecc3c7f302e, Score: 0.0489)\nAlso at 09:34 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Sam agreed with Evan\'s plan and expressed excitement about painting together next Saturday, anticipating it to be an enjoyable and creative experience.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: 5c081850-4570-445d-83a6-8c7383c0d4b5, Score: 0.0464)\nAt 09:32 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan responded to Sam\'s interest by describing painting as a very relaxing activity. Evan offered to assist Sam in getting started with painting, including recommending supplies, and invited Sam to let him know if he wanted to proceed.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 3bbfcf17-9c00-4391-ac45-62367610a79e, Score: 0.0461)\nAlso at 06:22 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan revealed to Sam that he had recently started taking painting classes a few days prior and was really enjoying the experience. He framed this as part of trying new things. Sam asked why Evan, who was already good at drawing, decided to join a painting class and inquired about how Evan originally started painting years ago. Evan shared an image of a painting of a forest scene on an easel and explained that a friend had given him that painting, which inspired him to start painting. He joined the classes to meet like-minded people and showcase his skills, believing that one can always improve. Sam complimented Evan\'s talent and asked if he had taken any other classes. Evan shared another image showing a brush, pencil, and eyeliners on a cloth, stating that he had only been painting with those tools so far but might explore other classes in the future. Evan described painting as a way to find peace and express himself.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 87e3e4f8-40ac-4095-87d1-f4f9173fbc3d, Score: 0.0457)\nAlso at 1:52 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan responded positively to Sam\'s idea of painting, calling it a cool idea and asking if Sam had tried painting before, showing encouragement and curiosity about Sam\'s experience.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 890041ae-cd7d-4f16-936b-60fbe7a633f2, Score: 0.0447)\nAt 09:02 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam praised Evan\'s artwork and inquired how Evan decided what to paint. Evan explained that he usually paints whatever is on his mind or reflects his feelings. His subjects often include good memories or places he wishes to visit. Evan described painting as a form of self-expression through art.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 6d9f8dc4-a216-410c-8035-a4831c81491d, Score: 0.0440)\nAt 7:16 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam thanked Evan for the encouragement and committed to trying painting, promising to update Evan on how it went. Evan responded enthusiastically, advising Sam to have fun and not put too much pressure on himself. Sam agreed to enjoy the process without stress. Evan encouraged Sam to keep him updated, and Sam promised to do so before they exchanged goodbyes.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 9a95ee80-36aa-4862-9093-bada86c9d53f, Score: 0.0437)\nAt 4:32 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam asked Evan about the emotions that inspired the painting he had shared. Evan explained that he painted it with a sense of joy and freedom. He described the spontaneous brush strokes and bold colors as reflecting a playful and liberated mood, embracing the creative process without restraint.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: ca8ab68c-b566-4585-aacd-6258fa0eab42, Score: 0.0433)\nOn September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:28 AM, Evan reached out to Sam after a long period without communication. Evan shared an image of a painting depicting a sunset over a body of water and asked Sam what he had been doing over the past few weeks.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: fb55dac6-4f62-4037-b70f-ac4a8828c27d, Score: 0.0429)\nOn September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:31 AM, Sam complimented Evan on an impressive painting Evan had created. Sam acknowledged Evan\'s success in finding painting as a way to de-stress and expressed interest in exploring a calming hobby himself, considering painting as a potential option to help manage stress.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: fffbb261-d314-4f84-a148-bbbb038897a7, Score: 0.0406)\nAlso at 4:07 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Sam complimented Evan\'s painting, calling it awesome and inquiring if Evan had painted it himself. Evan responded with sympathy for Sam\'s rough week and reassured him not to worry about the snacks. Evan shared that he was doing okay and had just finished painting a sunset, which helped him relax, indicating that painting was a therapeutic activity for Evan.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 82d2f461-2731-4913-aa4a-58c63107b2af, Score: 0.0404)\nAt 1:55 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed hope that he could find a hobby he was as passionate about as Evan was with watercolor painting, showing inspiration from Evan\'s enthusiasm.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 67c15a5b-428c-4818-b777-1764dfec2e04, Score: 0.0403)\nAt 1:54 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed admiration for Evan\'s painting skills and asked how Evan got into watercolor painting. Evan explained that a friend introduced him to the hobby and gave him advice, which led to him becoming hooked immediately.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: f9a77bf0-907a-4228-8792-7ef172220214, Score: 0.0299)\nAt 09:33 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Sam responded positively to Evan\'s offer, asking for help in choosing painting supplies. Sam also expressed excitement about planning a painting session soon.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 44e0766f-5809-4cb3-8704-e1d90069fcea, Score: 0.0284)\nAt 09:33 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan enthusiastically confirmed that painting is an excellent hobby. He advised Sam to acquire acrylic paints, brushes, a canvas or paper, and a palette for mixing colors. Evan also offered to provide specific product recommendations and suggested planning a painting session once Sam was ready.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 550ea07c-3c8f-46eb-bb42-415cc47c2622, Score: 0.0279)\nAt 4:30 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam admired the minimalistic and stunning nature of Evan’s painting and wondered about the inspiration behind it. Evan revealed that he had created the painting during a time when he was experiencing a mix of emotions including sadness, anger, and hopefulness. He reflected on how art can portray feelings without words. Sam expressed fascination with how art can express emotions so effectively.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: ae13ff3d-57d7-4546-a729-b3998a7587e5, Score: 0.0274)\nAt 4:33 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a photo of a woman holding flowers in front of her face, describing it as amazing and praising Evan’s serious talent and creativity. Sam noted that creating such a painting must have been very satisfying. Evan thanked Sam for the compliment and commented that the painting Sam shared had an inspiring vibe. Evan then asked Sam how long he had been painting.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 803fac33-3d15-45db-8b19-f3aa0288b4a5, Score: 0.0274)\nAt 09:00 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam asked Evan about the progress of his watercolor painting. Evan shared a photo of a painting depicting a cactus in the desert, stating that painting had been going well and served as an effective stress reliever. He mentioned that the painting was completed the previous week (last week, September 29, 2023).\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: e382ac6b-6b22-4a92-a29f-a7712aebfb5c, Score: 0.0271)\nAt 09:03 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam acknowledged the power of expressing oneself through art and complimented Evan\'s approach. Evan agreed, emphasizing that painting is a great way to communicate emotions and thoughts without using words.\n\n[Memory 19] (ID: f45cac51-9b54-4a53-a73d-6194eda02ca4, Score: 0.0270)\nAt 6:55 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Sam complimented Evan’s painting and asked who the girl standing next to it was. Evan explained that she was a close friend who had helped him get the painting published in an exhibition.\n\n[Memory 20] (ID: d71ab2d1-2916-4cec-99f8-5bbbe951444b, Score: 0.0256)\nOn October 14, 2023 (Saturday) at 4:07 PM, Evan reinitiated contact with Sam by sharing a photograph of a painting depicting a person standing on a cliff. Evan asked Sam how he was doing, noting it had been a while since they last talked and expressing hope that all was well. Sam replied with a photo of a person holding a box of sodas in front of a wall, admitting that he had experienced a rough week. Sam confessed that he gave in and bought some unhealthy snacks, which made him feel guilty.\n\n\n\nQuestion: When did Evan and Sam decide to paint together?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
