 on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan asked Sam if he was ready for an adventure and inquired about the destination of the kayaking trip. Sam replied that they were traveling through Lake Tahoe, mentioning that he had heard it was a great place for kayaking, indicating anticipation for the experience.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: a3d4c150-cd8f-493d-be3f-f56cf2172565, Score: 0.0466)\nAt 4:12 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan expressed enthusiasm about planning a kayaking trip together and promised to pick a cool spot. Sam shared a photograph showing a row of kayaks lined up on the shore of a river, confirming his excitement and readiness for the activity. Sam thanked Evan for his help and looked forward to the planned kayaking adventure.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 8ca960fd-da8f-4834-b7b4-ceb964c74840, Score: 0.0464)\nAt 4:14 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan complimented Sam\'s choice of Lake Tahoe for kayaking, describing it as an awesome pick with clear water and gorgeous views. Evan encouraged Sam to have a blast and to take lots of pictures. Sam thanked Evan and expressed that he was looking forward to the trip, showing excitement and appreciation.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: c8eacb03-fb12-4240-8dc1-dd937c1bf3c6, Score: 0.0455)\nAt 9:41 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan elaborated that kayaking and watching the sunset last summer was a truly peaceful experience. Sam agreed, noting that being in nature is very calming. Evan likened nature to a reset button for the mind and body. Sam wholeheartedly agreed and shared his intention to spend more time outdoors in nature to rejuvenate himself.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: b59161fc-37c8-480f-a48c-f23234b8af05, Score: 0.0438)\nAt 8:21 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed that Sam’s support had been invaluable during his attempts to try new things like yoga. Sam replied that everyone needs help when starting new activities and that having support is important. Evan agreed, noting that knowing he was not alone made a big difference. Sam encouraged Evan to keep him updated on how yoga went and said goodbye. Evan reciprocated the farewell, thanking Sam and promising to talk soon. This exchange highlighted their ongoing mutual encouragement and friendship.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: c7522bc3-8daa-4571-80e5-b9788362661d, Score: 0.0435)\nAt 9:40 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo taken from the front of a kayak during a camping trip last summer (summer 2023). He described the experience of watching an amazing sunset on the lake as unforgettable and emphasized how moments like these remind people of life’s beauty even during difficult times. Sam admired the photo and expressed that it must have been a great experience to be out on the lake.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: d0b268a6-9def-4568-ab22-727528a3db77, Score: 0.0414)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 3bbfcf17-9c00-4391-ac45-62367610a79e, Score: 0.0412)\nAlso at 06:22 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan revealed to Sam that he had recently started taking painting classes a few days prior and was really enjoying the experience. He framed this as part of trying new things. Sam asked why Evan, who was already good at drawing, decided to join a painting class and inquired about how Evan originally started painting years ago. Evan shared an image of a painting of a forest scene on an easel and explained that a friend had given him that painting, which inspired him to start painting. He joined the classes to meet like-minded people and showcase his skills, believing that one can always improve. Sam complimented Evan\'s talent and asked if he had taken any other classes. Evan shared another image showing a brush, pencil, and eyeliners on a cloth, stating that he had only been painting with those tools so far but might explore other classes in the future. Evan described painting as a way to find peace and express himself.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: ca584324-2870-4ea2-af05-457b8090bad3, Score: 0.0296)\nOn December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Sam shared a photograph with Evan showing a man standing on a rock overlooking a valley, announcing that he was embracing a healthier lifestyle. Sam mentioned that he had taken his friends on an epic hiking trip the previous Friday (December 29, 2023). Evan responded by sharing a photo of a small stream running through a lush green forest, expressing enthusiasm for Sam\'s hiking experience and remarking that nothing beats a good hike to feel alive.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: c6785ce5-5410-45be-b02d-59ae20df0b80, Score: 0.0280)\nAt 6:51 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Evan recalled that Sam had mentioned his love for hiking before. He emphasized that hiking is a great way to center oneself and connect with nature. Evan proposed that they should definitely plan a hike together soon.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 255bf297-4f37-41d7-bc3d-68eace473861, Score: 0.0275)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:23 AM, Sam said that although he had not gone on a road trip in a long time, he loved being surrounded by nature because it was tranquil and refreshing. Sam expressed a desire to hike more but noted it could be challenging. He mentioned working on becoming healthier and hoped that a road trip and hike might be possible soon. Evan shared a photo of a lake with a mountain in the background and said that nature was peaceful. Evan recommended hiking more, as he did, describing it as calming and fun. Evan proposed that they should go hiking together sometime.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 9976ae1f-6f69-4ad1-ab9f-3c3f8ede2617, Score: 0.0267)\nAt 10:24 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed enthusiasm about hiking together and asked Evan which lake he recommended for exploring local trails. Evan shared another photo of a lake with a mountain in the background, describing it as gorgeous with many nearby trails that Sam would love. Sam admired the view and asked if the location was nearby. Evan said it was only a two-hour drive from their location but assured Sam that the trip was worth every minute due to the incredible views and peaceful atmosphere. Sam concluded that a day trip was doable and expressed excitement about answering nature\'s call to check it out, thanking Evan.\n\n\n\nQuestion: When did Sam and his friend decide to try kayaking?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
