times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 943501fa-0341-4cbd-b519-e9a5a017294e, Score: 0.0325)\nAlso at 9:37 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan admitted to Sam that he had to apologize to his partner for an embarrassing drunken night. Sam sympathized with Evan\'s situation and shared that he was doing his best to manage his health. Sam then asked Evan how his partner had reacted to the news about the rose bushes, referring to a previous incident.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: d770831e-2e41-4ed3-99d5-71e86f4077e4, Score: 0.0325)\nAt 12:18 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan explained to Sam that he had gone out with friends the previous day (January 9, 2024) and had consumed a bit too much alcohol. He admitted to doing something he regretted that involved someone\'s roses. Sam asked for more details about the incident and whether everything was okay now.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 4dfa21f7-da6e-4dd9-9be2-973d2daeec9f, Score: 0.0308)\nOn November 21, 2023 (Tuesday) at 07:30 PM, Sam reached out to Evan after a long time, asking how he was doing and hoping all was well. Evan responded that life had been a wild ride lately. He shared that the previous week (November 14-20, 2023), he experienced a health scare that required a hospital visit. During a check-up, something suspicious was found, which frightened Evan. Fortunately, it turned out to be a misunderstanding. This experience made Evan realize the importance of monitoring his health closely.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 3d5bf21a-dcff-4409-aadb-1ccb82b51ae8, Score: 0.0308)\nAt 1:38 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Sam complimented Evan and his family, asking what was cooking that night. Evan replied that they were having a family get-together and enjoying homemade lasagna, expressing excitement. Evan also mentioned that he had started a new diet limiting himself to just two ginger snaps a day and asked Sam what was on his menu that evening.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 0ccff4bb-a2bc-4b28-a992-a191593013ed, Score: 0.0305)\nAt 12:17 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan reached out to Sam, hoping he was doing well and mentioning that something funny had happened the previous night (January 9, 2024). Sam responded promptly, asking Evan what had happened and inviting him to share the story.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 0176f4c3-0bb7-4e76-b8dc-92de50966b77, Score: 0.0303)\nAlso on December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Evan told Sam that he and his partner had taken their Prius for a long drive to the mountains the previous weekend (December 23-24, 2023). The trip was perfect until they experienced a minor accident on the way back. Sam expressed concern about their well-being, and Evan reassured him that they were fine. Evan explained that although the accident was minor, it somewhat dampened his experience of telling his work friends about his marriage. Despite this, Evan noted that his work friends had been very supportive.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: d71ab2d1-2916-4cec-99f8-5bbbe951444b, Score: 0.0288)\nOn October 14, 2023 (Saturday) at 4:07 PM, Evan reinitiated contact with Sam by sharing a photograph of a painting depicting a person standing on a cliff. Evan asked Sam how he was doing, noting it had been a while since they last talked and expressing hope that all was well. Sam replied with a photo of a person holding a box of sodas in front of a wall, admitting that he had experienced a rough week. Sam confessed that he gave in and bought some unhealthy snacks, which made him feel guilty.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 3bbfcf17-9c00-4391-ac45-62367610a79e, Score: 0.0284)\nAlso at 06:22 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan revealed to Sam that he had recently started taking painting classes a few days prior and was really enjoying the experience. He framed this as part of trying new things. Sam asked why Evan, who was already good at drawing, decided to join a painting class and inquired about how Evan originally started painting years ago. Evan shared an image of a painting of a forest scene on an easel and explained that a friend had given him that painting, which inspired him to start painting. He joined the classes to meet like-minded people and showcase his skills, believing that one can always improve. Sam complimented Evan\'s talent and asked if he had taken any other classes. Evan shared another image showing a brush, pencil, and eyeliners on a cloth, stating that he had only been painting with those tools so far but might explore other classes in the future. Evan described painting as a way to find peace and express himself.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: a365303c-bdc1-4f01-a90e-e0e519c3ac4e, Score: 0.0281)\nAt 1:39 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan repeated that he had started a new diet limiting himself to two ginger snaps daily and asked Sam about his dinner plans. Sam shared a photo of a plate with bread and meat, complimented Evan\'s discipline, and said they were keeping dinner light with homemade lasagna. Sam humorously noted that his meal could not compete with Evan\'s ginger snap limit.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 639cba1f-8b1e-4398-9a81-d41cce544e0e, Score: 0.0269)\nAlso at 4:15 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Sam promised to be Evan\'s cheerleader once he got some sleep. Sam then shared an amazing dream he had the previous night where he was soaring over skyscrapers, describing the feeling as incredible and wondering about its significance.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 8ea72b03-3952-442f-b41b-ee3309b41b77, Score: 0.0269)\nAt 11:02 AM on December 31, 2023 (Sunday), Sam commented that Evan\'s work friends were likely thrilled to hear about his marriage despite the accident. Evan agreed, describing the period as a whirlwind of emotions and expressing relief that the accident was minor. He reflected on the importance of taking it easy on the road. Sam emphasized the importance of safety and expressed gladness that Evan could still enjoy peaceful moments after the incident. Evan agreed, stating that nature brings peace and clarity and is a great experience. Sam added that nature helps put everything else into perspective and helps find inner peace by reminding people of the bigger picture.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: b59161fc-37c8-480f-a48c-f23234b8af05, Score: 0.0267)\nAt 8:21 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed that Sam’s support had been invaluable during his attempts to try new things like yoga. Sam replied that everyone needs help when starting new activities and that having support is important. Evan agreed, noting that knowing he was not alone made a big difference. Sam encouraged Evan to keep him updated on how yoga went and said goodbye. Evan reciprocated the farewell, thanking Sam and promising to talk soon. This exchange highlighted their ongoing mutual encouragement and friendship.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: abf17dac-c175-4338-acf4-6b4333ab5326, Score: 0.0266)\nAlso at 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Evan shared an anecdote about an event that occurred two weeks prior (around September 22, 2023). He had helped a lost tourist find their way, which unexpectedly turned into a spontaneous tour around the city. Evan described the experience as a blast. Sam responded positively, noting how helping others can lead to unexpected adventures.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: ca584324-2870-4ea2-af05-457b8090bad3, Score: 0.0263)\nOn December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Sam shared a photograph with Evan showing a man standing on a rock overlooking a valley, announcing that he was embracing a healthier lifestyle. Sam mentioned that he had taken his friends on an epic hiking trip the previous Friday (December 29, 2023). Evan responded by sharing a photo of a small stream running through a lush green forest, expressing enthusiasm for Sam\'s hiking experience and remarking that nothing beats a good hike to feel alive.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: f8c13275-c8a0-44bc-9718-92ad9b50c889, Score: 0.0256)\nAt 12:19 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan confessed that he had an embarrassing accident where he urinated near some roses. He apologized for the incident. Sam reacted with concern, asking if anyone had been upset and whether Evan was okay.\n\n\n\nQuestion: When did Evan have a drunken night with his friends?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
