3da247ac, Score: 0.0272)\nAlso at 4:16 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Sam thanked Evan for the suggestion to look into dream interpretation. Sam reflected that the journey toward better health felt endless at times but was convinced it would be rewarding in the end. Sam wished Evan good luck with finding his keys.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 5a726be1-b441-44e9-a8bb-d84741c753c3, Score: 0.0270)\nOn January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:28 AM, Evan encouraged Sam by suggesting that with a little more practice, Sam might learn to control his recurring flying dreams and asked Sam to update him once he mastered it. Evan wished Sam enjoyment of the fresh air and scenic views during his beach walks. Sam thanked Evan and expressed his intention to make the most of the outdoor activities, wishing Evan well in return.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 6f66ad4f-6870-4d71-aea5-6c231e5227f2, Score: 0.0265)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:56 PM, Sam told Evan that he had been trying to maintain his new health routine but found it tough due to pressure from his family. Evan acknowledged the importance of encouragement but cautioned against stress from others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 6d9f8dc4-a216-410c-8035-a4831c81491d, Score: 0.0255)\nAt 7:16 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam thanked Evan for the encouragement and committed to trying painting, promising to update Evan on how it went. Evan responded enthusiastically, advising Sam to have fun