times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 3a15043c-800c-4b95-8b28-2ce769af8cf1, Score: 0.0492)\nOn May 24, 2023 (Wednesday) at 7:11 PM, Evan reached out to Sam, sharing that since their last conversation, much had happened. Evan described a recent family road trip to Jasper the previous weekend (May 20-21, 2023), highlighting the drive along the Icefields Parkway and the stunning glaciers and lakes they saw. Evan shared a photo of a glacier taken during the trip. Sam responded with enthusiasm, noting that he had never been to Jasper but found the scenery breathtaking, and asked Evan for more details about the road trip and whether it was relaxing. Evan replied that the trip was great, emphasizing the fresh air, peacefulness, and a cozy cabin surrounded by mountains and forests that made the trip feel like a true retreat.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: 255bf297-4f37-41d7-bc3d-68eace473861, Score: 0.0466)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:23 AM, Sam said that although he had not gone on a road trip in a long time, he loved being surrounded by nature because it was tranquil and refreshing. Sam expressed a desire to hike more but noted it could be challenging. He mentioned working on becoming healthier and hoped that a road trip and hike might be possible soon. Evan shared a photo of a lake with a mountain in the background and said that nature was peaceful. Evan recommended hiking more, as he did, describing it as calming and fun. Evan proposed that they should go hiking together sometime.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 2c9e3ba8-8bcd-4186-933c-faf7c3dd9e52, Score: 0.0461)\nAt 10:21 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Evan shared a photograph of a car parked near a lake with mountains in the background, explaining that he had taken a road trip the previous month (July 2023). He described the scenery as stunning and said that being in nature helped him relax. Sam admired the photo and asked where Evan had gone, noting it must have been nice to get away. Evan replied that he had traveled to the Rocky Mountains, describing the experience as refreshing with incredible views. Evan asked Sam if he enjoyed road trips and exploring nature.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: a20302ba-38c3-44d4-b3e6-570d4b2350de, Score: 0.0457)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:21 PM, Sam admired the stunning sunset in Evan\'s photo and asked if it was a special spot for watching sunsets. Evan confirmed it was a peaceful place near his home where he often went to relax and unwind. Sam expressed interest in visiting the spot with Evan sometime. Evan wished he could bring Sam along and explained that the photo was taken the previous Friday (November 3, 2023) at his favorite beach spot. He described how watching the waves and sunset colors helped him find peace during tough times and symbolized nature\'s resilience. Evan suggested they plan a visit together someday. Sam agreed enthusiastically, calling the photo mesmerizing and supporting the plan. Evan expressed gladness that Sam liked the place and reiterated that it was calming. They agreed to make a point to visit together soon, with Sam calling the trip a perfect way to de-stress. Evan proposed planning the trip for next month (December 2023) and expressed excitement about exploring the spot together.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 8ea72b03-3952-442f-b41b-ee3309b41b77, Score: 0.0445)\nAt 11:02 AM on December 31, 2023 (Sunday), Sam commented that Evan\'s work friends were likely thrilled to hear about his marriage despite the accident. Evan agreed, describing the period as a whirlwind of emotions and expressing relief that the accident was minor. He reflected on the importance of taking it easy on the road. Sam emphasized the importance of safety and expressed gladness that Evan could still enjoy peaceful moments after the incident. Evan agreed, stating that nature brings peace and clarity and is a great experience. Sam added that nature helps put everything else into perspective and helps find inner peace by reminding people of the bigger picture.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: d1d45e34-2c13-4a16-91d8-40b009b3830c, Score: 0.0443)\nOn August 19, 2023 (Saturday) at 06:27 PM, Sam complimented Evan on the bright colors in his paintings and asked how he captured the tranquil beauty of nature. Evan shared an image of a tree with pink flowers in a field and explained that he aimed to convey the peacefulness of being outdoors through his paintings. Sam admired the picture and asked if Evan often spent time in such places. Evan responded with an image of a truck parked in the middle of a forest, saying he loved being in places like that because they brought back memories of road trips in his trusty car.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 427f14d6-3c3c-4419-bad3-af210fd5b1d8, Score: 0.0429)\nAt 7:12 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam acknowledged Evan\'s description of the peaceful trip and reflected on the importance of taking time for oneself, especially after a hard week. Sam revealed that his own week had been tough. Evan expressed sympathy and offered help. Sam appreciated the offer but explained that he had recently had a doctor\'s check-up a few days prior (around May 21, 2023), which revealed concerning weight results, describing the experience as eye-opening.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 0176f4c3-0bb7-4e76-b8dc-92de50966b77, Score: 0.0425)\nAlso on December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Evan told Sam that he and his partner had taken their Prius for a long drive to the mountains the previous weekend (December 23-24, 2023). The trip was perfect until they experienced a minor accident on the way back. Sam expressed concern about their well-being, and Evan reassured him that they were fine. Evan explained that although the accident was minor, it somewhat dampened his experience of telling his work friends about his marriage. Despite this, Evan noted that his work friends had been very supportive.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: d21f8c82-92c9-413f-9737-3726ec2fab9b, Score: 0.0301)\nAt 06:29 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Sam expressed interest in Evan\'s road trips and asked if he had visited any fun places during those rides. Evan shared a photo of a person skiing on a snowy trail and said that last month he had driven somewhere fun with amazing views. Sam asked if Evan took advantage of skiing opportunities in Banff, suggesting it sounded like a lot of fun. Evan shared an image of a group skiing down a snow-covered slope and confirmed that the trip was great for skiing, with amazing snow and lots of fun. Evan expressed excitement about returning next year and asked Sam if he had tried any winter sports.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 2c045826-338e-410d-a3c1-9f84a80fe27e, Score: 0.0284)\nAt 7:41 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan shared an image of a sunset over a body of water, describing the island as a little slice of paradise where he always felt peaceful and serene. Sam expressed gratitude for Evan sharing this glimpse into his peaceful retreat, acknowledging its calming qualities. This moment reinforced the theme of tranquility associated with Evan’s childhood home.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 1331051d-9ff7-4061-a44b-2e1f15b23de2, Score: 0.0277)\nAt 09:01 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam complimented Evan\'s paintings and asked about the sources of inspiration. Evan explained that the sunset painting was inspired by a vacation taken a few years ago, highlighting the stunning colors he experienced. The cactus painting was inspired by a road trip taken the previous month (September 2023). Evan expressed enthusiasm about the interesting places that inspired his artwork.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: a7d6ee30-3e27-4442-b6b3-f6fff097befa, Score: 0.0274)\nAt 9:39 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan complimented Sam’s countryside photo and asked if being in the countryside helped Sam relax and get fresh air away from the city. Sam confirmed that spending time in nature indeed helped him relax and provided fresh air, offering a reprieve from urban life.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: b490fba3-71ad-46c1-92ef-993bce8956ed, Score: 0.0273)\nOn August 7, 2023 (Monday) at 7:52 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a couple walking through the snow holding hands and told Sam about a recent trip to Canada during the previous week (last week, July 31 - August 6, 2023). Evan described meeting an incredible Canadian woman during the trip, which felt like a movie moment and made him feel alive. Sam responded by sharing a photo of a person walking on the beach with a surfboard, congratulating Evan on the special connection. Sam also expressed sympathy for Evan’s ongoing health issues, acknowledging how such challenges can make it difficult to fully enjoy life.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 7d77db47-4216-4f8e-b6a6-97f9bfa3b5e1, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 09:31 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan shared an image of a painting depicting a mountain range with a horse. He related to Sam\'s experience by saying that when he was stressed, he also sought comfort. Evan shared that he found painting or going for a drive helpful as coping mechanisms.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 9976ae1f-6f69-4ad1-ab9f-3c3f8ede2617, Score: 0.0269)\nAt 10:24 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed enthusiasm about hiking together and asked Evan which lake he recommended for exploring local trails. Evan shared another photo of a lake with a mountain in the background, describing it as gorgeous with many nearby trails that Sam would love. Sam admired the view and asked if the location was nearby. Evan said it was only a two-hour drive from their location but assured Sam that the trip was worth every minute due to the incredible views and peaceful atmosphere. Sam concluded that a day trip was doable and expressed excitement about answering nature\'s call to check it out, thanking Evan.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: abf17dac-c175-4338-acf4-6b4333ab5326, Score: 0.0262)\nAlso at 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Evan shared an anecdote about an event that occurred two weeks prior (around September 22, 2023). He had helped a lost tourist find their way, which unexpectedly turned into a spontaneous tour around the city. Evan described the experience as a blast. Sam responded positively, noting how helping others can lead to unexpected adventures.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What did Evan find relaxing about his road trip to Jasper?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
