times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 2e247e8b-d554-40ad-9b0b-649625a99699, Score: 0.0492)\nAt 7:59 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam asked Evan what made him decide to get the bonsai tree. Evan explained that he chose it because it symbolizes strength and resilience, and taking care of it motivates him to keep going through tough times.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: f22378ac-7282-4a23-9588-f17019418527, Score: 0.0481)\nAt 7:58 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam admired the amazing view in Evan\'s photo and remarked that the key was to find something that keeps one motivated. Evan then shared a photo of a bonsai tree in a black vase on a wooden table and agreed, stating that finding something that motivates and makes one happy, whether large or tiny, helps conquer struggles encountered.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: b0a529b1-16c8-4ed8-a6de-4d8df5678387, Score: 0.0474)\nAt 8:00 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam expressed amazement at the bonsai tree, noting how powerful yet simple it was. Evan thanked Sam and said it served as a reminder that even in little things, people can be tough.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: d1d45e34-2c13-4a16-91d8-40b009b3830c, Score: 0.0469)\nOn August 19, 2023 (Saturday) at 06:27 PM, Sam complimented Evan on the bright colors in his paintings and asked how he captured the tranquil beauty of nature. Evan shared an image of a tree with pink flowers in a field and explained that he aimed to convey the peacefulness of being outdoors through his paintings. Sam admired the picture and asked if Evan often spent time in such places. Evan responded with an image of a truck parked in the middle of a forest, saying he loved being in places like that because they brought back memories of road trips in his trusty car.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 00af2873-5948-4f01-8c43-6bf42dae2914, Score: 0.0459)\nAt 9:43 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a tree with pink flowers in a park. He related the image to a time last spring (spring 2023) when he was feeling down but found that the vibrant colors brought a smile to his face, even if only briefly. Evan encouraged Sam to find joy in small moments outdoors, especially when health issues interfere with daily life. Sam responded that the photo was gorgeous and that sometimes the little things truly matter.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 3bbfcf17-9c00-4391-ac45-62367610a79e, Score: 0.0457)\nAlso at 06:22 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan revealed to Sam that he had recently started taking painting classes a few days prior and was really enjoying the experience. He framed this as part of trying new things. Sam asked why Evan, who was already good at drawing, decided to join a painting class and inquired about how Evan originally started painting years ago. Evan shared an image of a painting of a forest scene on an easel and explained that a friend had given him that painting, which inspired him to start painting. He joined the classes to meet like-minded people and showcase his skills, believing that one can always improve. Sam complimented Evan\'s talent and asked if he had taken any other classes. Evan shared another image showing a brush, pencil, and eyeliners on a cloth, stating that he had only been painting with those tools so far but might explore other classes in the future. Evan described painting as a way to find peace and express himself.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 7e975a95-6a59-4ddb-b081-009a09109c48, Score: 0.0414)\nOn August 7, 2023 (Monday) at 7:55 PM, Sam expressed a wish that Evan\'s motivation would never fade and considered ordering a similar smartwatch, asking Evan if it was worth it. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a person\'s wrist wearing a smartwatch and explained that his family motivates him to stay healthy. He emphasized that the smartwatch helps significantly with his health goals by tracking his progress and serving as a constant reminder to keep going.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 255bf297-4f37-41d7-bc3d-68eace473861, Score: 0.0288)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:23 AM, Sam said that although he had not gone on a road trip in a long time, he loved being surrounded by nature because it was tranquil and refreshing. Sam expressed a desire to hike more but noted it could be challenging. He mentioned working on becoming healthier and hoped that a road trip and hike might be possible soon. Evan shared a photo of a lake with a mountain in the background and said that nature was peaceful. Evan recommended hiking more, as he did, describing it as calming and fun. Evan proposed that they should go hiking together sometime.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 10ee995d-98bc-411a-9b2f-0609605b3631, Score: 0.0284)\nAt 06:25 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Sam asked Evan what he had been learning in his painting classes. Evan shared an image of a table covered with various watercolors and explained that the classes focused on watercolor techniques. The instructor emphasized observing nature and painting what they see. Evan described this as a relaxing way to take a break from everyday stress. Sam expressed interest and asked what type of nature Evan enjoyed painting most. Evan shared an image of a painting depicting a sunset over the ocean and said he loved painting landscapes because nature\'s beauty captivates him and brings him peace.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 44e0766f-5809-4cb3-8704-e1d90069fcea, Score: 0.0282)\nAt 09:33 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan enthusiastically confirmed that painting is an excellent hobby. He advised Sam to acquire acrylic paints, brushes, a canvas or paper, and a palette for mixing colors. Evan also offered to provide specific product recommendations and suggested planning a painting session once Sam was ready.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: d0b268a6-9def-4568-ab22-727528a3db77, Score: 0.0280)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: c8eacb03-fb12-4240-8dc1-dd937c1bf3c6, Score: 0.0276)\nAt 9:41 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan elaborated that kayaking and watching the sunset last summer was a truly peaceful experience. Sam agreed, noting that being in nature is very calming. Evan likened nature to a reset button for the mind and body. Sam wholeheartedly agreed and shared his intention to spend more time outdoors in nature to rejuvenate himself.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 8ea72b03-3952-442f-b41b-ee3309b41b77, Score: 0.0273)\nAt 11:02 AM on December 31, 2023 (Sunday), Sam commented that Evan\'s work friends were likely thrilled to hear about his marriage despite the accident. Evan agreed, describing the period as a whirlwind of emotions and expressing relief that the accident was minor. He reflected on the importance of taking it easy on the road. Sam emphasized the importance of safety and expressed gladness that Evan could still enjoy peaceful moments after the incident. Evan agreed, stating that nature brings peace and clarity and is a great experience. Sam added that nature helps put everything else into perspective and helps find inner peace by reminding people of the bigger picture.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 890041ae-cd7d-4f16-936b-60fbe7a633f2, Score: 0.0270)\nAt 09:02 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam praised Evan\'s artwork and inquired how Evan decided what to paint. Evan explained that he usually paints whatever is on his mind or reflects his feelings. His subjects often include good memories or places he wishes to visit. Evan described painting as a form of self-expression through art.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: c12668ff-1c90-46f2-94d3-4876c8894666, Score: 0.0265)\nAt 1:33 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan thanked Sam and described the moment of sharing their marriage news as awesome. He expressed feeling lucky to have found a partner who truly understands him and emphasized how happy their families were about the marriage, calling that the best part. Sam responded by acknowledging how great it was that Evan had found someone who understood him and noted the comfort that family support brings. Evan agreed, emphasizing the importance of family support and how it brought a good feeling to their lives. Sam concurred, stating that family brings love and happiness and is always there no matter what. Evan reiterated that family is special because of their never-ending love and support. Sam agreed, noting that both he and Evan have amazing families who are always there for them, calling it a blessing. Evan echoed this sentiment, saying their families provide joy, support, and love, and he could not imagine life without them. Sam shared that his own family had been his rock through everything. Evan shared a photo of a group of people sitting at a table with food, agreeing that families are their rock and that they are blessed to have them.\n\n\n\nQuestion: Why did Evan decide to get the bonsai tree?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini'