om others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 832d3c12-6656-40d6-b307-da6fea341b2d, Score: 0.0450)\nAt 8:01 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam emphasized that little things matter because they build resilience over time. Evan agreed, noting that every small action taken for oneself helps in the long run. Sam added that small steps add up and encouraged staying consistent and not giving up. Evan concurred, stating that consistency and perseverance would take them far and concluded that it was a great chat.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 0ef8b6b5-3217-403a-87f1-dc2a9c0b5c68, Score: 0.0440)\nAlso at 3:12 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan reassured Sam that progress takes time and encouraged him to be patient with himself. Evan emphasized the importance of Sam\'s health and expressed his belief in Sam\'s ability to succeed. He motivated Sam to keep going and stay upbeat, reinforcing the message with a positive affirmation: \'You got this!\'\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 4b175d81-75c5-420a-ac22-6d1e9308774c, Score: 0.0437)\nOn November 21, 2023 (Tuesday) at 7:30 PM, Evan asked Sam how he had been doing. Sam responded with concern about Evan\'s recent health scare, expressing relief that it was just a misunderstanding. Sam reflected on how such a health scare can be frightening and can prompt a person to re-evaluate what is important in life. This conversation marked the beginning of a deeper exchange about health and life priorities between Evan an