2025-12-18 02:01:27,436 - [answer-locomo_8_qa103] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9bc77b5e-f612-41a4-8292-d3f094bae8c2', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: ae71e0d1-61d1-4e58-a1f5-dd607d61192c, Score: 0.0487)\nAt 06:19 PM on August 19, 2023 (Saturday), Evan asked Sam if he had any favorite healthy meal recipes to share. Sam responded by sharing an image of two bowls of food with chopsticks and sauce, describing a flavorful and healthy grilled chicken and vegetable stir-fry recipe he had found and was enjoying. Evan complimented the dish\'s appearance and inquired if the sauce was a family secret, expressing interest in trying new recipes. Sam clarified that the sauce was homemade and offered to share the recipe. Evan accepted the offer enthusiastically. Sam then shared an image of a recipe card featuring a drawing of a vase of flowers and invited Evan to try the recipe and provide feedback.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: b2ee18d5-c43d-483f-9eb0-7141ac091c46, Score: 0.0484)\nAt 4:21 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a photo of a plate with a piece of salmon and some vegetables, reporting that the cooking class had been great and that he had learned awesome recipes. Sam described making a yummy grilled dish the previous night. Evan responded that the dish looked delicious and asked what ingredients Sam had used. Evan expressed interest in eating healthy and requested recipe suggestions.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 7bb49b4d-5b1c-440a-b91f-cd521cf98938, Score: 0.0479)\nAt 4:22 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam explained that he marinated the salmon with a few different ingredients and grilled it with vegetables, resulting in a flavorful dish. Sam offered to share more recipes from his cooking class and asked Evan what kind of recipes he was looking for. Evan replied that he would appreciate recipes that included more vegetables.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 76cfa14f-42fd-453a-819b-fb25360244e6, Score: 0.0455)\nOn August 19, 2023 (Saturday) at 06:22 PM, Evan thanked Sam for sharing the recipe and expressed his intention to try it out. Evan noted that experimenting with new recipes was a great way to stay busy and creative.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 250d7631-f71f-4c4a-8c47-690422d963b9, Score: 0.0448)\nAt 11:04 AM on December 31, 2023 (Sunday), Evan shared a photo of a woman sitting at a table with plates and glasses, stating that nature had been a great healer for him. He mentioned wanting to share some new healthy snacks he had been trying. Sam complimented the snacks as healthy and delicious, noting they were perfect for after a hike or post-accident recovery. Evan then shared a photo of cookies cooling on a rack, explaining that the cookies were nutrient-packed, easy to make, and offered to send Sam the recipes. Sam expressed appreciation and asked if Evan had any other healthy snack ideas. Evan shared another photo showing a bowl of coconut balls and a bowl of oats, describing a recipe for energy balls he had discovered. Sam asked if Evan liked them, acknowledging that they could be an acquired taste. Evan confirmed he enjoyed them, highlighting that they were energizing and a healthy way to satisfy a sweet tooth. Sam expressed enthusiasm for the healthy snack tips and thanked Evan. Evan hoped Sam would enjoy the recipes.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 33750198-be02-453f-838b-94223d926984, Score: 0.0446)\nAlso at 4:20 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a positive update that he was taking a cooking class to learn how to make healthier meals. Evan expressed sympathy for Sam\'s rough week but noted that these challenges were forcing both of them to take better care of themselves. Evan mentioned hearing that Sam\'s cooking class was packed with healthy recipes and asked how it was going and whether Sam had picked up any new tasty meals.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 8e4eb694-d96e-441a-9cfc-bee375292e87, Score: 0.0446)\nAt 4:23 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam confirmed he had a tasty and easy roasted vegetable recipe to share with Evan. Sam then inquired about Evan\'s well-being after his son\'s soccer accident, acknowledging it must have been tough. Evan responded that his son\'s ankle was getting better but still sore. He described the initial period as rough but was thankful the injury was not serious.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 051b804c-6856-425c-8809-af26e6351a95, Score: 0.0429)\nOn December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:09 AM, Sam thanked Evan for the healthy snack recipes and said he would give them a try. Sam remarked that the snacks looked delicious and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s help.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 8fb0cf2e-b991-462a-8bba-a62c4f673940, Score: 0.0410)\nOn August 19, 2023 (Saturday) at 06:17 PM, Sam shared an image with Evan showing a bowl containing spinach, avocado, and strawberries. Sam announced that he was on a diet and living healthier, acknowledging that it had been tough but expressing determination to stick with it. Evan congratulated Sam on the great news and asked how the changes were going. Sam admitted it was tough but confirmed his persistence. Evan praised Sam\'s dedication and inquired about any positive changes noticed. Sam reported experiencing more energy and less sluggishness after eating, which he found very encouraging. Evan responded enthusiastically, highlighting the positive impact of feeling more energized after meals and encouraged Sam to keep up the good work.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: ac0ad99d-4757-4b7a-9a82-624ed8b6db28, Score: 0.0383)\nAt 10:54 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a table full of fresh produce and vegetables to illustrate the dietary changes he made, such as reducing sugary snacks and increasing his intake of fruits and vegetables. He explained that these changes significantly improved his health and asked Sam if he had considered making any dietary adjustments.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 83e99abe-51da-47b3-84ee-ac3d7524ba1e, Score: 0.0380)\nAlso at 09:28 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Sam replied to Evan, sharing an image of a bowl containing beef and vegetables alongside a package of Healthy Choice. Sam described his life as an up and down ride.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: d89588b9-3a21-429e-ad3b-0aa2d63e4ecc, Score: 0.0379)\nAlso at 3:55 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam mentioned that he was trying to eat healthier these days. Evan complimented the salad Sam shared and explained that he was being extra careful with his health, trying to reduce processed foods and sugary snacks despite his fondness for ginger snaps. Evan asked Sam if he had made any recent dietary changes.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 6b4a1dac-43fc-44f4-b729-1b16591d5c32, Score: 0.0369)\nOn October 6, 2023 (Friday) at 08:57 PM, Sam sent Evan a photograph of a bowl of fruit with a striped cloth, indicating a new focus on healthier eating habits. Sam greeted Evan, noting it had been a long time since they last connected, and asked what was new with Evan.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 3d5bf21a-dcff-4409-aadb-1ccb82b51ae8, Score: 0.0308)\nAt 1:38 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Sam complimented Evan and his family, asking what was cooking that night. Evan replied that they were having a family get-together and enjoying homemade lasagna, expressing excitement. Evan also mentioned that he had started a new diet limiting himself to just two ginger snaps a day and asked Sam what was on his menu that evening.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: e7cc6553-06e8-448f-aa4e-69efd72bd263, Score: 0.0295)\nOn January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:24 AM, Evan shared a photo of a salad containing chicken, avocado, tomatoes, corn, and cheese with Sam. Evan encouraged Sam by saying the salad was a step in the right direction and reminded Sam to focus on maintaining a balanced diet alongside low-impact exercises. Evan asked Sam to keep him updated on the progress. Sam responded positively, complimenting the salad and inquiring about the inspiration behind it. Additionally, Sam requested suggestions for low-impact exercises to complement the diet.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: a365303c-bdc1-4f01-a90e-e0e519c3ac4e, Score: 0.0294)\nAt 1:39 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan repeated that he had started a new diet limiting himself to two ginger snaps daily and asked Sam about his dinner plans. Sam shared a photo of a plate with bread and meat, complimented Evan\'s discipline, and said they were keeping dinner light with homemade lasagna. Sam humorously noted that his meal could not compete with Evan\'s ginger snap limit.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: efbffc38-e07d-40d7-9b15-3402833135e3, Score: 0.0288)\nAt 1:44 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Sam shared a photo of a container of caramel-covered french fries and commented that Evan\'s honeymoon plans sounded amazing, highlighting skiing, trying local dishes, and enjoying breathtaking views as the perfect combination. Evan mentioned he was looking forward to trying poutine while in Canada. Sam noted that he had never tried poutine and acknowledged it as a Canadian specialty, asking Evan to let him know how he liked it. Evan agreed to keep Sam posted on whether poutine lived up to the hype. Sam encouraged Evan to share all the details and wished him an incredible trip. Evan thanked Sam and reciprocated the good wishes.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: dc98b4ae-2463-4d54-abdd-f6b589c5abbb, Score: 0.0272)\nAlso at 1:40 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Sam shared a photo of a pie topped with raspberries and limes, teasing Evan that it looked delicious. Evan responded that it looked yummy and asked if Sam had made it. Sam clarified that he had not made the pie; it was a photo from his cousin\'s wedding and described it as super special.\n\n[Memory 19] (ID: 15b8326d-accf-49e9-be71-6ad4599efc3b, Score: 0.0257)\nAt 10:57 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed enthusiasm about Evan’s snack recommendations, describing them as delicious, and thanked Evan. Sam also indicated an intention to read "The Great Gatsby" sometime in the future.\n\n[Memory 20] (ID: 47e1a4de-66d6-405f-9bbb-0fbf91e7ba27, Score: 0.0257)\nAt 1:42 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan shared a photo of a wedding cake decorated with candles and flowers on a table, commenting that weddings are indeed special and the cake looked great. Sam responded by complimenting the cake and noting it reminded him of special occasions. Sam then asked Evan if he had any upcoming plans.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What kind of recipe did Evan request from Sam on 19 August, 2023?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
