2025-12-18 02:01:39,438 - [answer-locomo_8_qa115] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9fac6d1d-0d35-4a9b-a561-8f0fcaf7c630', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: c0ea7989-c999-4b25-a06b-4a6dc0de02cd, Score: 0.0492)\nAt 08:58 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam sympathized with Evan\'s knee injury, acknowledging the difficulty of the situation. Sam asked if there were ways for Evan to remain active while healing. Evan responded that physical therapy had helped somewhat. Although he could not perform intense workouts, Evan was doing gentle exercises to maintain strength, noting that it was not as fulfilling as outdoor activities but still beneficial.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: bb56d93e-569c-4f98-81f9-d2da6752eab9, Score: 0.0484)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:20 AM, Sam reflected on life\'s unpredictability and emphasized the importance of adaptability and finding alternative ways to stay active when facing obstacles. Sam suggested Evan consider low-impact exercises or physical therapy for his knee. Sam also expressed interest in the book Evan mentioned. Evan confirmed that physical therapy was planned and hoped to get an appointment soon. Meanwhile, Evan was keeping activity low-key by swimming, which he found suitable for his condition. Sam agreed that swimming was a good choice because it is low-impact, easy on the joints, and refreshing, encouraging Evan to maintain his active lifestyle.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: ce007fdd-7b7e-43b2-8974-3a3dc27aa55c, Score: 0.0474)\nAlso at 08:57 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam inquired if Evan had picked up any new hobbies. Evan replied by sharing a photograph showing a person with a cast on their leg, explaining that he had injured his knee playing basketball with his children the previous week (last week, September 29, 2023). Evan described the injury as a setback that made staying active difficult. He expressed missing outdoor adventures they had enjoyed with family the previous year, calling those times \'good times with the family.\'\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: d129d43f-96db-4dcb-b493-bc2f2aadd6ee, Score: 0.0466)\nAt 10:19 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s knee injury, acknowledging how frustrating it is when the body does not cooperate. Sam asked if there was anything he could do to help. Evan appreciated Sam\'s concern and philosophized that life throws curveballs. Evan then shifted the conversation to mention a book he had been reading, saying it was getting better with every page and that he could not put it down.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: bdee660c-22f1-43bd-b80e-86700d293907, Score: 0.0466)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:18 AM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had started a new diet and exercise routine the previous Monday (August 21, 2023) and that it had made a huge difference, making him feel great. Sam asked Evan about any recent changes in his life. Evan responded that he was glad Sam\'s new routine was going well but shared that he had twisted his knee the previous Friday (August 25, 2023), causing significant pain and making it difficult to maintain his usual fitness routine. Evan expressed frustration because staying active was very important to him.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: e6eb97c3-ed81-4f29-883a-b23c49dd855f, Score: 0.0441)\nAt 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam expressed gladness that physical therapy was helping Evan and emphasized the importance of self-care. Sam asked if Evan had tried any enjoyable indoor activities or hobbies. Evan replied that he had been practicing his favorite hobby, watercolor painting, which he found to be a relaxing and engaging way to pass the time and enjoy colors.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: f0d0bcd1-cee7-4e28-983f-12468d7701e4, Score: 0.0431)\nAt 4:24 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam expressed relief that Evan\'s son\'s ankle was improving and acknowledged how hard it is to see loved ones hurt. Sam reminded Evan to look after himself as well, emphasizing the importance of health care. Evan agreed that taking care of themselves was a must and asked Sam how he had been feeling lately.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 6f66ad4f-6870-4d71-aea5-6c231e5227f2, Score: 0.0423)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:56 PM, Sam told Evan that he had been trying to maintain his new health routine but found it tough due to pressure from his family. Evan acknowledged the importance of encouragement but cautioned against stress from others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: e90206a4-4f5d-4515-b6bd-98f884055000, Score: 0.0422)\nAlso at 7:54 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam observed that Evan’s children appeared to be having a great time and inquired about how long Evan had been prioritizing his health. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a box containing a fitness watch and explained that his health journey has been ongoing for two years. He acknowledged that the process has had ups and downs but affirmed that he is doing his best to maintain his health.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 8e4eb694-d96e-441a-9cfc-bee375292e87, Score: 0.0421)\nAt 4:23 PM on August 15, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam confirmed he had a tasty and easy roasted vegetable recipe to share with Evan. Sam then inquired about Evan\'s well-being after his son\'s soccer accident, acknowledging it must have been tough. Evan responded that his son\'s ankle was getting better but still sore. He described the initial period as rough but was thankful the injury was not serious.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 9e7e3ee2-ec8c-4a3d-885c-0308f3593c85, Score: 0.0411)\nOn August 15, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:20 PM, Evan shared a photo of a person with a cast on their foot and updated Sam that it had been a few days since they last talked. Evan explained that life had been tough lately because his son had a soccer accident the previous Saturday (August 12, 2023) and hurt his ankle. Evan described how difficult it was to see his son hurt and that he had been looking after him and taking him to the doctor. Evan reflected on the challenges of being a dad watching his child go through pain. Sam expressed sympathy and said he could imagine how hard it must have been for Evan. Sam also shared that things had not been easy for himself either, mentioning a tough week and a doctor\'s appointment that served as a wake-up call to take better care of his own health.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 816b1c3e-762a-4816-a424-836783262dc5, Score: 0.0405)\nAlso at 03:09 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan responded by sharing a photo of himself performing a squat on a gym machine. He acknowledged that health challenges could be discouraging. Evan described how he had started lifting weights one year ago and found it to be a challenging but rewarding journey, noting visible progress. Evan offered to support Sam if he was interested in trying weightlifting.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 4eca99f1-707e-4890-87d0-d4df8e66d867, Score: 0.0303)\nAt 7:36 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam noticed Evan seemed to be having a good time and asked what Evan did to stay fit and healthy. Evan recounted that he maintained his fitness by regularly going to the gym and also enjoyed taking his car out for a spin, activities that helped him stay active and engaged. This conversation revealed Evan\'s active lifestyle habits.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 94db81d9-3819-4236-9665-bb021a583c78, Score: 0.0292)\nAt 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Evan shared that what worked for him was finding a fitness routine he genuinely enjoyed, which became his go-to activity. He loved the feeling of being healthy and strong. Evan emphasized making exercise fun and incorporating small smarter dietary choices that added up over time. He encouraged Sam by affirming that Sam had the capability to succeed.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 0d13f40e-4a92-4403-a6cf-1167d2a93d33, Score: 0.0272)\nOn July 27, 2023 (Thursday) at 10:52 AM, Sam confided in Evan that his friends had mocked his weight last Friday, which hurt him deeply and motivated him to make changes to improve his health. Evan responded with empathy, reassuring Sam that progress takes time and offering to work on the health journey together. Sam expressed gratitude for Evan’s support and shared that he was actively working on his health and becoming more physically active.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 4a6c4761-ccd0-407d-8408-104286282251, Score: 0.0260)\nAlso at 10:58 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan asked Sam if he had considered exercising, emphasizing that physical activity is just as important as maintaining a healthy diet.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: fec7ac28-e6ad-472a-8b38-dbf112117136, Score: 0.0258)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:59 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man sitting at a table filled with fruits and vegetables, illustrating his own health journey. He explained to Sam that about two years ago, he went through a similar phase where he changed his diet and started walking regularly. Sam complimented Evan on his appearance and asked how he managed the change. Evan responded that he shifted his focus to overall well-being rather than quick results, which relieved pressure and made a significant difference.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: b59161fc-37c8-480f-a48c-f23234b8af05, Score: 0.0258)\nAt 8:21 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed that Sam’s support had been invaluable during his attempts to try new things like yoga. Sam replied that everyone needs help when starting new activities and that having support is important. Evan agreed, noting that knowing he was not alone made a big difference. Sam encouraged Evan to keep him updated on how yoga went and said goodbye. Evan reciprocated the farewell, thanking Sam and promising to talk soon. This exchange highlighted their ongoing mutual encouragement and friendship.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What activity does Evan do to keep himself busy while healing his knee?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
