emories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 2c045826-338e-410d-a3c1-9f84a80fe27e, Score: 0.0471)\nAt 7:41 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan shared an image of a sunset over a body of water, describing the island as a little slice of paradise where he always felt peaceful and serene. Sam expressed gratitude for Evan sharing this glimpse into his peaceful retreat, acknowledging its calming qualities. This moment reinforced the theme of tranquility associated with Evan’s childhood home.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: 55667a3b-6b84-4080-bce7-bb77204d1878, Score: 0.0458)\nAt 4:29 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam admitted that he had not experienced love in the same way but had started enjoying running in the mornings as a way to clear his head. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a painting with a white background featuring blue, orange, and black colors. He acknowledged Sam’s approach to life, emphasizing the importance of finding what works for oneself. Evan encouraged Sam to keep trying new things, suggesting that he might find his own version of love in unexpected places and urged him to embrace the journey, which is full of surprises.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: abf17dac-c175-4338-acf4-6b4333ab5326, Score: 0.0428)\nAlso at 08:59 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Evan shared an anecdote about an event that occurred two weeks prior (around September 22, 2023). He had helped a lost tourist find their way, which unexpectedly turned into a spontaneous tour around the city. Evan described the experience as a blast. Sam responded positively, noting how helping others can lead to unexpected adventures.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 0ba8092d-2421-42f5-b8c4-21b8dcec3339, Score: 0.0416)\nAt 4:08 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan asked Sam how everything was going and if there was anything new and exciting in his life. Sam thanked Evan and admitted that he had been unable to resist the unhealthy snacks, acknowledging the need to do better. Sam also shared that he was dealing with work stress and trying to stay motivated, revealing ongoing challenges in his daily life.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 666dba78-b532-486a-86f8-2f5bdb73f4c3, Score: 0.0310)\nAt 7:32 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shifted the conversation back to Evan, asking how he was doing following his health scare. Evan responded positively, stating that he was doing well and that doctors had confirmed everything was fine. He reflected that the experience taught him the value of life. Evan also commented on the movie Sam had mentioned, expressing interest in it. This moment underscored Evan\'s recovery and his renewed appreciation for life.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: de625c2a-3b0c-40c3-8eed-4888ee7f8341, Score: 0.0301)\nAlso at 1:51 PM on October 17, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam remarked on Evan\'s mention of another lost tourist, humorously noting that Evan seemed to be becoming the go-to person for tourists in need, highlighting a recurring pattern in Evan\'s recent experiences.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: bb56d93e-569c-4f98-81f9-d2da6752eab9, Score: 0.0301)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:20 AM, Sam reflected on life\'s unpredictability and emphasized the importance of adaptability and finding alternative ways to stay active when facing obstacles. Sam suggested Evan consider low-impact exercises or physical therapy for his knee. Sam also expressed interest in the book Evan mentioned. Evan confirmed that physical therapy was planned and hoped to get an appointment soon. Meanwhile, Evan was keeping activity low-key by swimming, which he found suitable for his condition. Sam agreed that swimming was a good choice because it is low-impact, easy on the joints, and refreshing, encouraging Evan to maintain his active lifestyle.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 4dfa21f7-da6e-4dd9-9be2-973d2daeec9f, Score: 0.0299)\nOn November 21, 2023 (Tuesday) at 07:30 PM, Sam reached out to Evan after a long time, asking how he was doing and hoping all was well. Evan responded that life had been a wild ride lately. He shared that the previous week (November 14-20, 2023), he experienced a health scare that required a hospital visit. During a check-up, something suspicious was found, which frightened Evan. Fortunately, it turned out to be a misunderstanding. This experience made Evan realize the importance of monitoring his health closely.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: c12668ff-1c90-46f2-94d3-4876c8894666, Score: 0.0291)\nAt 1:33 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan thanked Sam and described the moment of sharing their marriage news as awesome. He expressed feeling lucky to have found a partner who truly understands him and emphasized how happy their families were about the marriage, calling that the best part. Sam responded by acknowledging how great it was that Evan had found someone who understood him and noted the comfort that family support brings. Evan agreed, emphasizing the importance of family support and how it brought a good feeling to their lives. Sam concurred, stating that family brings love and happiness and is always there no matter what. Evan reiterated that family is special because of their never-ending love and support. Sam agreed, noting that both he and Evan have amazing families who are always there for them, calling it a blessing. Evan echoed this sentiment, saying their families provide joy, support, and love, and he could not imagine life without them. Sam shared that his own family had been his rock through everything. Evan shared a photo of a group of people sitting at a table with food, agreeing that families are their rock and that they are blessed to have them.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: b490fba3-71ad-46c1-92ef-993bce8956ed, Score: 0.0288)\nOn August 7, 2023 (Monday) at 7:52 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a couple walking through the snow holding hands and told Sam about a recent trip to Canada during the previous week (last week, July 31 - August 6, 2023). Evan described meeting an incredible Canadian woman during the trip, which felt like a movie moment and made him feel alive. Sam responded by sharing a photo of a person walking on the beach with a surfboard, congratulating Evan on the special connection. Sam also expressed sympathy for Evan’s ongoing health issues, acknowledging how such challenges can make it difficult to fully enjoy life.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: a20302ba-38c3-44d4-b3e6-570d4b2350de, Score: 0.0278)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:21 PM, Sam admired the stunning sunset in Evan\'s photo and asked if it was a special spot for watching sunsets. Evan confirmed it was a peaceful place near his home where he often went to relax and unwind. Sam expressed interest in visiting the spot with Evan sometime. Evan wished he could bring Sam along and explained that the photo was taken the previous Friday (November 3, 2023) at his favorite beach spot. He described how watching the waves and sunset colors helped him find peace during tough times and symbolized nature\'s resilience. Evan suggested they plan a visit together someday. Sam agreed enthusiastically, calling the photo mesmerizing and supporting the plan. Evan expressed gladness that Sam liked the place and reiterated that it was calming. They agreed to make a point to visit together soon, with Sam calling the trip a perfect way to de-stress. Evan proposed planning the trip for next month (December 2023) and expressed excitement about exploring the spot together.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 852a01aa-f30f-4a2a-8c67-892405b6f172, Score: 0.0276)\nAt 7:39 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan affirmed that growing up on the island had shaped him and that it would always hold a special place in his heart. Sam agreed, describing such places as soul-calming. This conversation emphasized the emotional and formative significance of Evan’s childhood environment.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 0c4b57aa-aaa7-4ede-aa2f-1adf2a90793b, Score: 0.0275)\nAt 7:53 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Evan shared a photo of a container of cookies on a counter and thanked Sam for his kind words. Evan described his new relationship as fun and energizing, a refreshing change especially after dealing with health issues.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 2448af38-d37a-4d74-963b-84d5c6145773, Score: 0.0266)\nAt 7:57 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam thanked Evan for the recommendation and inquired about other sources of motivation. Evan shared a photo of a small island with a lone boat in the water and explained that he was motivated by a thirst for adventure, particularly through interesting hikes, which he found pretty cool.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What adventurous theme is emerging in Evan\'s life as mentioned by Sam?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
