emories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 356c5bcf-0b7b-4631-a1a8-1b3c5dce8472, Score: 0.0492)\nOn December 5, 2023 (Tuesday) at 8:16 PM, Evan reached out to Sam to share some frustrating news: his newly purchased Prius had broken down. Evan explained that this was a significant stressor because he relied on the car for his active lifestyle and road trips. He expressed frustration that something new could malfunction so soon. Sam responded empathetically, acknowledging how difficult it is to deal with a new car breaking down, especially when it is the primary mode of transportation.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: cccb3361-1af1-4223-b6a1-c63d03f440e2, Score: 0.0481)\nAt 8:17 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan elaborated that he had been counting on the new Prius to be reliable, and dealing with unexpected issues was challenging. He accepted that even new cars can have problems. Sam offered a positive perspective, suggesting that setbacks like this can sometimes lead to new opportunities. Evan agreed and expressed that he was trying to view the situation as a chance to explore alternative ways to stay active and travel, possibly trying something different.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 7776c65b-bf42-429f-90cf-2ab35c7358f3, Score: 0.0476)\nAlso at 1:48 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan explained that his old Prius had broken down, prompting him to repair and sell it. He shared a photo depicting a lake with rocks and mountains in the background, revealing that the family trip destination was the Rocky Mountains. Evan invited Sam to check out the scenic image from their Rockies trip.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: c2130e46-bd2f-4714-8242-094771b57cae, Score: 0.0464)\nOn May 18, 2023 (Thursday) at 1:47 PM, Sam greeted Evan warmly and asked about any new developments since their last meeting. Evan responded that he had just returned from a family trip, traveling in his new Toyota Prius. This marked a recent change for Evan, who was eager to share this update with Sam.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 0176f4c3-0bb7-4e76-b8dc-92de50966b77, Score: 0.0459)\nAlso on December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Evan told Sam that he and his partner had taken their Prius for a long drive to the mountains the previous weekend (December 23-24, 2023). The trip was perfect until they experienced a minor accident on the way back. Sam expressed concern about their well-being, and Evan reassured him that they were fine. Evan explained that although the accident was minor, it somewhat dampened his experience of telling his work friends about his marriage. Despite this, Evan noted that his work friends had been very supportive.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 1484a97d-3a3c-402a-840a-5891917aa38b, Score: 0.0457)\nAt 1:48 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam asked Evan what had happened to his old Prius and where Evan and his family had traveled during their recent trip. Sam\'s curiosity focused on the fate of Evan\'s previous vehicle and the location of the family vacation.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 7d0d047c-7b97-4b4f-be15-ea8807845529, Score: 0.0448)\nAt 09:04 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam shared his frustration with his new phone, specifically that its navigation app frequently malfunctioned, making it challenging to get around. Evan responded by complimenting Sam\'s writing as a great form of self-expression and asked what kind of writing Sam enjoyed.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: bdee660c-22f1-43bd-b80e-86700d293907, Score: 0.0439)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:18 AM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had started a new diet and exercise routine the previous Monday (August 21, 2023) and that it had made a huge difference, making him feel great. Sam asked Evan about any recent changes in his life. Evan responded that he was glad Sam\'s new routine was going well but shared that he had twisted his knee the previous Friday (August 25, 2023), causing significant pain and making it difficult to maintain his usual fitness routine. Evan expressed frustration because staying active was very important to him.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 5f042a9a-c509-4cbf-84e6-561a21b06bc7, Score: 0.0433)\nAt 4:03 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed sympathy for Sam’s frustrating experience with the broken self-checkout machines at the supermarket and hoped that such an issue would not happen again. Sam acknowledged Evan’s concern and wished Evan to take care of himself, ending the brief exchange on a positive note.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 5ba08f8a-6a8d-4efb-a3e0-0b870dba01bb, Score: 0.0429)\nAt 4:02 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam told Evan that he was excited about starting workouts but shared a recent frustrating experience at the supermarket. Sam explained that all the self-checkout machines were broken when he tried to shop, which negatively affected his mood. This incident occurred just before their conversation, as Sam mentioned he was coming from the shop.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 4b42c3a8-169c-4f13-80b0-7296bd00957d, Score: 0.0427)\nAlso at 11:09 AM on December 31, 2023 (Sunday), Sam shared that he had gone to the store again and, unsurprisingly, encountered issues with the self-checkout, describing it as a regular annoyance. Evan responded that he had never experienced problems with self-checkout. Sam joked that he seemed to attract such issues and offered to be called by Evan if he ever wanted to experience similar problems at the store.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: fb253bfa-ac7c-4a08-8270-64b0ac364cdc, Score: 0.0395)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 1:50 PM, Sam reached out to Evan, expressing that he had been missing their chats. Sam revealed that he had experienced a significant health scare the previous weekend (last weekend, October 7-8, 2023), which resulted in an emergency room visit due to a severe stomachache. The diagnosis was gastritis, which alarmed Sam and served as a wake-up call to prioritize his health. Sam mentioned plans to adopt a more nutritious diet and engage in regular exercise. Additionally, Sam shared that his phone had been malfunctioning, adding to his stress. Evan responded with sympathy, acknowledging that gastritis can be tough and emphasizing the importance of taking care of oneself.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: f8c13275-c8a0-44bc-9718-92ad9b50c889, Score: 0.0280)\nAt 12:19 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan confessed that he had an embarrassing accident where he urinated near some roses. He apologized for the incident. Sam reacted with concern, asking if anyone had been upset and whether Evan was okay.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 6f66ad4f-6870-4d71-aea5-6c231e5227f2, Score: 0.0278)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:56 PM, Sam told Evan that he had been trying to maintain his new health routine but found it tough due to pressure from his family. Evan acknowledged the importance of encouragement but cautioned against stress from others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: d129d43f-96db-4dcb-b493-bc2f2aadd6ee, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 10:19 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s knee injury, acknowledging how frustrating it is when the body does not cooperate. Sam asked if there was anything he could do to help. Evan appreciated Sam\'s concern and philosophized that life throws curveballs. Evan then shifted the conversation to mention a book he had been reading, saying it was getting better with every page and that he could not put it down.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: ff0bbfeb-76f7-4148-bbca-9e1a9f068a4b, Score: 0.0267)\nAlso at 10:55 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared a photo of a table displaying various sodas and water bottles, encouraging Sam to replace soda with flavored seltzer water as a healthier alternative. Evan motivated Sam by acknowledging the initial difficulty but expressed confidence in Sam’s ability to succeed. Additionally, Evan mentioned that he was engrossed in a new mystery novel that he found very gripping.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 5ecd42f2-a4ee-48c3-92f6-ca156967e30a, Score: 0.0263)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:18 PM, Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s job loss and asked what had happened. Evan explained that the company downsized, and he was part of that reduction. He was currently searching for a new job, which was challenging, but he remained hopeful and kept his spirits up. Sam acknowledged the difficulty of sudden job loss and praised Evan for handling it well. Sam offered to be there for Evan to talk or help in any way and expressed confidence that Evan would get through this. Evan thanked Sam for the support, emphasizing how much it meant to have someone to talk to, and promised to reach out if needed. Sam reiterated his availability and encouraged Evan to stay positive, affirming that life can be tough but they could get through it together.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: 4b175d81-75c5-420a-ac22-6d1e9308774c, Score: 0.0261)\nOn November 21, 2023 (Tuesday) at 7:30 PM, Evan asked Sam how he had been doing. Sam responded with concern about Evan\'s recent health scare, expressing relief that it was just a misunderstanding. Sam reflected on how such a health scare can be frightening and can prompt a person to re-evaluate what is important in life. This conversation marked the beginning of a deeper exchange about health and life priorities between Evan and Sam.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What was the main reason for Evan\'s frustration with his new Prius breaking down?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
