2025-12-18 02:02:42,686 - [answer-locomo_8_qa136] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-1585d5e1-a8ac-4635-a2f8-73e731073962', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: f9df7ebe-552b-4b3b-b7d6-0d64d6cc659a, Score: 0.0489)\nAt 6:52 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Evan empathized with Sam’s challenges and encouraged him to believe in himself and take progress one day at a time. Evan reminded Sam that his worth is not defined by his weight. Sam appreciated Evan’s support and admitted that breaking out of his comfort zone was tough.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: 7083f6cf-9422-4226-8f57-d84e41cc70c2, Score: 0.0476)\nAlso at 6:51 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Sam confided in Evan that he was struggling with his weight, which was negatively affecting his confidence. He expressed feelings of lacking motivation and difficulty overcoming the challenges related to his weight.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: fe099c8e-8a71-4b93-a130-bde4a21419a6, Score: 0.0469)\nAlso at 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam mentioned that he had been looking for a hobby to stay motivated and was thinking about trying painting. Sam asked Evan if painting would help him de-stress. Evan affirmed that painting was a great way to relieve stress and be creative, allowing freedom to explore colors, textures, and express feelings. Evan shared that he had been painting for a few years and found it peaceful. However, Evan clarified that painting alone would not address Sam\'s weight concerns and recommended exercise as an additional necessary component.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 427f14d6-3c3c-4419-bad3-af210fd5b1d8, Score: 0.0460)\nAt 7:12 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam acknowledged Evan\'s description of the peaceful trip and reflected on the importance of taking time for oneself, especially after a hard week. Sam revealed that his own week had been tough. Evan expressed sympathy and offered help. Sam appreciated the offer but explained that he had recently had a doctor\'s check-up a few days prior (around May 21, 2023), which revealed concerning weight results, describing the experience as eye-opening.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 3cb95a3a-9f97-46ad-8996-5ad40e9cd764, Score: 0.0455)\nOn October 8, 2023 (Sunday) at 03:09 PM, Sam reached out to Evan to share a personal concern. Sam revealed that during a medical check-up the previous Monday (October 2, 2023), his doctor had warned that his weight posed a serious health risk and that without changes, the situation could worsen. Although Sam had previously joked about his weight, the news was now hitting him hard, and he admitted to having a difficult time coping.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 0d13f40e-4a92-4403-a6cf-1167d2a93d33, Score: 0.0453)\nOn July 27, 2023 (Thursday) at 10:52 AM, Sam confided in Evan that his friends had mocked his weight last Friday, which hurt him deeply and motivated him to make changes to improve his health. Evan responded with empathy, reassuring Sam that progress takes time and offering to work on the health journey together. Sam expressed gratitude for Evan’s support and shared that he was actively working on his health and becoming more physically active.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: d98dcd44-6e2f-4652-aa81-78684fe57000, Score: 0.0439)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:13 PM, Sam excitedly informed Evan that he had become a Weight Watchers coach within his group, describing it as a significant accomplishment that made him feel proud. Evan congratulated Sam enthusiastically, expressing pride and acknowledging that becoming a Weight Watchers coach was a big deal. Sam appreciated Evan\'s support and reflected on the journey toward better health, noting that being chosen as a coach was an important step. Evan praised Sam\'s progress and expressed excitement about what lay ahead in Sam\'s health quest. Sam shared that being a coach would help keep him motivated and assist others in staying committed, acknowledging the challenge but feeling ready. Evan affirmed that helping others stay motivated is rewarding and said Sam was an inspiration, encouraging him to keep up the great work. Sam thanked Evan for his kind words, admitting the road had been difficult but expressing determination to continue making a positive impact.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 0ef8b6b5-3217-403a-87f1-dc2a9c0b5c68, Score: 0.0439)\nAlso at 3:12 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan reassured Sam that progress takes time and encouraged him to be patient with himself. Evan emphasized the importance of Sam\'s health and expressed his belief in Sam\'s ability to succeed. He motivated Sam to keep going and stay upbeat, reinforcing the message with a positive affirmation: \'You got this!\'\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 0eea3c65-614c-4365-b6bd-5fa195db5787, Score: 0.0419)\nAt 8:19 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan complimented the smoothie bowl Sam had shared and asked how the Weight Watchers meeting had gone. Evan also mentioned that he had been considering trying yoga as a gentle yet effective way to relieve stress and improve flexibility. He asked Sam for his opinion on yoga, seeking advice based on Sam’s experience.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: d90202cd-0443-4f96-bd47-f0d12a002f27, Score: 0.0395)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:51 PM, Evan encouraged Sam to set specific fitness goals such as running a certain distance or completing a number of push-ups. Evan explained that having clear goals would provide motivation and something to strive for. He also suggested that Sam find an exercise activity that he enjoys and consider exercising with a buddy to add fun and accountability. Evan asked Sam if this plan sounded good to him.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: fbe9c621-102b-4d56-98b2-3c7bb5648996, Score: 0.0305)\nAt 7:31 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam confided to Evan that he had been experiencing some physical discomfort that was limiting his movement. Sam mentioned efforts to improve his condition through dietary changes, though he acknowledged the difficulty in maintaining these changes. Evan empathized with Sam\'s situation, recognizing how challenging it is when health issues hold someone back. Evan encouraged Sam by expressing belief in his ability to improve through small, manageable steps.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: b2c7ffb8-3e6d-48a9-ade3-bf4747fd3bd2, Score: 0.0295)\nAlso at 03:10 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan encouraged Sam by emphasizing the importance of starting with proper form and technique. He recommended finding a trainer to help avoid injuries while building strength. Evan advised starting with light weights and gradually increasing intensity as strength improved. He stressed the importance of consistency in the workout routine and invited Sam to keep him updated on his progress, wishing him good luck.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 70b2af4d-07e6-41f2-be2f-4f1a6a8a164f, Score: 0.0284)\nOn June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:01 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man with a beard holding a dumbbell to Sam, expressing his enthusiasm and support for their workout goals. Evan emphasized that exercise clears the mind and encouraged Sam to join him in reaching their fitness objectives. Sam responded positively, expressing excitement and requesting help to get started with exercising. Evan gladly offered to meet with Sam to demonstrate some basic exercises, reinforcing their shared commitment to achieving their fitness goals together.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 0657e829-24b3-4e16-9f24-6894a7e01b87, Score: 0.0282)\nAt 4:11 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Evan expressed gladness to support Sam and noted the importance of surrounding oneself with caring people. Evan asked about the note Sam had shared, wondering if it was a reminder or motivational quote. Sam confirmed it was a quote helping him stay motivated by reminding him that progress is more important than perfection and that taking small steps toward a healthier life still counts as progress.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 7f05ee0f-3875-45d3-b516-3902552b0bc3, Score: 0.0272)\nAt 09:28 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Sam asked Evan if he had seen the before-and-after photos he posted showing the results of his diet, explaining that he was working to motivate others to make better choices. Evan responded enthusiastically, expressing love for the photos and stating that making healthier choices had made a significant difference for him as well. Evan reflected on how small changes can have a big impact and asked Sam if the diet was making a difference for him too.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 40823404-2eb2-4e52-a556-066fc3863616, Score: 0.0253)\nAlso at 8:19 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam responded that the Weight Watchers meeting had been insightful and that the smoothie bowl was well received. Sam strongly recommended yoga, sharing that it had greatly improved his flexibility and reduced his stress levels. He encouraged Evan to try it and offered to provide yoga tips or other support if needed. Evan expressed gratitude and confirmed he would try yoga, appreciating Sam’s suggestion.\n\n\n\nQuestion: According to Evan, what is important for Sam to believe in concerning his weight?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
