inting or going for a drive helpful as coping mechanisms.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: ae13ff3d-57d7-4546-a729-b3998a7587e5, Score: 0.0427)\nAt 4:33 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam shared a photo of a woman holding flowers in front of her face, describing it as amazing and praising Evan’s serious talent and creativity. Sam noted that creating such a painting must have been very satisfying. Evan thanked Sam for the compliment and commented that the painting Sam shared had an inspiring vibe. Evan then asked Sam how long he had been painting.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 199f1ed0-b8a8-4cd8-bc6e-345c1dc64984, Score: 0.0423)\nAt 6:54 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Evan shared a photo of a woman standing in front of a painting. He explained that trying something new and succeeding brings a great feeling of accomplishment. Evan encouraged Sam to give it a try, even if it is just a small effort, assuring him that he would be amazed by the results.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: fffbb261-d314-4f84-a148-bbbb038897a7, Score: 0.0423)\nAlso at 4:07 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Sam complimented Evan\'s painting, calling it awesome and inquiring if Evan had painted it himself. Evan responded with sympathy for Sam\'s rough week and reassured him not to worry about the snacks. Evan shared that he was doing okay and had just finished painting a sunset, which helped him relax, indicating that painting was a therapeutic activity for Evan.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 9a95ee80-36aa-4862-9093-bada86c9d53f, Score: 0.0404)\nAt 4:32 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam asked Evan about the emotions that inspired the painting he had shared. Evan explained that he painted it with a sense of joy and freedom. He described the spontaneous brush strokes and bold colors as reflecting a playful and liberated mood, embracing the creative process without restraint.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: d5160beb-19f4-40ee-b11d-28e4992c8a17, Score: 0.0288)\nOn December 26, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:34 PM, Sam shared with Evan that he occasionally sketches but had not yet created anything remarkable. Sam expressed optimism that he would soon have something to show off and found Evan\'s passion for sketching inspiring. Evan appreciated Sam\'s encouragement and offered to help him get started whenever he wanted. During this exchange, Evan also mentioned that he had lost his keys again, noting that it had become a weekly ritual for him to misplace them.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 1331051d-9ff7-4061-a44b-2e1f15b23de2, Score: 0.0276)\nAt 09:01 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam complimented Evan\'s paintings and asked about the sources of inspiration. Evan explained that the sunset painting was inspired by a vacation taken a few years ago, highlighting the stunning colors he experienced. The cactus painting was inspired by a road trip taken the previous month (September 2023). Evan expressed enthusiasm about the interesting places that inspired his artwork.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 890041ae-cd7d-4f16-936b-60fbe7a633f2, Score: 0.0275)\nAt 09:02 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam praised Evan\'s artwork and inquired how Evan decided what to paint. Evan explained that he usually paints whatever is on his mind or reflects his feelings. His subjects often include good memories or places he wishes to visit. Evan described painting as a form of self-expression through art.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 82d2f461-2731-4913-aa4a-58c63107b2af, Score: 0.0274)\nAt 1:55 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam expressed hope that he could find a hobby he was as passionate about as Evan was with watercolor painting, showing inspiration from Evan\'s enthusiasm.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 87e3e4f8-40ac-4095-87d1-f4f9173fbc3d, Score: 0.0269)\nAlso at 1:52 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Evan responded positively to Sam\'s idea of painting, calling it a cool idea and asking if Sam had tried painting before, showing encouragement and curiosity about Sam\'s experience.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 550ea07c-3c8f-46eb-bb42-415cc47c2622, Score: 0.0269)\nAt 4:30 PM on December 26,