emories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: bbc400c1-5c37-4518-93cb-f9df7fa780c3, Score: 0.0464)\nAlso at 7:31 PM on November 21, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan asked Sam if he had tried any new hobbies recently to help distract from his health issues. Sam replied by sharing an image of a book featuring a picture of a man on its cover, explaining that although he had not tried many new activities lately, he had recently acquired this item the day before (November 20, 2023) and considered it his go-to \'feel good\' movie or flick. This exchange highlighted Sam\'s attempt to find comfort and distraction through media.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: fe099c8e-8a71-4b93-a130-bde4a21419a6, Score: 0.0450)\nAlso at 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam mentioned that he had been looking for a hobby to stay motivated and was thinking about trying painting. Sam asked Evan if painting would help him de-stress. Evan affirmed that painting was a great way to relieve stress and be creative, allowing freedom to explore colors, textures, and express feelings. Evan shared that he had been painting for a few years and found it peaceful. However, Evan clarified that painting alone would not address Sam\'s weight concerns and recommended exercise as an additional necessary component.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 67d3fe15-a9ab-4ee4-bb5d-b1d39d1e8b90, Score: 0.0436)\nAt 9:38 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan shifted the conversation by asking Sam if he had found any low-impact exercises that he enjoyed. Sam replied by sharing a photo of a field with a fence and a dirt road, explaining that he had not yet found exercises he liked. Instead, Sam had been taking car rides recently, which helped him relax and enjoy the scenery. Sam mentioned that the photo was taken last week (January 4-10, 2024) in the countryside.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 3dccb320-89ad-498a-9cb0-335408925164, Score: 0.0427)\nAt 4:09 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan empathized with Sam about work stress and asked if Sam had tried anything new to de-stress, suggesting that picking up a hobby might help. Sam responded by expressing interest in trying something different outdoors and asked Evan for suggestions, indicating a willingness to explore new stress-relief activities.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: 70b2af4d-07e6-41f2-be2f-4f1a6a8a164f, Score: 0.0313)\nOn June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:01 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man with a beard holding a dumbbell to Sam, expressing his enthusiasm and support for their workout goals. Evan emphasized that exercise clears the mind and encouraged Sam to join him in reaching their fitness objectives. Sam responded positively, expressing excitement and requesting help to get started with exercising. Evan gladly offered to meet with Sam to demonstrate some basic exercises, reinforcing their shared commitment to achieving their fitness goals together.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: 55667a3b-6b84-4080-bce7-bb77204d1878, Score: 0.0311)\nAt 4:29 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam admitted that he had not experienced love in the same way but had started enjoying running in the mornings as a way to clear his head. Evan responded by sharing a photo of a painting with a white background featuring blue, orange, and black colors. He acknowledged Sam’s approach to life, emphasizing the importance of finding what works for oneself. Evan encouraged Sam to keep trying new things, suggesting that he might find his own version of love in unexpected places and urged him to embrace the journey, which is full of surprises.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 6f66ad4f-6870-4d71-aea5-6c231e5227f2, Score: 0.0297)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:56 PM, Sam told Evan that he had been trying to maintain his new health routine but found it tough due to pressure from his family. Evan acknowledged the importance of encouragement but cautioned against stress from others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: 5c081850-4570-445d-83a6-8c7383c0d4b5, Score: 0.0289)\nAt 09:32 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan responded to Sam\'s interest by describing painting as a very relaxing activity. Evan offered to assist Sam in getting started with painting, including recommending supplies, and invited Sam to let him know if he wanted to proceed.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: fb55dac6-4f62-4037-b70f-ac4a8828c27d, Score: 0.0282)\nOn September 11, 2023 (Monday) at 09:31 AM, Sam complimented Evan on an impressive painting Evan had created. Sam acknowledged Evan\'s success in finding painting as a way to de-stress and expressed interest in exploring a calming hobby himself, considering painting as a potential option to help manage stress.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 4b175d81-75c5-420a-ac22-6d1e9308774c, Score: 0.0281)\nOn November 21, 2023 (Tuesday) at 7:30 PM, Evan asked Sam how he had been doing. Sam responded with concern about Evan\'s recent health scare, expressing relief that it was just a misunderstanding. Sam reflected on how such a health scare can be frightening and can prompt a person to re-evaluate what is important in life. This conversation marked the beginning of a deeper exchange about health and life priorities between Evan and Sam.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: e7bf3bf4-7e97-4075-a048-bbfc1e48bfaa, Score: 0.0274)\nAt 1:52 PM on May 18, 2023 (Thursday), Sam shared a photo of a person holding a paint set in a store and mentioned that he had not yet found a hobby but was thinking about trying painting. Sam asked Evan if he had any hobbies he loved, indicating openness to exploring creative activities.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 427f14d6-3c3c-4419-bad3-af210fd5b1d8, Score: 0.0255)\nAt 7:12 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam acknowledged Evan\'s description of the peaceful trip and reflected on the importance of taking time for oneself, especially after a hard week. Sam revealed that his own week had been tough. Evan expressed sympathy and offered help. Sam appreciated the offer but explained that he had recently had a doctor\'s check-up a few days prior (around May 21, 2023), which revealed concerning weight results, describing the experience as eye-opening.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What did Sam recently start enjoying to clear his head?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
