2025-12-18 02:02:45,685 - [answer-locomo_8_qa139] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-2651156a-79d5-4d7d-9940-5f1cca238001', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 556c1043-b67c-43dd-b478-d3258e2f7346, Score: 0.0492)\nAt 4:35 PM on December 26, 2023 (Tuesday), immediately following their previous conversation, Sam suggested to Evan that he should put a GPS sensor on his keys to prevent losing them. Evan agreed that it was a great idea and planned to do so as soon as he found his keys.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: bc5d733b-128a-4c09-bac8-79033da247ac, Score: 0.0484)\nAlso at 4:16 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Sam thanked Evan for the suggestion to look into dream interpretation. Sam reflected that the journey toward better health felt endless at times but was convinced it would be rewarding in the end. Sam wished Evan good luck with finding his keys.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: d5160beb-19f4-40ee-b11d-28e4992c8a17, Score: 0.0471)\nOn December 26, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:34 PM, Sam shared with Evan that he occasionally sketches but had not yet created anything remarkable. Sam expressed optimism that he would soon have something to show off and found Evan\'s passion for sketching inspiring. Evan appreciated Sam\'s encouragement and offered to help him get started whenever he wanted. During this exchange, Evan also mentioned that he had lost his keys again, noting that it had become a weekly ritual for him to misplace them.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: e6d879da-9c1c-410c-89a3-a53b6a31cb8d, Score: 0.0466)\nAt 4:15 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Evan encouraged Sam to keep up the good work, cheering for him. Evan then humorously shared that he had been searching for his keys for the last half hour with no luck and joked about losing it every week.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: f786d673-2bb8-4dcc-9e73-cddb2a905c1c, Score: 0.0462)\nAt 4:17 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Evan said he would keep going step by step and was confident he would find the keys. Sam agreed. Evan then urged Sam to go to bed and take care, ending the conversation.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: bb56d93e-569c-4f98-81f9-d2da6752eab9, Score: 0.0455)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:20 AM, Sam reflected on life\'s unpredictability and emphasized the importance of adaptability and finding alternative ways to stay active when facing obstacles. Sam suggested Evan consider low-impact exercises or physical therapy for his knee. Sam also expressed interest in the book Evan mentioned. Evan confirmed that physical therapy was planned and hoped to get an appointment soon. Meanwhile, Evan was keeping activity low-key by swimming, which he found suitable for his condition. Sam agreed that swimming was a good choice because it is low-impact, easy on the joints, and refreshing, encouraging Evan to maintain his active lifestyle.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 7fa56183-9d04-4838-b1cb-65d243a22aea, Score: 0.0410)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 03:02 PM, Evan advised Sam to take his health journey one day at a time and celebrate small victories. Sam agreed that focusing on small wins was a good plan and committed to taking it one day at a time. Evan congratulated Sam on every little victory and reaffirmed his support. Sam expressed that Evan\'s support meant everything to him and toasted to moving forward. Evan encouraged Sam to keep pushing ahead and offered ongoing help, wishing Sam to take care.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: f22378ac-7282-4a23-9588-f17019418527, Score: 0.0401)\nAt 7:58 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Sam admired the amazing view in Evan\'s photo and remarked that the key was to find something that keeps one motivated. Evan then shared a photo of a bonsai tree in a black vase on a wooden table and agreed, stating that finding something that motivates and makes one happy, whether large or tiny, helps conquer struggles encountered.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 6d9f8dc4-a216-410c-8035-a4831c81491d, Score: 0.0397)\nAt 7:16 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Sam thanked Evan for the encouragement and committed to trying painting, promising to update Evan on how it went. Evan responded enthusiastically, advising Sam to have fun and not put too much pressure on himself. Sam agreed to enjoy the process without stress. Evan encouraged Sam to keep him updated, and Sam promised to do so before they exchanged goodbyes.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 44e0766f-5809-4cb3-8704-e1d90069fcea, Score: 0.0390)\nAt 09:33 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan enthusiastically confirmed that painting is an excellent hobby. He advised Sam to acquire acrylic paints, brushes, a canvas or paper, and a palette for mixing colors. Evan also offered to provide specific product recommendations and suggested planning a painting session once Sam was ready.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 4f448d89-7a27-42ef-a41d-452f25c6b206, Score: 0.0292)\nAt 4:11 PM on October 14, 2023 (Saturday), Evan reassured Sam that kayaking was a fun way to exercise and enjoy nature. Evan offered to help Sam by recommending a good kayaking spot when Sam was ready to try it. Sam responded by thanking Evan for the idea and shared that he and his mate were just around the corner from a lake where they planned to try kayaking immediately, demonstrating prompt action on Evan\'s suggestion.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 47b65c3f-d784-4a2e-9f54-6194e65bde99, Score: 0.0288)\nAlso at 09:04 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Evan recommended that Sam try updating his phone software, as this usually resolved such issues for him. Sam thanked Evan for the tip and explained that he enjoyed writing in his journal and doing creative writing, which helped him express his innermost thoughts and feelings.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: 2829f750-a1f2-40f0-8dba-d6fe6ae5a2d7, Score: 0.0288)\nAt 6:53 PM on December 17, 2023 (Sunday), Evan acknowledged that stepping out of one’s comfort zone can be intimidating but reassured Sam that it is worthwhile. Evan advised Sam to challenge himself to try something new, even if it is a small step. Sam thanked Evan and agreed to take his advice, though he noted that trying new things can be difficult.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: ccb7e5d6-f827-4387-b9e3-df419ead514d, Score: 0.0276)\nAt 3:13 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan shared an image with Sam: a photo of a notepad containing a note alongside a pair of scissors. Along with the image, Evan expressed gladness at being there for Sam and emphasized that progress is key. He encouraged Sam to keep pushing forward and stay positive, reinforcing his earlier motivational messages with the phrase, \'You got this!\'\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: 5c081850-4570-445d-83a6-8c7383c0d4b5, Score: 0.0273)\nAt 09:32 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Evan responded to Sam\'s interest by describing painting as a very relaxing activity. Evan offered to assist Sam in getting started with painting, including recommending supplies, and invited Sam to let him know if he wanted to proceed.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 8467c014-d097-4afd-af90-aec4379f7e70, Score: 0.0265)\nAt 3:57 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam agreed that Evan\'s ideas were good and said he would give them a try. Evan encouraged Sam to keep him informed about how it went, emphasizing that small changes could significantly improve health and that every step mattered. Sam thanked Evan and promised to keep him posted. Evan expressed his commitment to supporting Sam on their respective health journeys, reminding Sam that progress takes time. Sam acknowledged this and expressed readiness to keep trying and making small changes. Evan motivated Sam to keep up the effort, assuring him that every bit counted and that he would reach his goals. Sam appreciated Evan\'s support, stating it meant a lot to have Evan in his corner.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 7705d6bd-b7e2-43f3-a5e0-9e00fcc859f8, Score: 0.0260)\nAlso at 09:32 AM on September 11, 2023 (Monday), Sam expressed enthusiasm about trying painting to see if it would help him relax. Sam asked Evan to suggest some basic painting supplies to get started.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What did Sam suggest Evan should do with his keys?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
