emories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: bb56d93e-569c-4f98-81f9-d2da6752eab9, Score: 0.0487)\nOn August 27, 2023 (Sunday) at 10:20 AM, Sam reflected on life\'s unpredictability and emphasized the importance of adaptability and finding alternative ways to stay active when facing obstacles. Sam suggested Evan consider low-impact exercises or physical therapy for his knee. Sam also expressed interest in the book Evan mentioned. Evan confirmed that physical therapy was planned and hoped to get an appointment soon. Meanwhile, Evan was keeping activity low-key by swimming, which he found suitable for his condition. Sam agreed that swimming was a good choice because it is low-impact, easy on the joints, and refreshing, encouraging Evan to maintain his active lifestyle.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: 49ff8723-3693-4005-9dcd-394a90af54f4, Score: 0.0481)\nAt 12:25 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan explained to Sam that the salad idea came from a nearby restaurant. He recommended swimming, yoga, and walking as effective low-impact exercises. Sam appreciated the restaurant inspiration and exercise tips. Sam also shared that he had watched the movie The Godfather the previous night (January 9, 2024), which motivated him to maintain his routine. Sam quoted the famous line, "I\'m gonna make him an offer he can\'t refuse," highlighting how the movie inspired his motivation.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: 391dbe07-59a6-4c84-b59a-8faf2ca192b9, Score: 0.0479)\nAt 12:27 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan shared a photo of a woman standing on a beach at sunset, suggesting that there are many enjoyable low-impact exercises beyond yoga, including beach walks. Evan described beach sunsets as both good exercise and calming experiences. Sam responded that the image looked zen and said he planned to try beach walks based on Evan\'s recommendation. Sam also shared that he had a recurring dream of flying over skyscrapers, which he wanted to brag about.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 8baebd81-4ccb-4ae9-98b0-f68970b857e8, Score: 0.0469)\nAt 12:23 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan asked Sam what advice he planned to seek from the doctor. Sam replied that he intended to ask about a balanced diet plan and to get recommendations for low-impact exercises suitable for his current situation.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: e7cc6553-06e8-448f-aa4e-69efd72bd263, Score: 0.0459)\nOn January 10, 2024 (Wednesday) at 12:24 AM, Evan shared a photo of a salad containing chicken, avocado, tomatoes, corn, and cheese with Sam. Evan encouraged Sam by saying the salad was a step in the right direction and reminded Sam to focus on maintaining a balanced diet alongside low-impact exercises. Evan asked Sam to keep him updated on the progress. Sam responded positively, complimenting the salad and inquiring about the inspiration behind it. Additionally, Sam requested suggestions for low-impact exercises to complement the diet.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: b2c7ffb8-3e6d-48a9-ade3-bf4747fd3bd2, Score: 0.0455)\nAlso at 03:10 PM on October 8, 2023 (Sunday), Evan encouraged Sam by emphasizing the importance of starting with proper form and technique. He recommended finding a trainer to help avoid injuries while building strength. Evan advised starting with light weights and gradually increasing intensity as strength improved. He stressed the importance of consistency in the workout routine and invited Sam to keep him updated on his progress, wishing him good luck.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 67d3fe15-a9ab-4ee4-bb5d-b1d39d1e8b90, Score: 0.0448)\nAt 9:38 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan shifted the conversation by asking Sam if he had found any low-impact exercises that he enjoyed. Sam replied by sharing a photo of a field with a fence and a dirt road, explaining that he had not yet found exercises he liked. Instead, Sam had been taking car rides recently, which helped him relax and enjoy the scenery. Sam mentioned that the photo was taken last week (January 4-10, 2024) in the countryside.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: c0ea7989-c999-4b25-a06b-4a6dc0de02cd, Score: 0.0444)\nAt 08:58 PM on October 6, 2023 (Friday), Sam sympathized with Evan\'s knee injury, acknowledging the difficulty of the situation. Sam asked if there were ways for Evan to remain active while healing. Evan responded that physical therapy had helped somewhat. Although he could not perform intense workouts, Evan was doing gentle exercises to maintain strength, noting that it was not as fulfilling as outdoor activities but still beneficial.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 40823404-2eb2-4e52-a556-066fc3863616, Score: 0.0429)\nAlso at 8:19 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Sam responded that the Weight Watchers meeting had been insightful and that the smoothie bowl was well received. Sam strongly recommended yoga, sharing that it had greatly improved his flexibility and reduced his stress levels. He encouraged Evan to try it and offered to provide yoga tips or other support if needed. Evan expressed gratitude and confirmed he would try yoga, appreciating Sam’s suggestion.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 0eea3c65-614c-4365-b6bd-5fa195db5787, Score: 0.0427)\nAt 8:19 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan complimented the smoothie bowl Sam had shared and asked how the Weight Watchers meeting had gone. Evan also mentioned that he had been considering trying yoga as a gentle yet effective way to relieve stress and improve flexibility. He asked Sam for his opinion on yoga, seeking advice based on Sam’s experience.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: d90202cd-0443-4f96-bd47-f0d12a002f27, Score: 0.0419)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:51 PM, Evan encouraged Sam to set specific fitness goals such as running a certain distance or completing a number of push-ups. Evan explained that having clear goals would provide motivation and something to strive for. He also suggested that Sam find an exercise activity that he enjoys and consider exercising with a buddy to add fun and accountability. Evan asked Sam if this plan sounded good to him.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: 94db81d9-3819-4236-9665-bb021a583c78, Score: 0.0417)\nAt 7:15 PM on May 24, 2023 (Wednesday), Evan shared that what worked for him was finding a fitness routine he genuinely enjoyed, which became his go-to activity. He loved the feeling of being healthy and strong. Evan emphasized making exercise fun and incorporating small smarter dietary choices that added up over time. He encouraged Sam by affirming that Sam had the capability to succeed.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: ba411852-7a5d-4e69-9705-562e411d823d, Score: 0.0410)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Sam responded positively to Evan\'s advice, agreeing that setting goals and having someone to exercise with might be helpful. Sam expressed willingness to give this approach a try.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: 70b2af4d-07e6-41f2-be2f-4f1a6a8a164f, Score: 0.0406)\nOn June 6, 2023 (Tuesday) at 4:01 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a man with a beard holding a dumbbell to Sam, expressing his enthusiasm and support for their workout goals. Evan emphasized that exercise clears the mind and encouraged Sam to join him in reaching their fitness objectives. Sam responded positively, expressing excitement and requesting help to get started with exercising. Evan gladly offered to meet with Sam to demonstrate some basic exercises, reinforcing their shared commitment to achieving their fitness goals together.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: e4345cdb-f400-4807-88d8-778b2e81e466, Score: 0.0405)\nAt 10:53 AM on July 27, 2023 (Thursday), Evan shared an image of a set of five cards with the words "let it shine," including a photo of his gym membership card, symbolizing his commitment to health. He revealed that he had struggled with his health a few years ago but persevered. Evan emphasized that exercise alone is not enough; diet and lifestyle changes are also crucial. Sam responded enthusiastically, asking Evan what had the biggest impact on his health journey.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: d0b268a6-9def-4568-ab22-727528a3db77, Score: 0.0390)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:52 PM, Evan expressed enthusiasm about Sam\'s decision to start exercising, reassuring him that getting started would become easier over time. Evan reminded Sam that exercise is about feeling good and achieving goals. He proposed planning a hike together soon as a motivating activity.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 6f66ad4f-6870-4d71-aea5-6c231e5227f2, Score: 0.0262)\nOn October 25, 2023 (Wednesday) at 02:56 PM, Sam told Evan that he had been trying to maintain his new health routine but found it tough due to pressure from his family. Evan acknowledged the importance of encouragement but cautioned against stress from others. Evan also shared that he had just returned from his morning walk, which helped him start the day actively. Sam agreed that having a great support system made things easier and thanked Evan for his support. Evan encouraged Sam to take it slow and treat himself kindly. Sam admitted sometimes being impatient for quick results but recognized the need for patience. Evan emphasized that progress takes time and advised taking it one step at a time. Sam agreed, appreciating the advice to take it slow rather than overdoing it, and expressed gratitude for Evan\'s support.\n\n\n\nQuestion: What suggestions did Evan give for low-impact exercises?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
