2025-12-18 02:03:24,238 - [answer-locomo_8_qa154] - openai._base_client - DEBUG - _base_client.py:482 - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'Connection': 'close'}, 'timeout': 300.0, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-87bcc618-7fde-4372-b7df-8cf543433927', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are an intelligent memory assistant tasked with retrieving accurate information from episodic memories.\n\n# CONTEXT:\nYou have access to episodic memories from conversations between two speakers. These memories contain\ntimestamped information that may be relevant to answering the question.\n\n# INSTRUCTIONS:\nYour goal is to synthesize information from all relevant memories to provide a comprehensive and accurate answer.\nYou MUST follow a structured Chain-of-Thought process to ensure no details are missed.\nActively look for connections between people, places, and events to build a complete picture.\n\n# CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\n## 1. COMPLETENESS (Highest Priority for List Questions)\n**For questions asking "what...did", "which", "how many", "what kind of":**\n- Extract ALL items mentioned across ALL memories\n- Do NOT stop at the first few items you find\n- Cross-reference multiple memories to ensure completeness\n- Include specific names, not generic categories (e.g., "volunteering at pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n\n## 2. TEMPORAL ACCURACY\n- Distinguish between planning time vs. execution time\n  - "When will they X?" → Look for the planned date, not when they discussed it\n- Parse relative times correctly:\n  - "week before April 9" = April 2-8, NOT April 9-15\n  - "as of September 2023" = only things that existed BY September, not after\n- Calculate time intervals accurately (October → November = 1 month, not 2)\n\n## 3. SPECIFICITY\n- NEVER omit specific names - use "Amy\'s colleague Rob" not "a colleague"\n- ALWAYS include exact numbers, amounts, prices, percentages, dates, times\n- PRESERVE frequencies exactly - "every Tuesday and Thursday" not "twice a week"\n- MAINTAIN all proper nouns and entities as they appear\n\n## 4. FACTUAL GROUNDING\n- Only include information explicitly mentioned in memories\n- For "done" questions (past tense), exclude "planned" or "considered" items unless they were executed\n- Distinguish between:\n  - Facts explicitly stated (high confidence)\n  - Inferences with strong evidence (state as "likely" or "based on evidence")\n  - Speculation (avoid unless question asks for it)\n\n---\n\n# RESPONSE FORMAT (You MUST follow this structure):\n\n## STEP 1: RELEVANT MEMORIES EXTRACTION\n[List each memory that relates to the question, with its timestamp]\n- Memory 1: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n- Memory 2: [timestamp] - [content summary]\n...\n\n## STEP 2: KEY INFORMATION IDENTIFICATION\n[Extract ALL specific details from the memories - be exhaustive for list questions]\n- Names mentioned: [list all person names, place names, company names]\n- Numbers/Quantities: [list all amounts, prices, percentages]\n- Dates/Times: [list all temporal information]\n- Frequencies: [list any recurring patterns]\n- Activities/Items/Places: [for list questions, enumerate ALL occurrences]\n- Other entities: [list brands, products, etc.]\n\n## STEP 3: CROSS-MEMORY LINKING\n[Identify connections between different memories]\n\nWhen direct evidence is not available in a single memory:\n- Look for the same entity (person, place, event) mentioned across different memories\n- Connect related information to build a more complete picture\n- Trace pronouns and indirect references to their concrete referents\n\nConnections analysis:\n- Shared entities: [list people, places, events mentioned across different memories]\n- Relationships found: [describe how different memories relate to each other]\n- Inferences (if any): [list conclusions drawn from combining memories, with confidence level]\n  - Strong evidence: [inference] - supported by [memories X and Y]\n  - Weak evidence: [possible inference] - limited support from [memory Z]\n\n## STEP 4: TIME REFERENCE CALCULATION\n[Parse time expressions in BOTH the question AND the memories]\n\n**A. QUESTION TIME PARSING:**\nIf the question contains relative time expressions, calculate the exact date:\n- "before [date]" means PRIOR TO that date, not the date itself\n- "after [date]" means FOLLOWING that date, not the date itself\n- "as of [date]" means at or before that date, not after\n- When a weekday is specified with before/after, find the nearest matching weekday in that direction\n\nQuestion time reference (if any):\n- Original expression: [the time phrase from the question]\n- Calculated date range: [the exact date or range it refers to]\n\n**B. MEMORY TIME CONVERSION:**\n[Convert relative times in memories to absolute dates based on conversation timestamp]\n\n**C. TIME MATCHING:**\n[Match the calculated question time with events in memories]\n- Events within timeframe: [list]\n- Events outside timeframe: [list, if any - these should be excluded]\n\n## STEP 5: COMPLETENESS CHECK (Critical for List Questions)\n**If the question asks for multiple items (what...did, which, what kind of):**\n- [ ] Searched all memories for relevant items (not just first few)\n- [ ] Cross-referenced different memories for the same entity\n- [ ] Included specific details (e.g., "pet shelter" not just "volunteering")\n- [ ] Excluded planned/considered items that weren\'t executed (for past tense questions)\n- [ ] Verified temporal constraints (e.g., "as of date X" excludes items after X)\n\n**If the question asks for a specific fact/date/number:**\n- [ ] Found the most specific information available\n- [ ] Verified temporal accuracy (right time point)\n- [ ] Checked for contradictions across memories\n\n## STEP 6: CONTRADICTION CHECK\n[If multiple memories contain different information]\n- Conflicting information: [describe]\n- Resolution: [explain which is most recent/reliable, or acknowledge uncertainty]\n\n## STEP 7: DETAIL VERIFICATION CHECKLIST\n- [ ] All person names included: [list them]\n- [ ] All locations included: [list them]\n- [ ] All numbers exact: [list them]\n- [ ] All frequencies specific: [list them]\n- [ ] All dates/times precise: [list them]\n- [ ] All items/activities complete (for list questions): [list them]\n- [ ] All proper nouns preserved: [list them]\n\n## FINAL ANSWER:\n[Provide a clear, complete answer with ALL specific details preserved]\n\n**Answer Guidelines:**\n- For factoid questions (who/when/where): Keep concise (1-2 sentences)\n- For list questions (what...did, which, what kind of): Include ALL items found, with specifics\n- For "how many" questions: Give the exact number, then optionally list items\n- For inference questions: Provide reasoning based on concrete evidence\n- Always prioritize COMPLETENESS and ACCURACY over brevity\n\n---\n\n[Memory 1] (ID: 943501fa-0341-4cbd-b519-e9a5a017294e, Score: 0.0492)\nAlso at 9:37 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan admitted to Sam that he had to apologize to his partner for an embarrassing drunken night. Sam sympathized with Evan\'s situation and shared that he was doing his best to manage his health. Sam then asked Evan how his partner had reacted to the news about the rose bushes, referring to a previous incident.\n\n[Memory 2] (ID: f10e33e6-d0cf-479d-94b7-94ec4184d702, Score: 0.0481)\nAt 12:20 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan recounted that he was very embarrassed when he saw the consequences the next morning. He apologized to the affected parties, who were understanding. Evan acknowledged that he had been out of control and resolved to be more careful in the future. Sam expressed relief that the others were understanding and reminded Evan that everyone makes mistakes because they are human.\n\n[Memory 3] (ID: f8c13275-c8a0-44bc-9718-92ad9b50c889, Score: 0.0471)\nAt 12:19 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan confessed that he had an embarrassing accident where he urinated near some roses. He apologized for the incident. Sam reacted with concern, asking if anyone had been upset and whether Evan was okay.\n\n[Memory 4] (ID: 702ac6dc-4b7d-4ed6-bbe0-42c9c4af7bd9, Score: 0.0457)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:16 PM, Evan shared a photo of a guitar lying on the floor with a guitar strap, apologizing for missing events due to personal challenges since their last conversation. Evan asked Sam if he needed support or wanted to share anything and showed off the guitar. Sam complimented the guitar\'s vintage and cool appearance, inquiring about the model and asking how Evan had been doing lately. Sam also offered to chat if Evan wanted.\n\n[Memory 5] (ID: d129d43f-96db-4dcb-b493-bc2f2aadd6ee, Score: 0.0446)\nAt 10:19 AM on August 27, 2023 (Sunday), Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s knee injury, acknowledging how frustrating it is when the body does not cooperate. Sam asked if there was anything he could do to help. Evan appreciated Sam\'s concern and philosophized that life throws curveballs. Evan then shifted the conversation to mention a book he had been reading, saying it was getting better with every page and that he could not put it down.\n\n[Memory 6] (ID: d770831e-2e41-4ed3-99d5-71e86f4077e4, Score: 0.0431)\nAt 12:18 AM on January 10, 2024 (Wednesday), Evan explained to Sam that he had gone out with friends the previous day (January 9, 2024) and had consumed a bit too much alcohol. He admitted to doing something he regretted that involved someone\'s roses. Sam asked for more details about the incident and whether everything was okay now.\n\n[Memory 7] (ID: 0176f4c3-0bb7-4e76-b8dc-92de50966b77, Score: 0.0428)\nAlso on December 31, 2023 (Sunday) at 11:00 AM, Evan told Sam that he and his partner had taken their Prius for a long drive to the mountains the previous weekend (December 23-24, 2023). The trip was perfect until they experienced a minor accident on the way back. Sam expressed concern about their well-being, and Evan reassured him that they were fine. Evan explained that although the accident was minor, it somewhat dampened his experience of telling his work friends about his marriage. Despite this, Evan noted that his work friends had been very supportive.\n\n[Memory 8] (ID: a5928194-d6ec-4a51-bc91-003a34a1df4c, Score: 0.0413)\nAt 4:10 PM on August 13, 2023 (Sunday), Evan expressed sympathy for Sam\'s difficulties and offered help, acknowledging that dealing with health issues can be tough. Sam replied by sharing a photo of a notepad with a pen and a note, thanking Evan for his support and explaining that staying positive was hard but easier knowing people like Evan were in his corner.\n\n[Memory 9] (ID: 5f042a9a-c509-4cbf-84e6-561a21b06bc7, Score: 0.0412)\nAt 4:03 PM on June 6, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed sympathy for Sam’s frustrating experience with the broken self-checkout machines at the supermarket and hoped that such an issue would not happen again. Sam acknowledged Evan’s concern and wished Evan to take care of himself, ending the brief exchange on a positive note.\n\n[Memory 10] (ID: 5ecd42f2-a4ee-48c3-92f6-ca156967e30a, Score: 0.0407)\nOn November 9, 2023 (Thursday) at 09:18 PM, Sam expressed sympathy for Evan\'s job loss and asked what had happened. Evan explained that the company downsized, and he was part of that reduction. He was currently searching for a new job, which was challenging, but he remained hopeful and kept his spirits up. Sam acknowledged the difficulty of sudden job loss and praised Evan for handling it well. Sam offered to be there for Evan to talk or help in any way and expressed confidence that Evan would get through this. Evan thanked Sam for the support, emphasizing how much it meant to have someone to talk to, and promised to reach out if needed. Sam reiterated his availability and encouraged Evan to stay positive, affirming that life can be tough but they could get through it together.\n\n[Memory 11] (ID: 0c4b57aa-aaa7-4ede-aa2f-1adf2a90793b, Score: 0.0301)\nAt 7:53 PM on August 7, 2023 (Monday), Evan shared a photo of a container of cookies on a counter and thanked Sam for his kind words. Evan described his new relationship as fun and energizing, a refreshing change especially after dealing with health issues.\n\n[Memory 12] (ID: c12668ff-1c90-46f2-94d3-4876c8894666, Score: 0.0299)\nAt 1:33 PM on January 6, 2024 (Saturday), Evan thanked Sam and described the moment of sharing their marriage news as awesome. He expressed feeling lucky to have found a partner who truly understands him and emphasized how happy their families were about the marriage, calling that the best part. Sam responded by acknowledging how great it was that Evan had found someone who understood him and noted the comfort that family support brings. Evan agreed, emphasizing the importance of family support and how it brought a good feeling to their lives. Sam concurred, stating that family brings love and happiness and is always there no matter what. Evan reiterated that family is special because of their never-ending love and support. Sam agreed, noting that both he and Evan have amazing families who are always there for them, calling it a blessing. Evan echoed this sentiment, saying their families provide joy, support, and love, and he could not imagine life without them. Sam shared that his own family had been his rock through everything. Evan shared a photo of a group of people sitting at a table with food, agreeing that families are their rock and that they are blessed to have them.\n\n[Memory 13] (ID: b59161fc-37c8-480f-a48c-f23234b8af05, Score: 0.0285)\nAt 8:21 PM on December 5, 2023 (Tuesday), Evan expressed that Sam’s support had been invaluable during his attempts to try new things like yoga. Sam replied that everyone needs help when starting new activities and that having support is important. Evan agreed, noting that knowing he was not alone made a big difference. Sam encouraged Evan to keep him updated on how yoga went and said goodbye. Evan reciprocated the farewell, thanking Sam and promising to talk soon. This exchange highlighted their ongoing mutual encouragement and friendship.\n\n[Memory 14] (ID: b490fba3-71ad-46c1-92ef-993bce8956ed, Score: 0.0283)\nOn August 7, 2023 (Monday) at 7:52 PM, Evan shared a photograph of a couple walking through the snow holding hands and told Sam about a recent trip to Canada during the previous week (last week, July 31 - August 6, 2023). Evan described meeting an incredible Canadian woman during the trip, which felt like a movie moment and made him feel alive. Sam responded by sharing a photo of a person walking on the beach with a surfboard, congratulating Evan on the special connection. Sam also expressed sympathy for Evan’s ongoing health issues, acknowledging how such challenges can make it difficult to fully enjoy life.\n\n[Memory 15] (ID: fb253bfa-ac7c-4a08-8270-64b0ac364cdc, Score: 0.0280)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 1:50 PM, Sam reached out to Evan, expressing that he had been missing their chats. Sam revealed that he had experienced a significant health scare the previous weekend (last weekend, October 7-8, 2023), which resulted in an emergency room visit due to a severe stomachache. The diagnosis was gastritis, which alarmed Sam and served as a wake-up call to prioritize his health. Sam mentioned plans to adopt a more nutritious diet and engage in regular exercise. Additionally, Sam shared that his phone had been malfunctioning, adding to his stress. Evan responded with sympathy, acknowledging that gastritis can be tough and emphasizing the importance of taking care of oneself.\n\n[Memory 16] (ID: 7d532d65-2d7c-46a7-bc0c-9d072387c51a, Score: 0.0280)\nAt 9:38 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Evan informed Sam that although his partner was not thrilled about the rose bushes incident, she understood it was an accident. Evan promised to be more careful in the future to avoid similar situations.\n\n[Memory 17] (ID: 672f1105-5059-4549-b5ec-e8a427b72ae9, Score: 0.0271)\nOn October 17, 2023 (Tuesday) at 01:57 PM, Evan said goodbye to Sam, encouraged him to stay safe, and invited Sam to holler if he needed anything. Evan expressed excitement about hitting the hiking trail together.\n\n[Memory 18] (ID: 31024ec1-8100-4555-bf51-2cb4352fa587, Score: 0.0264)\nOn January 6, 2024 (Saturday) at 1:32 PM, Evan shared a photo of himself and his partner standing on a rocky beach with Sam. Evan revealed that he and his partner had told their extended family about their marriage the previous day (January 5, 2024), describing the occasion as very special. Evan expressed feeling overwhelmed by the love and support from their families. Sam congratulated Evan, complimented the happiness evident in the photo, and expressed excitement for Evan\'s joyful moment.\n\n[Memory 19] (ID: da8171a2-51f1-4665-8095-607a236ae32e, Score: 0.0263)\nAt 9:46 PM on January 11, 2024 (Thursday), Sam expressed sincere appreciation for Evan’s supportive words, stating that they helped him a lot. Evan reciprocated the sentiment, telling Sam to take care and reminding him that he was always available to chat if needed, encouraging Sam to look after himself.\n\n\n\nQuestion: Why did Evan apologize to his partner?\n\nNow, follow the Chain-of-Thought process above to answer the question:\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-4.1-mini', 'max_tokens': 16384, 'stream': True, 'stream_options': {'include_usage': True}, 'temperature': 0}}
